(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, inspected the homes of veterans affected by the typhoon on March 27 at the Techo Santepheap Center (two squares).
This was also attended by Brigadier General Chim Bun An, Chief of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Veterans and local authorities on March 30, 2022.
At that time, Senior Minister Kun Kim ordered the construction team to build new houses for the veterans whose houses were severely damaged (completely damaged) and had to be rebuilt within a month of 39 houses.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also urged all veterans to pay close attention to the weather, as this is a rainy season with strong winds and can cause any eventuality to happen to you.
At the same time, Senior Minister Kun Kim also said that he must continue to protect himself as much as possible and must follow the instructions of the medical team, especially following the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
