"Son under the full moon" was filmed by the film production team at Sambor Prei Kuk temple
(Kampong Thom): The film "Son under the full moon" was filmed at the Sambor Prei Kuk temple resort in Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province, 28 km from Kampong Thom provincial town. Supervise the actual location by the film production committee.
The visit to the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site was attended by Mr. Hun Many, accompanied by Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province and colleagues this morning, March 30, 2022.
Taking the opportunity, Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that the story of the son under the full moon is a historical story about the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, with many important events in Seek peace for the people.
He continued that because the story of the film is historical at the national level, the history of the actual life of Samdech Techo, Samdech decided to set up a film production committee.
Although the film is produced by a private company, the commission is responsible for overseeing the content and actual historical sites. All the members of the committee are real experts in film production who have won the trust of Samdech Techo, the original owner of the story.
(Phnom Penh): On March 30, 2022, Ms. Tina Reeds, British Ambassador to Cambodia, and Ms. Davyani Kopragade, Ambassador of India to Cambodia, together with Ms. Hoeung Gek Lim, acted as Tina. The British Red Crescent in Cambodia and the young secretary, acting as the successor to India, Dr. Deviani Cobra Garde of India in Cambodia, paid a joint visit to the Samdech Mey Library.
The Embassy of India also has a young secretary who is the winner of the "Ambassador One Day" competition, although the selection process is different. The two ambassadors who competed in the "Ambassador One Day" competition paid a joint visit to the "Samdech Mey" library on March 30, 2022. It is the first joint event on the subject by the British Embassy and the Indian Embassy in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
On the occasion of this visit, Ms. Sofarina presented an interesting diary of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk entitled "The Royal Journey of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk to the Liberated Areas of Cambodia." Cambodian National Front in 1973 to the delegation.
The British and Indian Ambassadors praised the role of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, as well as the Samdech Mey Library, in preserving documents for the public and contributing to the Khmer Rouge tribunal seeking justice for its victims. Educated the students and the younger generation about the Khmer Rouge regime.
Finally, the delegation made a note on the Golden Book of the "Samdech Mey" library, which has the following content:
Young secretary from Ratanakkiri province: "This is the first time for me to visit the library" Samdech Mey ". I was very happy to hear the brave heroism of the Princess. But I seem sad when I hear about the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime. I will remember this day and share it with my community. ”
Hoeung Gek Lim from Phnom Penh: “I really saw it with my own eyes. It should be a place you must visit once in your life. I have listened to the history of my nation. ”
