The following is the announcement of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration: General Knowledge: Which countries have the worst floods in human history?
(Foreign): Floods are a catastrophic disaster that kills people every year and wreaks havoc on nations around the world. Do you know which countries suffered the most floods in our world history?
In China, floods have wreaked havoc for thousands of years, but people are still living with the floods from ancient times to the present, and there are still deaths every year. The catastrophic disaster was caused by two major rivers, the Changjiang (Yangtze) and the Yellow River, with an estimated 350 million people living along the Changjiang River and another 100 million living along the Yellow River.
According to records, in 1887 the Yellow River flooded an area of 30,000 square kilometers, inundating about 1,500 Chinese villages. The Changjiang River in the south is also prone to catastrophic floods, with the largest flood occurring in 1887, affecting about 900,000 people. Until 1938, the floods also caused casualties similar to those of 1887.
From the late 1990s until now, China has been hit hard by a series of floods. In response to the disaster, Beijing has built three mountain dams since 2003 to mitigate the effects of the Changjiang or Yangtze River floods.
Apart from China, a number of other countries were affected by the floods, including India, Bangladesh, Vietnam, Pakistan, Indonesia, Egypt, Myanmar, Afghanistan, Nigeria, Brazil, Thailand, Congo, Iraq and Cambodia.
In fact, scientists have divided the flood into three major categories:
