Cambodia, South Korea expect the entry into force of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement to boost trade and investment in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, said that the free trade agreement between Cambodia and Korea will help pave the way for increased trade and investment between the two countries. Up more.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea said this during a meeting with Dr. Koo Yun-cheol, Minister of Government Policy Coordination of the Republic of Korea on the afternoon of March 29, 2022 at the Council for the Development of Cambodia. On the occasion of his visit to Cambodia for 3 days from March 28 to 30, 2022.
A free trade agreement between Cambodia and Korea was signed in late October 2021, which will enter into force soon.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea praised the direct investment from Korea, which not only brings capital and technology, but also brings a spirit of unyielding struggle.
Mr. Khu Yun-chul, Minister of Government Policy Coordination of the Republic of Korea, thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Council for the Development of Cambodia, for its continued support to Korean investors in Cambodia.
He believes that this support, combined with Cambodia's new investment law and the entry into force of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement, will encourage more Korean investment in Cambodia.
Meanwhile, the Minister for Government Policy Coordination of the Republic of Korea invited Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea and his colleagues to visit the Republic of Korea at an appropriate time to strengthen bilateral cooperation in the field of investment and development cooperation.
Mr. Sok Chendasophea thanked the Korean government for continuing to maintain uninterrupted direct flights between Seoul and Phnom Penh from the early stages of the Kovid-19 epidemic to the present. This has enabled Cambodia to connect with the world.
It should be noted that as of February 2022, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has registered 219 qualified Korean investment projects with a total investment capital of about 5 billion US dollars.
