Duke Kith Meng Attracts Mekong Business Group from Lang Chang to Study Investment Possibilities in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, on the morning of March 30, 2022, addressed the opening ceremony of the 3rd Lang Chang Mekong Business Forum, co-organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Mekong Institute. Promoting agribusiness and investment in food processing.
The forum was chaired by Mr. Chuon Dara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, represented by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and was attended by more than 150 representatives from the public and private sectors of Lang Chang Mekong in Phnom Penh and more than 200 in Phnom Penh. Online.
On the occasion of the opening ceremony of the business forum, Duke Kith Meng warmly welcomed all the business delegations of Lang Chang Mekong and emphasized that Lang Chang Mekong has a similar culture, long-term friendly relations and goals. Joint development as well as great potential for joint cooperation.
Agriculture plays an important role in the socio-economic development of Mekong, a country of more than 248 million people. Trade and investment among the Mekong countries have continued to grow despite the impact of Kovid-19.
The President stressed the importance of promoting good cooperation between the countries of Langchang and Mekong towards common prosperity.
For example, the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement entered into force in January 2022, which helped boost the Cambodia-China bilateral economic and trade relationship to a high level, as well as help develop Cambodia's agricultural sector, as China is an importer of products. One of the main Cambodian agriculture, which includes products: rice, mango and bananas.
In this regard, the President invited business delegations from Mekong, Lang Chang and all businessmen to visit and study investment opportunities in Cambodia, which has a strong economy, a wide market and rich opportunities.
The 3rd Langchang Mekong Business Forum is part of a long-term project funded by the Special Fund for Langkang Mekong Cooperation of the People's Republic of China.
The two-day business forum focuses on four key events:
Discussion on agro-industry, agribusiness, food processing, policy support, challenges and opportunities and sharing of experiences of Cambodian companies in agro-industry 2: Trade meeting 3: Trade fair 4: Visit to Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone and Cambodian companies in the agro-industry sector.
