(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health and relevant partners this morning, March 30, 2022, organized the opening ceremony of the 25th National TB Review Conference at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Prof. Xia Huang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, with the participation of Ms. Nargiza Khodjeava, Technical Director for Non-Communicable Diseases and Lifelong Health of the World Health Organization in Cambodia, Ms. Hanh Nguyen, Deputy Director of the United Nations Mission United States for Development in Cambodia, including representatives of a number of ministries and institutions.
According to the report of the National Center for Tuberculosis Control and Hansen, in 2021, the TB control work has achieved remarkable new achievements. In Cambodia, TB morbidity and mortality rates have dropped dramatically, from 579 cases per 100,000 population in 2000 to 274 cases per 100,000 population, the report said. In 2020, which is equivalent to a decrease of 53%.
Prof. Xia Huang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, warmly congratulated and appreciated this proud achievement for the Royal Government under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Significantly for the health and well-being of the Cambodian people. Samdech Techo has given high priority to the health sector, especially the fight against infectious diseases, including tuberculosis, AIDS and malaria, including:
* Increase in salaries and other allowances for civil servants and staff. * Support for the expansion of the Equity Fund and the National Social Security Fund, especially for health care and support for the poor, civil servants, workers and pregnant women. Pregnancy and childbirth, etc. * Additional staffing of health workers to the Ministry of Health. * As well as promoting the expansion of physical infrastructure, as well as medical facilities and the provision of medicine.
Professor Xia Huang said that in addition, for the work to eradicate TB during 2022-2023, we will have a lot of work to meet the strategy to end TB and sustainable development goals.
To achieve the goal of the new year 2022 as well as the next year, please take this opportunity to have some interest as follows:
2: Care must be taken to strengthen the implementation of policies to diagnose and treat TB free of charge in order to encourage patients to receive quality TB services as soon as possible.
3: Further efforts should be made to prevent tuberculosis prevention, pediatric tuberculosis work, and in particular TB research among children living close to TB patients and high-risk groups, such as those living with HIV and diabetes. Elderly people and in prisons.
On behalf of the Ministry of Health, he expressed his deepest gratitude and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, for his constant support of the health sector, especially the fight against TB. He thanked the relevant partners who have supported the fight against tuberculosis at all levels, making the work of the National TB Control Program at all levels to achieve good results.
Mr. Xia Huang also sincerely appreciated and thanked for the hard work of relevant institutions, local authorities at all levels, officials and health managers in the capital, provinces, districts, who have supported the work to eradicate TB. This is constantly growing. Prey Veng Provincial Governor Distributes CRC Donations to 60 Families Affected by Typhoon
