Minister of Labor: UN in Cambodia has made a significant contribution to the socio-economic development of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Over the years, the United Nations in Cambodia and its development partners have made a significant and active contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development.
This was stated by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training during the courtesy call of Ms. Pauline Tamesis, United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia, who ended her term in Cambodia. In the morning of March 30, 2022 at the Ministry.
The Minister said that all UN agencies in Cambodia are important partners of the Royal Government of Cambodia. These partnerships provide Cambodia with a comprehensive policy, technical, capacity building and financial framework that benefits the youth and the Cambodian people in general, and Cambodia can address a number of key issues in the context of Kovid. 19 Successful.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng is deeply reminiscent of the fact that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has been working with the UN for the past four years during her tenure. Proudly successful.
On behalf of the Ministry of Labor, the Minister highly appreciated the fruitful progress and progress under her coordination. These are the achievements that she has left in Cambodia, hoping that she will be successful in her new job.
Ms. Pauline Tamesis said that these achievements are also due to the wise leadership of the Minister and the leadership of the Ministry. In the past, the United Nations in Cambodia has been able to achieve success due to the fact that the owners of the country are fully able to cooperate in a good partnership with each other.
At the same time, she praised the Ministry of Labor for always protecting the interests of workers, especially the vaccination campaign for workers who have maintained employment and income sustainability, as well as other social protection systems that the Ministry Zealous in these endeavors.
She claims that although her mission is over, the UN has a lot of work to do in Cambodia, including the UN's five-year strategic plan to work with the Cambodian government. The UN requested the support of Minister Ith Sam Heng and other Cambodian government ministries and institutions.
The Minister was pleased with the launch of the UN's five-year strategic plan to work in partnership with the Cambodian government. In the past, the Cambodian government has adopted a strategic plan after the Kovid-19 crisis, continuing to implement the existing ones in a new context by learning to live with Kovid. Human resource training.
He stressed that despite the progress in the field of employment and training of human resources, there are still challenges that need to be addressed in accordance with national and international standards, laws and the involvement of other stakeholders.
