Cambodia, Pakistan agree to establish memorandum of understanding to strengthen tourism cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Pakistan have reached an agreement to draft a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on tourism cooperation in the near future to enhance cooperation in this important area and promote Mutual tourism movement, as both countries have the same potential for tourism.
On that occasion, Mr. Zahei Ruddin praised the vaccination policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, who implemented the Kovid 19 vaccination campaign to strengthen the community in the socio-economic and open. The country receives international tourists again.
He noted Cambodia's tourism potential, which has a wide range of attractions, such as Siem Reap-Angkor, coastal areas and ecotourism sites.
Mr. Zaheed Ruddin is determined that during his tenure as Ambassador of Pakistan to Cambodia, he will work to strengthen and further develop Cambodia-Pakistan tourism cooperation, as Cambodia and Pakistan have great potential in the field of tourism. Same.
In response to the remarks of the Pakistani Ambassador, Minister Thong Khon informed that in order for the strengthening of cooperation in the field of tourism to be strong, Cambodia intends to prepare a memorandum of understanding with Pakistan as soon as possible. In the future, when the preparation is completed, both parties will sign this memorandum together.
Under the umbrella of the memorandum, the two countries will establish tourism visits between the public and private sectors to boost tourism between the two countries.
The Minister also added that currently Cambodia-Pakistan does not have direct flights together, so the important task is to facilitate the travel of tourists, because if you want to increase tourism, it is necessary to have a travel connection. First.
The two sides also discussed encouraging Pakistani investors to invest in Cambodia, especially in the tourism sector, to attract Islamic tourists from Pakistan and other countries. General Ith Sarath: Peace is invaluable no matter today or the next day, so be protected at all costs
