Readers' views: What are the good legal options that lead to the end of the conflict at NagaWorld? Demonstrators should accept compensation from the company!
Following the ruling of the Arbitration Council, of the 373 former NagaWorld employees, more than 100 agreed to accept compensation from the company, leaving only about 200.
According to the labor law, when there is a decision from the Arbitration Council and in case the company is willing to compensate them, it means that the company will not take them back to work and the employees. There is no right to order or force the company to accept its terms.
From a legal point of view, former NagaWorld employees have no choice but to accept the compensation offered by NagaWorld in accordance with the Labor Law, as such anarchic protests are not a solution and are not effective in putting pressure on them. NagaWorld can not because the company has followed the legal procedures.
At the same time, the refusal to accept the compensation of the remaining former NagaWorld employees deviated from the rule of law and completely departed from the decision of the Arbitration Council and also showed the dishonesty of the unwanted protesters. There is a solution to end labor disputes.
Through this activity, it can be concluded that the demonstration has a clear plan, structure, leadership and training, in addition to the force of the demonstrators and the leaders of the demonstrators who actually practice, there is also a clear command from the outside. Along with the internal protests, there were also demonstrations in support of various countries by the international union network.
In general, if the remaining 200 former NagaWorld employees are genuinely willing to seek a settlement with NagaWorld, they should respond to the call of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training as well as the institution. Involved and as they promised before the court released on bail to end the dispute.
On the other hand, in case the dispute does not end, what needs to be done is to continue the proceedings in court. According to the law, the employer has the right to dismiss the employee only if the company agrees to settle in accordance with the law, but if the employee does not agree with the dismissal or dismissal, they have the right to sue to find a solution.
However, in the event that the employer resigns, there is no permission to return to work, only to accept compensation. This is a legal principle that former employees and staff of NagaWorld should not continue to incite or lead activities that violate any law that may affect security, public order and society.
By: Sok Veasna, Labor Rights Officer at NGO
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Asks All Border Provinces to Increase Control of Imports of Chemicals and Drugs
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, requested all border provinces to increase controls on the import of chemicals and drugs from abroad. Hundreds of kilograms of narcotics trucks continued to arrive in Cambodia, but were stopped by Lao authorities.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan made this request during the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the results of drug control work in 2021 and work direction in 2022 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh on the morning of March 30. This 2022.
The appeal of the President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs made a few days ago in Stung Treng province, there was a case of transporting more than 600 kilograms of drugs in a row, 3 units in a row, but the authorities Laos was able to crack down while the trucks used to transport fertilizer in the border province of Stung Treng.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan calls on all capital-provincial authorities, especially those bordering neighboring countries, including Laos, Thailand and Vietnam, to step up crackdowns on drugs imported from abroad without further negligence. While this unit has compromised the security and social order.
At the same time, the President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs also called on all relevant authorities to closely monitor border crossings, corridors and other areas where drug criminals smuggle in chemicals to produce drugs. Addicted, as this case has been and was suppressed in Kampong Speu in the past.
