Kampong Chhnang Provincial Governor Leads a Red Cross Branch to Bring Relief to 8 Families Affected by Typhoon in Teuk Phos District
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Provincial Governor and Honorary Chairman of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, on the afternoon of March 29, 2022, led the working group of the Provincial Red Cross Branch to bring donations to the people affected by the typhoon. 8 families in Dam Reap village, Aphivath commune, Teuk Phos district.
The Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province talked to the people that natural disasters always happen everywhere, but no one wants it, but we can not avoid it. On behalf of the provincial authorities, we would like to express our condolences for the houses and property of the victims who were damaged by the wind, the houses collapsed, the roofs and walls were opened.
He also asked you to be very careful, especially to join together to maintain hygiene and implement the rules of the Royal Government is "3 do not and 3 prevent" to participate in the fight to prevent and eradicate Kovid-19 disease. Spread into the base.
On that occasion, Ms. Born Sophy, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, also said that where there are difficulties such as natural disasters, the Red Cross always comes down to help solve your problems in all areas.
Today, she would like to bring a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and bring the Red Cross gifts to 8 families, with each family receiving rice. 25 kilos, 1 noodle, 1 kit and a budget of 100,000 riels. Separately, the houses of the people who suffered the worst house collapse received an additional 500,000 Riels.
The commune chief of Aphivath also confirmed that eight houses were damaged by the strong wind, one of them collapsed and seven roofs and walls were opened on the afternoon of March 27 in Dam Reap village, Aphivath commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province. .
