Saudi Arabia announces suspension of military operations in Yemen
Riyadh: The Saudi-led Arab League, which is battling Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen, on Tuesday said it would suspend military operations from Wednesday. Following a call for a ceasefire by the United Nations. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday, March 30, 2022.
The United Nations has been cooperating with the Arab League, including the Houthi rebels, to seek a peace deal to end the war in Yemen that has erupted since 2015, as well as to restore the country's humanitarian situation. Hundreds of thousands of Yemenis are facing famine.
