Vietnam's economic growth slows to 5% in Q1
According to the General Statistics Office of Vietnam, GDP grew by 5.05% in the first three months of this year compared with the same period last year. This is down from the 5.22% previously reported rate for the last quarter of 2021.
Vietnam's parliament in January approved a stimulus package worth about 347 trillion VND ($ 15.2 billion) to revive the economy affected by Kovid-19. The budget will focus on increasing infrastructure costs and assisting businesses and workers affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak, which the government expects to boost GDP growth by 6% to 6.5% this year. .
