Private Security Management Department Continues to Hold 34th Private Security Agency Training Course to Strengthen Capacity
(Phnom Penh): The Private Security Management Department of the National Police General Commission this morning, March 30, 2022, continued to hold the 34th Private Security Agency Training Course to strengthen the capacity and increase the knowledge of private security agencies. The opening ceremony was presided over by Lt. Gen. Men Sam An, Deputy Director of the Private Security Management Department, on behalf of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department.
Speaking on behalf of the Director of the Department of Private Security Management, Major General Men Sam An expressed his condolences and greetings from the leadership, especially Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and General Dr. Neth Savoeun. General Commissioner of the National Police to all private security agencies.
The Deputy Director of the Department continued that today is an important opportunity to continue to open training courses for private security agencies to be able to participate in the protection of security, order and safety for the whole society. He also reminded of the past involvement of private security agencies with the competent authorities, especially with the National Police Force in maintaining order and social security.
Lt. Gen. Men Sam An also sincerely commended and encouraged all private security agencies who paid attention to their work and participated in disseminating and implementing the safe village-commune policy, especially cooperation. With the National Police in the past and in the future.
