Singapore Ambassador to Cambodia visits Anlong Veng Peace Center and Anlong Veng District Historic Site
(Oddar Meanchey): The Ambassador of Singapore to Cambodia, Ms. Tu Lechheng, on March 29, 2022, visited the Anlong Veng Peace Center and the historical tourist site of Anlong Veng District, where the war ended and peace began. Repeat.
The Ambassador became the second ASEAN diplomat to visit the Anlong Veng area while Cambodia was chairing the rotating ASEAN.
The Ambassador arrived at the Anlong Veng Peace Center with a warm welcome from Mr. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and Dr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of the Anlong Veng Peace Center.
During her visit, she aims to explore the historical site of Anlong Veng, the last stronghold of the Khmer Rouge movement. Anlong Veng district has 14 historical sites that serve national and international tourist destinations.
On the occasion of the Ambassador's visit, Dr. Ly Sok Kheang also presented some work related to the establishment of a classroom forum on the history of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979).
The Ambassador then proceeded to the former Pol Pot and Khieu Samphan houses, the former Ta Mok meeting house on Dangrek Mountain and the Ta Mok House Museum. Youk Chhang, director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, described each historical site in detail and focused on the discussion of the word "peace" that Cambodia has received today.
Brigadier General Nith Narong also participated in commenting on the historical story of the war in Anlong Veng and the achievement of peace under the win-win policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Currently, Anlong Veng is starting to take a step towards a new face through the construction of the "Victory Monument in Anlong Veng".
Before returning, Ambassador Tuy Le Chheng expressed her appreciation for the study visit to learn about war and peace in Cambodia, as well as the mission of the Anlong Veng Peace Center in educating young people about the history of the Khmer Rouge.
