Singapore supports US military presence in Asia
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Singapore Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong on Monday met with US Secretary of Defense Lloyd Austin at the Pentagon, where the two reaffirmed their defense ties. The parties strongly recognize Singapore's role as a major US security cooperation partner. This was released by CNA on Tuesday, March 29, 2022.
According to a statement issued by the Singapore Prime Minister's Office, Lee Hsien Loong and Austin discussed defense cooperation in areas such as the Internet, virtual intelligence and joint training, and agreed on the importance of participation. The United States' permanent presence in Asia, as well as the exchange of views on the international and regional situation, especially the war in Ukraine.
According to Lee Hsien Loong, Singapore believes the US presence in the Asia-Pacific region is crucial to lasting peace, stability and prosperity in the region, and Singapore will continue to support the US military presence in Asia. .
