Samdech Techo Hun Sen Issues Sub-Decree Recognizing Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri University
Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri University has two locations, the first location is at Wat Preah Ind Samaki Thom, Trapeang Krapeu village, Kraing Makak commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, and the second location is in Rokar Thom village, Bek Chan commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province. The university is under the auspices of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri University also offers undergraduate training with 5 faculties: * Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Languages * Faculty of Science and Technology * Faculty of Social Sciences * Faculty of Engineering and Architecture * High School of Development and Tourism.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon briefs Cambodian diplomats and embassies on his first visit to Myanmar
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, on March 29, 2022, provided information to foreign diplomats and embassies in Cambodia on his first visit to the country. Myanmar as Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair.
On Facebook, the Deputy Prime Minister confirmed: "Not unlike last week's press conference, when I just returned to Cambodia, I gave a brief assessment of this issue and the future direction we have planned. . "We are also looking forward to my own visit or to represent the Special Envoy's office in the spirit of promoting the progress of this work."
It should be noted that Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, in his capacity as Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair on Myanmar, paid his first working visit to the country on March 21-23, 2022. The mission was accompanied by His Excellency Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and His Excellency Lim Jock Hoi, Secretary-General of ASEAN.
(Phnom Penh): The Chom Chao flyover and subway, which is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, so far, the whole construction site is 100 percent completed, and is scheduled to be officially inaugurated on the 31st. March 2022, presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In order for the above ceremony to run smoothly and successfully, on the afternoon of March 29, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, led a professional officer of local authority and contractor to inspect the actual situation at the venue of the ceremony. Located west of the flyover and the Chom Chao subway.
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed professional officers and district authorities and relevant officials to clean the remaining work, such as cleaning the soil and debris, that is, until the day of the ceremony is all clean. In addition, the strengthening of order and security work was also recommended by Mr. Khuong Sreng.
In connection with the inauguration of the Choam Chao flyover and subway, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has also issued a notice for residents to avoid traffic and temporarily suspend traffic across the Choam Chao intersection (formerly Chom Chao roundabout). Also on March 31, 2022, that is, start closing and avoiding traffic from 5 am until the end of the program.
It should be noted that the Choam Chao flyover and subway is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, contracted by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC), with a construction period of 30 months and a construction budget of approximately 22 million US dollars. .
Based on the technical specifications of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, this construction site is divided into 3 parts.
* Bridge 1: It is the main flyover connecting traffic from Russian Boulevard to National Road No. 3, with a total length of 408 meters and a width of 15.8 meters, with two lanes to two lanes to a bridge slope of 4.5 meters and a maximum height. The traffic under the bridge is 5.5 meters.
* Second Bridge: Separate from the main flyover, turn left and connect the traffic from Russian Boulevard to Veng Sreng for one-way traffic with one lane for cars and one lane for motorcycles with a total length of 202 meters (40 meters of flyover, subway) 118 meters long and 44 meters long dirt road) 5.25 meters wide.
The surface road is the main road connecting National Road 4 to Veng Sreng Road with a total length of 235 meters and a width of 8.5 meters for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles. The subway is a 470-meter-long, 8.5-meter-wide one-way traffic lane from National Highway 4 to the Russian Federation Boulevard for one-way traffic with one lane for cars and one lane for motorcycles.
The bridge will be 100 years old, equipped with lighting poles, road network around the flyover and underground water reservoir, as well as automatic pump motors.
It should be noted that the flyover and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout officially opened the construction site on June 29, 2018 under the presidency of Prime Minister Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. This flyover is the sixth flyover in Cambodia.
The 34th ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHRC) Meeting has officially started.
The meeting also evaluated the overview of the plan of the old mandate 2019-2021 and the preparation of the implementation of the new mandate plan 2022-2024. AYA Representative in 2022-2024, Mr. Keo Remy, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian National Human Rights Committee, chaired the meeting, focusing on the rights of persons with disabilities and other related issues.
Mr. Keo Remy stated that the workshop aims to facilitate the change of work that has already been done in the past and to ensure the community of AICHR institutions and also to strengthen the relationship with stakeholders.
According to Sreang Chenda, a member of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, the meeting discussed the ICHA normative documents as well as the sharing of various ASEAN documents related to human rights as well as the ASEAN Charter and the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. ASEAN and AICA Statutes relating to human rights that ACHA must uphold.
In addition, he said, there are plans to focus on human rights issues, focusing on the rights of people with disabilities, what needs to be done to promote people with disabilities and protect their rights.
It should be noted that on the occasion of the opening of the Icha meeting, Mr. Keo Remy welcomed the representatives of each country to participate and shared experiences related to human rights issues.
Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana and Lok Chumteav Ly Hiek Ratana Donate $ 10,000 on the Occasion of the 159th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2022
