Kampong Thom Deputy Governor Raises Nutrients in Breast Milk and Promotes Breastfeeding
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Touch Sokha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, mentioned many good nutrients in breast milk and called for the promotion of breastfeeding because there is no better product than breast milk. No, including powdered milk that is formulated correctly.
This confirmation was made by the Deputy Governor during the official opening ceremony of the breastfeeding room at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall and at the Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Women's Affairs on March 29, 2022.
To participate in implementing Cambodia's commitment to achieve the exclusive breastfeeding rate for infants and children from zero to 6 months by 85% by 2030, Deputy Governor Touch Sokha appealed to the Department And other workplaces should consider setting up a breastfeeding room to facilitate women returning from work to continue breastfeeding in accordance with Articles 14 and 185 of the Cambodian Labor Law.
Congratulations! A baby wild elephant was born from the love between a male wild elephant and a female domestic elephant named Chi Pal two years ago.
(Phnom Penh): It is amazing and unimaginable that a female elephant named Jipal, who was teased by a male wild elephant for two weeks before returning to a conservation site in Mondulkiri province, gave birth to a baby A female elephant on March 25, 2022, was surprised because she did not expect to be pregnant.
He said that on behalf of the Department of Environment of Mondulkiri Province, always support the activities of conservation of natural resources, culture, traditions and customs of the indigenous people in Mondulkiri. According to the tradition of the Pnong people in Mondulkiri province, when an elephant has a child, it must be sacrificed by cutting buffaloes, cows, pigs, chickens and ducks to ask for happiness.
Secretary of State Neth Pheaktra and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that Chi Pich was the second district baby elephant to be born in the last three months, while in December 2021 a local baby elephant named Noel was born in On the territory of Ratanakkiri province. This is the most exciting news.
