Arrest of a police officer at the General Department of Logistics in connection with the case of fraud of nearly 300,000 dollars, the case of running into the police force
(Phnom Penh): A police officer working in the General Department of Logistics and Finance of the Ministry of Interior was arrested by the Criminal Police Force and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the complaint of the victim related to the case of nearly $ 300,000 fraud. Run into the ranks of National Police officers.
According to the report, after the arrest, the Criminal Police Department sent 39-year-old Leng Sothy Vun, a police officer living at No. 03, Street 123, Village 1, Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkar Mon, to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the afternoon of March 29, 2022. This.
Twenty-eight victims have lodged a complaint with the Criminal Police Department, alleging that in late 2019, Leng Sothyvun used his position as a police officer at the General Department of Logistics to defraud victims. He, an assistant to an adult, was able to run the 28 victims to join the National Police for only six months and was named in all the ranks, requiring a fee of $ 18,000 each.
Believing in the suspect, the victim collected $ 280,000 and handed it over to Leng Sothy Vun to run as promised, but in the end the suspect was unable to escape and refused to return the money to the victim. Only then did the victims decide to file a complaint against the suspect to the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior to seek justice.
In front of the police, the suspect, Leng Sothy Vun, admitted that he actually received $ 280,000 from the victims to run for the National Police.
Kampot tourist port construction project achieved 93.41%, scheduled to be completed by the end of June 2022
(Kampot): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on March 29, 2022, led the relevant technical working group of the Ministry to inspect the progress of the construction of the international tourist port in Kampot province with the participation of the technical team of the Department. Public Works and Transport, construction company representatives, technical consultants and stakeholders.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed that the project to build an international tourist port in Kampot province, located in Teuk Chhou district, is being built on an area of 4 hectares with a depth of 4.5 meters, financed by the Asian Development Bank. US $ 10 million and as of March 22, 2022, 93.41% of the construction has been completed, which is scheduled to be completed on June 30, 2022.
The Senior Minister also emphasized that under the shadow of peace and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Cambodia will become a high middle income country by 2030, the living standard of the people will be richer, better and more prosperous. Develop more and step up to become a high-income country by 2050.
Mr. Sun Chanthol further stated that after the completion of the construction, this international tourist port will be an important gateway for national and international tourists to travel by water, especially tourists from Thailand and Vietnam. Cambodia is a port for travelers, not a cargo port.
It should be noted that this port contributes to the development of tourism in Kampot province, helps create job opportunities, increase income and improve the living standards of the people. This port is part of the tourism infrastructure development project for sustainable growth in the Greater Mekong Subregion. The construction of this port is under the control of the sub-project implementation unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
The port is an important international gateway by sea, connecting tourist transport to the southern islands and connecting Kampot province of Cambodia to the world. Through this port, it will further promote the development of tourism and related sectors in Kampot province, Bokor mountain resort and Cambodia's coastal tourist destinations.
US Department of Health and US Embassy Disseminate Results on Using Technology to Improve the Quality of Health Services and Green Smart Hospital
(Phnom Penh): Our medical program of First Vision Tech Asia in collaboration with the US Embassy in Cambodia and the Ministry of Health this morning, March 29, 2022, organized a workshop to disseminate the results of the project on "Using technology to improve the quality of health services. And Green Smart Hospital. ”
The project supported hospitals and clinics from Phnom Penh, Battambang and Siem Reap to implement the project and named it "Green Smart Hospital Member Network".
The Smart Green Hospital Network is a network of 20 member hospitals and clinics that have participated in the Clean and Green Urban Environment Campaign, shifting from paper, printing and reducing the use of hospital facilities. Turn to the "Our Hospital" digital hospital management system to improve technology in green hospitals.
The 20 hospitals and clinics that are members of the project have decided to join the Smart Green Hospital membership network, shifting their hospitals from paper to digital to make it easier to manage and operate in Its hospitals, as well as promoting technology systems in the health sector in Cambodia.
The Green Smart Hospital Network project started in October 2020 and will be completed by the end of March 2022. The project involves 867 doctors and hospital staff and manages 108,750 patient records, most of them women.
Through the use of digital hospital management systems, we not only participate in clean and green urban environment campaigns, but also accelerate all operations in hospitals or clinics through digital systems to accelerate treatment. Fast, modern, saves time and money for providers and patients, especially women and children.
Ms. Pong Limsan also added that we also have another purpose is to contribute to the environment, because we know that in the past, hospitals used paper to fill out patient documents and operations. But now we are replacing all those transactions digitally. Our project also helps a lot with patients who are women and children.
At the same time, Mr. W. Patrick Murphy congratulated the 20 hospitals and clinics that have successfully implemented the Green Smart Hospital Network project now and he expects that this project will greatly contribute to support Provide customer service as well as contribute to mitigating environmental impacts and climate change.
Dr. O Vandin said that the project "Using technology to operate a smart green hospital" aims to contribute to the modernization of digital technology in the health sector in Cambodia, and is another positive step in the contribution. Implement the National Health Strategic Plan, which has been focusing on modernizing digital technology in public and private hospitals.
This project has helped private hospitals in Phnom Penh, Battambang and Siem Reap to process digital healthcare services and put all of these hospitals and clinics in charge, not just as responsible providers. But becoming a hospital and clinic is responsible for building a green city and a clean environment.
Ms. O Vandin said that the use of modern digital technology to improve the quality of health services is also an important point that is included in the strategic policy of the Ministry of Health of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Ministry of Health is also supporting and encouraging the full participation of all stakeholders, including government institutions, the private sector and partner organizations.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: Cambodia is applying for a loan from a Chinese friend to build National Road No. 3 Kampot-Veal Rinh
(Kampot): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, stated that so far, the Ministry is waiting for the budget to request a loan from a Chinese friend to build a 20-kilometer National Road No. 3 Kampot-Veal Rinh. Meters in areas with contaminated soil, technically correct and durable.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "Samdech Techo Hun Sen has asked his Chinese friend for a concessional loan to build the 20-kilometer road, and HE Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, has written a letter. "In writing to the Chinese embassy, and to request this funding officially, we are waiting for a loan from a Chinese friend for us to build here."
In order to solve the problem of 20 km road in the current situation, the Senior Minister also stated that the Ministry is trying to find sources of funds to rehabilitate this road to facilitate people's traffic and transportation more smoothly. First, temporarily until the Ministry receives the budget for the construction of this road in a technical manner and can be used for a long time.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the section of National Road No. 3 (Kampot-Veal Renh) has a total length of 54.3 km, of which the World Bank has already provided funding for the restoration of 34 km, but 20 km. Others have a lot of problems that can not be fixed, damaged for a long time and never stuck firmly.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also asked for tolerance from the people and road users, especially users of this section of road for causing difficulties in traveling late and requested not to exceed the transport. The weight limit set by law, which makes the road worse and worse.
