Kampong Chhnang Provincial Information Department official: Some journalists are still writing violent news and inciting anger, causing problems for themselves and the society
(Kampong Chhnang): The Department of Information of Kampong Chhnang Province on the morning of March 29, 2022, in cooperation with the Peace Press Organization (ACT), opened a training course for 10 journalists in the province and 5 farming communities in Anchanh Rong commune. Write and disseminate information peacefully and non-violently. The training course was held for 2 days in Kampong Chhnang Provincial Information Department.
At the opening ceremony of the above training course, Mr. Heng Choch, Deputy Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Information Department, said to all participants that in order to gain knowledge in this training course, all participants must pay attention to learn in order to gain knowledge in Write peaceful and non-violent news for implementation in your career as a journalist with professional ethics, help the people and help the society to have peace.
He added that in the past, a small number of journalists did not fully understand the professional ethics, and continued to write violent and provocative news, causing problems for themselves and society. He hopes that this training will help journalists in Kampong Chhnang to gain knowledge that is important to apply to help people, communities and society to achieve peace.
Ms. Srey Sotheavy, Director of Peace Media (ACT), at the opening ceremony of the training, also said that the opening of this training course is to want journalists to know how to write and disseminate information peacefully to participate in conflict resolution and conflict resolution. Violence at the local and community level for the people to live in peace.
