Senior officials of the Ministry of Information remind journalists to take strict measures to improve the quality of factual information for the benefit of the public
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kem Kunavath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information, reminded journalists and media units to take strict measures to improve the quality of information and to produce content for the public good.
At the same time, Mr. Kem Kunavath said that the media has played a prominent role in disseminating professional information during the outbreak of the Kovid 19 epidemic and helping to disseminate health guidelines, preventive measures to the public. Timely as there is an increase in fake news and misinformation.
He said that the meeting of national journalists and journalists from LMC member countries today is a good start to strengthen the knowledge and professionalism of LMC journalists and is a forum for journalists to learn from the discussion. Networking and sharing experiences with each other about our role as journalists in contributing to the strengthening of LMC cooperation, promoting peace, prosperity and economic development.
In addition, the Secretary of State stated that in order to become a journalist who can contribute to the strengthening of this cooperation, journalists must have the ability to report and disseminate accurate information and to cooperate among journalists. Towards the establishment of the Lanchang-Mekong Journalists Club.
Mr. Kem Kunavath said that in the past, media cooperation among LMC member countries was bilateral and there was no platform where journalists from all six countries worked together to share information and work experience. That no. Strengthening cooperation among journalists can enhance the quality and richness of information, efficiency and time savings.
At the same time, the senior official of the Ministry of Information stated that this potential cooperation focuses on three pillars of cooperation: first: political and security issues, second: economic development and sustainability, and third: Socio-cultural and people-to-people exchanges, especially people-to-people contacts in the border areas of the country along the Lancang-Mekong River.
He stressed that the media and the media have played an important role in raising public awareness of LMC cooperation and as an important means of sharing information from the economy, politics, society and culture of the country. Members. The value and importance of the media and the press is even more apparent when a country faces insecurity, war, or a public health crisis such as Kovid 19.
