(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association has strengthened the capacity of branch managers of financial institutions throughout the country to manage branches effectively, sustainably, ethically and professionally through the training of district and provincial branch managers of microfinance institutions. And member banks nationwide.
These five regional workshops, in collaboration with the Credit Bureau of Cambodia (CBC) under the auspices of the National Bank of Cambodia, will contribute to the sustainability of financial institutions for the benefit of both clients and the financial sector as a whole. As well as contributing to boost national economic growth. Sister sues her brother to the court to demand the land back after his brother violated the fence to block the road in Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province
(Kampong Speu): A 71-year-old woman decided to file a lawsuit against her brother to the Kampong Speu Provincial Court to reclaim more than 1,000 square meters of land after her brother blocked the road. Travel to and from home.
Plaintiff Oum Yoeun, 71 years old, living in Kork Dangkor village, Pich Mony commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province, stated in his complaint dated 28 March 2022 that in 1982 he had occupied the land plot 579 (which is in dispute). With the local authority knowing and legally recognizing that the land is located in Kork Dangkor village, Pich Mony commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province.
Suddenly, at the beginning of February 2022, Oum Chum, his brother, built a fence to block the road so that the landowner, Oum Yoeun, could not enter or leave the house at the back, so the landowner decided to file a lawsuit to claim his land. He returned and asked the court to help open the back door because his family, who lived in the back, had no access to his house.
Nop Sok, chief of Pich Mony commune, said he had initially banned Oum Chum from building a fence because it was illegal, but he did not listen to the commune chief and continued to do so arbitrarily.
The commune chief continued, "This land is definitely the legal property of Oum Yoeun, so Oum Chum blocked the entrance to his house illegally and he will make a report to clarify this more if there is a request from you." Relevant laws.
Please be informed that the plaintiff, Oum Yoeun, had filed a complaint with the local authority in the village, commune, and district to claim the land back, but Oum Chum refused to return it and built a roadblock. Do not allow landowners to enter or leave the house in the back lot.
Around this case, Mrs. Oum Yoeun complained to her brother Oum Chum to the court to claim this land because many local authorities and witnesses who knew the truth expressed their support and asked the court to deal with this matter as soon as possible. Oum Chum has never heard of the local authorities' resolution and ban, claiming that a police officer from the Kampong Speu Provincial Police.
