Neak Oknha Kith Meng Highlights Investment Potential in Cambodia at Francophone Economic and Trade Economic Forum
A press release from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, obtained by Fresh News on the afternoon of March 28, 2022, states that the forum focuses on three main areas: digital, renewable energy and agriculture. Industry as well as a business meeting between Cambodian companies and Francophonie.
Speaking on the occasion of this high-level economic forum, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, warmly welcomed the Francophone delegation to visit the Kingdom of Cambodia, the first Francophone International Economic and Trade Mission in Southeast Asia. .
The President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce emphasized that the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce is pleased to participate in this historic event, and that the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce has always supported the activities of the International Organization of Francophonie to promote Cambodia's economic relations with Francophonie, especially the connection. Cambodian company with Francophonie.
The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce co-organized two outreach workshops on Francophone economic and trade missions. The first workshop will be held on December 7, 2021 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the second workshop will be held on February 8, 2022 at Aquation Park, Koh Pich.
The President briefed the Francophone delegation on Cambodia's potential sectors, strong economic growth over the past few decades, and outlined the Royal Government of Cambodia's correct and timely measures to curb the spread of disease. Kovid 19 and the restoration of economic and business activity.
In addition, Cambodia has a wide market and a favorable geographical location at the heart of ASEAN, which provides business opportunities as a basis for production and export of products to the world market within the framework of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement. RCEP) Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement and other concessional frameworks to the United States and the European Union.
On the occasion of this high-level economic forum, on behalf of the President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, Duke Kith Meng signed three Memoranda of Understanding between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Chamber of Commerce of Francophonia, chaired by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs. Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Louise Mushikiwabo, Secretary-General of the Francophone International Organization:
