Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Reminds Measures to Prevent Any Tactics Attempting to Destroy or Obstruct the Election Process
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the Permanent Security Command for Elections (CEC) has reaffirmed various measures to prevent any tactics that attempt to destroy or obstruct The election process.
Speaking at the meeting to disseminate the inter-institutional plan on the work of reviewing the list and national-sub-national elections through the audio and video transmission system on the morning of March 28, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom mentioned the important role of C. "The purpose of the CPPCC is to take measures to prevent and combat any tactics that attempt to disrupt or obstruct the election process in any form," he said.
He reiterated his role in ensuring a peaceful, neutral political environment for free, fair and just elections in accordance with the principles of democracy, non-intimidation, non-violence and non-violence. Provide complete security and provide equal security services.
The CPP was established in late 2021 with Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng as its chairman, accompanied by three vice presidents, including Samdech Pichey Sena Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister. Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance.
During the meeting, Sar Kheng stressed that the Permanent Security Command for the Election must ensure a calm and neutral political environment so that the election can be free, fair and just in accordance with the principles of democracy, without threats or intimidation. Violence will ensure complete security and provide equal security services.
According to Samdech Sar Kheng, many national and sub-national elections in the past and the future are historic and proud events, as well as a demonstration of the political will and commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Promoting good governance, pursuing a policy of decentralization and deconcentration at the grassroots level, strengthening liberal democracy, pluralism, respect for human rights, strengthening the rule of law and national development.
