Support for Japanese government soars over war-related actions in Ukraine
According to a poll conducted by Japan's Nikkei and TV Tokyo, 67 percent of those interviewed this weekend said they support the Kishida government's move on Russia's special military operations in Ukraine since February 24 is considered by the West to be an invasion. Only 22 percent oppose the Japanese government's move.
The support rate for Kishida's government in October 2021 was 61 percent. Japan has joined the West in imposing economic sanctions on Russia, and the rise in support is a good sign as Japan's parliamentary elections approach in July.
