Preah Ang Duong Hospital has been a public administration institution since November 2012. The hospital is a polyclinic that provides eye, ear, nose, throat, dental, dermatology, cosmetic and rehabilitation services, obstetrics, gynecology, gastroenterology, hepatology, general surgery and diabetes.
The advent of otolaryngology, which is equipped with state-of-the-art equipment for diagnosis, treatment and surgery, will improve the provision of medical services to patients and will be another important part of the development of the health sector. In Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, expressed his great pleasure and congratulations to the Cambodian people for their achievements in providing better ear, nose and throat treatment services. Samdech Techo expressed the expectation that the new clinic will make a significant contribution to the treatment of people with ear, nose and throat diseases.
Cambodia and the Republic of Korea were connected during the 1970s and severed in 1975. It was not until 1997 that the relationship was reconnected. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, was a key player in seeking to connect this relationship by overcoming difficulties, as Cambodia was at the time having relations with North Korea, a conflicting party with South Korea.
At the inauguration ceremony of the new achievements as a result of the relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pride in the efforts to re-establish relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, added, "It is not just about aid or loans, but it is relevant in all areas, including politics, diplomacy, economy, society and culture, which we must do in all countries without discriminating against political regimes." "I am happy that what we have been here is for the benefit of our people."
Mr. Park Heung-kyung, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, stated that after the re-establishment of diplomatic relations in 1997, due to the important role of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia and the Republic of Korea have been making significant progress. Noticeable in bilateral relations. Relations have been deepened in all areas, including politics, economics and cooperation, development and culture.
Through this assistance, Korea has been providing assistance to the Ministry of Health for the construction of the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Vision Center at Preah Ang Duong Hospital, the building at Pursat Provincial Hospital and the building at Battambang Provincial Hospital. Among the valuable initiatives we have recently made is the groundbreaking of Maternal and Child Health Centers in Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri Provinces.
The Ambassador expressed the strong commitment of the Korean Government to its contribution to the ongoing efforts to develop the health sector in Cambodia. He added that on the path to a bright and prosperous future for Cambodia, the Republic of Korea and the Korean people will continue to be with the Kingdom of Cambodia and with the Cambodian people.
