The Cambodia-Korea Friendship Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital at Ang Duong Hospital was established to provide specialized treatment for people with ear, nose and throat problems.
A five-story building equipped with state-of-the-art equipment for diagnosis, treatment and surgery has been built on the grounds of Ang Duong Hospital to help improve the hospital's medical services.
The new Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital has a total area of 4,177.94 square meters with a total of 128 beds, including: outpatient, operating room, post-surgery room and emergency room.
