(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, March 28, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Dr. Park Heng Kyung, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, officially inaugurated the Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital. The Cambodian-Korean friendship was born from the fruits of the "Capacity Building Project for the Ear, Nose and Throat Center at Ang Duong Hospital".
During the inauguration, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today he was pleased to attend the inauguration of the Cambodia-Republic of Korea Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital at Ang Duong Hospital.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this year marks the 25th anniversary of the relationship between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea. The 25th anniversary of the many achievements of the relationship was opened and inaugurated.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodia-Republic of Korea Friendship Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital, which was inaugurated today, is the result of good relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Korea.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as the founder of the reconnection of relations with the Republic of Korea, Samdech is very proud of this relationship has led to many achievements.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for the transfer of all available Korean technology to Cambodian medical teams.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen is pleased that Preah Ang Duong Hospital has launched a patient information management technology system.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for 47 years, Samdech has been blind. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in addition to his eyes, he also had a problem with his right ear due to the use of weapons, which required only five shots, but Samdech fired up to 12 shots.
