Director General of Accounting and Auditing: Cambodia needs more accountants to ensure audit services!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Tharin, Director General of Accounting and Auditing Regulator, stated that Cambodia is in need of more accountants to ensure the adequacy of the supply of audit services in the market both now and in the future.
Mr Butharin added that although the world, as well as Cambodia, was in the midst of Kovid 19, autonomy had increased and so had fiscal revenues. Boosting the level of transparency in the financial statements, accounting and accounting of enterprises with audited services has helped increase fiscal revenue, even at a time when the economy has slowed.
