This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital at Ang Duong Hospital
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, March 28, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Dr. Park Heng Kyung, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, officially inaugurated the Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital. The Cambodian-Korean friendship was born out of the fruits of the "Capacity Building Project for the Ear, Nose and Throat Center at Preah Ang Duong Hospital".
The Cambodia-Korea Friendship Ear, Nose and Throat Hospital was built after the construction of the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Vision Building at Preah Ang Duong Hospital.
The vision building was inaugurated in 2015. The building was constructed under a grant from KOICA at a cost of US $ 5.5 million. The building has 75 rooms, including an outpatient room, an inpatient room and an operating room.
