Nearly a third of the Netherlands is below sea level, with the lowest point being 6.7 meters below sea level and the highest point just over 300 meters above sea level. So you can imagine that the Netherlands has a very flat surface.
You may be wondering why this European country does not sink under the sea? The reason is because the Netherlands has a special defense system. Through the construction of a robust dam system and a state-of-the-art pumping system, combined with sand dunes along its shores, the Netherlands has the ability to stay afloat. The Netherlands has a coastline of 230 km, of which 75% is sand dunes, which can be several kilometers long.
