Senior Minister Kun Kim Meets and Visits More Than 100 “A1 and A2” Disabled Veterans in Kandal Province
(Kandal): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on March 26, 2022, paid a courtesy call on 127 “A1 and A2” disabled veterans in Kandal province. .
The meeting was also attended by the Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, Deputy Provincial Governor, Provincial Police Commissioner, Provincial Military Area Commander, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, District Governor and Inspector. Municipal police, district administration chiefs, and veterans also attended.
After listening to the welcome report of the President of the Provincial Veterans Association and speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim urged all leaders of the Takeo Provincial Veterans Association to continue to do good deeds and do their best to solve all problems. Difficulties of the Veterans Association.
The Senior Minister also mentioned that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, who always mentioned the consideration for veterans with great and invaluable merits, dared to sacrifice meat. Fresh blood and all kinds of sacrifices in the cause of liberating the nation, the people from the genocidal regime, making Cambodia peaceful and prosperous to this day.
He said that Cambodian veterans in Kandal province are a heroic example and a great merit of the heroic warriors of the Armed Forces and people of all walks of life who have bravely sacrificed their lives for the cause of our beloved motherland. Of us.
He added that the patriotic sacrifices of our heroes, veterans, warriors and our people at all stages of history have contributed significantly to the protection of territorial integrity, building peace and social stability for the Kingdom of Cambodia to ensure Economic and social development for the benefit of the motherland and the people of Cambodia.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also praised and appreciated the active and voluntary efforts of the leaders of the association at all levels, making the work of the association a remarkable progress. He also advised the leaders of the association at all levels to continue to visit the veterans to find out about their living conditions, health and measures to help them when there is a problem in time.
Separately, the leadership of the Provincial Veterans Association must cooperate with professional institutions to act as a staff for the provincial governor to manage the social land concessions given by the state to be divided into lots and to request Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association to build houses. To homeless members.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also emphasized to the meeting that all that the Cambodian Veterans got today was because our country is peaceful, so we must thank the peace and be grateful to Samdech Techo Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of peace.
At the same time, 127 disabled veterans "A1 and A2" received some money and gifts, while the director of the administrative post and all participating officials also received money.
