Post chief in Prey Veng province who shot and killed his wife was jailed
(Prey Veng): Police Chief of Phnov I Administration, Sithor Kandal District, Prey Veng Province, was arrested and sent to the Provincial Court and detained on March 26, 2022 after shooting his wife. Caused death in a pool of blood.
According to Prey Veng provincial police, the shooting happened at 8:30 pm on March 24, 2022, on the road in front of Phat Sandong pagoda in Phat Sandong village, Phnov 1 commune, Sithor district. Kandal, Prey Veng Province.
Authorities identified the gunman as 53-year-old Mao Sovan Hong, chief of the Phnov 1 administrative police station, living in Phat Sandong village, Phnov 1 commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province. The victim was his wife, Sok Muy, 51 years old.
The gunman reportedly fired K54 assault rifles at four of the victims, but two exploded in the middle and neck, killing them instantly at the scene. The reason for the shooting was a verbal dispute on the street after the birthday party of the villagers together.
It should be noted that in this shooting incident, under the direct command of Major General Prum Santhor, Prey Veng Provincial Police Commissioner and led by Brigadier General Pov Chivi, Deputy Police Commissioner, received a criminal plan and led the force all night, leading to the arrest of the Post Chief. The first administrative police immediately went to build a case for legal proceedings.
