(Phnom Penh): In the framework of the one-hour celebration of Earth Day on the morning of March 26, 2022, the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Tourism, Mondulkiri Provincial Administration, WWF and partner private companies jointly organized a race program under the theme " Run for the environment, nature and health ”on the territory of Sen Monorom, Mondulkiri province, which has been certified as a clean land city of ASEAN.
The event was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Mr. Top Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, and was attended by nearly 200 participants from Phnom Penh and Mondulkiri.
He said that nature can be without people, but people can not be without nature, it is needed every day. He stressed that if nature is destroyed, human and animal life will face the same destruction. Respect, love, care and conservation of natural resources is respect for the love of human life. "We respect nature, nature will give us a lot of respect and benefits," he said.
Runners, both Cambodians and foreigners, are full of happy and proud faces. The race is about 5 km in Sen Monorom, from the WWF headquarters to Sous Chbar Damrey Dek in the center of Sen Monorom. The image of the race shows the people of Sen Monorom the importance of protecting and conserving natural resources and taking into account the health of themselves and the community as a whole.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that from Sen Monorom city, Mondulkiri province, people will understand more clearly that the environment and natural resources are really important and our health is more important and also depends on the natural environment.
In this race, the 1st to 3rd place winners received some prizes and equipment from the presidency from the Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Tourism, Provincial Administration and WWF.
Separately, the one-day Land Day will be celebrated on the evening of March 26, presided over by Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra at Sen Monorom Park, expecting a large number of participants. On the other hand, the famous singers in Cambodia are Miss Meas Soksophea and other singers and there are also performances from indigenous people.
