Minister Khieu Kanharith Chairs a Press Conference on the 2nd Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, on the evening of March 26, 2022, presided over a press conference on the 2nd Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award for the Cambodian Voice of Persons with Disabilities under the slogan "Thank you for bringing peace". "There is hope."
The program is scheduled to take place in three provincial capitals, starting in late April in Phnom Penh, and the semi-finals are scheduled to take place in Sihanoukville. The final is scheduled to take place in Siem Reap.
The conference program was also attended by leaders of the Ministry of Information and relevant ministries, as well as leaders from various media, which took place at the Sofitel Phnom Penh.
The 2nd Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award for Cambodian People with Disabilities is not a coincidence, this program was initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Under the context of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has explored all means to help people with disabilities improve and improve their living standards and provide opportunities for people with disabilities to express their abilities and talents in street, art, music, traditional and contemporary music.
The 2nd Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award for the Cambodian Voice of Persons with Disabilities was organized for two purposes:
* First, promote the role and values of people with disabilities in society to give them the opportunity to show their abilities and talents, so that they have more opportunities to participate in many important social activities.
Second, show the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting the strong and independent capacity of people with disabilities so that they can integrate with society in all areas.
Although people with disabilities have disabilities, but their morale and will are not disabled, they are also important human resources and can not be lacking in helping to develop the socio-economic. So we must not leave people with disabilities, we must protect their legal rights and freedoms, and fully support their development.
The organization of this program is expected that all people with disabilities continue to be strong and active, without despairing or giving up opportunities for themselves, no matter what the circumstances, to demand their role and self-worth in society together. Build a social environment full of harmony.
