Please be informed that the construction of this new party building is a unique achievement in a peaceful society, this building is 60 meters wide and 89.2 meters long, maximum height 23.56 meters, with a total usable area of 10,492 square meters. Built on an area of 36,000 square meters, there is a basement, ground floor, first floor, second floor and basement.
The building was designed using a combination of styles and was built facing east on National Road 21 in Tuol Krasaing village, Roka Khpos commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province. The front of the building is adorned with two Angkor Wat-style standing stone lion statues, the roof is designed in the ancient Khmer style and divided into three parts by the main roof and the center of the building and connected to each other for music.
All the roofs are highlighted by the Angkor Wat Meas sculptor, which can be seen from all directions of the building.
The front entrance is divided into three sections for ease of use and is decorated with vertical sections and diamond pillars using the Banteay Srei style. As well as decorating and arranging various infrastructures in the entire party building, the total budget for the construction of more than 8 million dollars has not yet been paid for the land. OIF Secretary-General to visit Cambodia next week and lead the first Francophone Economic and Trade Mission in Southeast Asia
