(Phnom Penh): Regarding the registration of candidates of 17 political parties to compete in the Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate, the Candlelight Party was the most complained and objected by the people because it was not implemented. In accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022.
Mr. Hang Puthea said that the resolution of the complaint is at least 3 days after receiving the complaint, the NEC will prepare to resolve it. The briefing process or public process is based on the facts and the law that the NEC has the principles to implement in accordance with the rules and procedures of the election. The names of some candidates were removed by the NEC.
Previously, the NEC decided to delete the list of candidates of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey 1, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh (Decision on Case 051) because the list of candidates is not quality, forged documents and has a case in Some other communes.
Please be informed that the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election will be held on June 5, 2022. There are 17 political parties that have registered their candidates.
NEC Decides to Delete Candlelight Party Candidates in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey 1
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has decided to delete the list of candidates of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 1, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh, because the list of candidates does not have the quality to falsify documents that could face criminal penalties. Also.
The NEC stated that the law is in accordance with Article 42 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election and Section 6.6.3.5 of the Rules and Procedures for Commune / Sangkat Council Election. The fifth mandate, 2022, which states that "a brief biography and declaration of approval for the candidacy of candidates must be filled in the hands of each candidate."
Considering that the Candlelight Party has violated the above provisions, the Trial Chamber of the NEC decided to approve the complaint by deleting the Candlelight Party Candidate List in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang and Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 1 Election Commission rejects and deletes the list of candidates of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 1.
However, on March 22, 2022, the Candlelight Party issued a statement rejecting the NEC's decision to delete its party list. Regarding the rejection of the Candlelight Party, NEC member Hang Puthea said at a press conference on March 25 that "this statement does not reflect the implementation of laws, regulations and procedures of Commune / Sangkat council elections, ”he said.
Mr. Som Solida also stated that the issuance of the Candlelight Party's statement was contrary to the spirit of the NEC's Resolution No. 051, by diverting the subject matter from the delisting claim to the delisting claim. Candidates.
He made it clear that there were two lawsuits in Tuol Svay Prey 1 in the following cases:
* The first complaint is to remove 4 candidates from the list of candidates of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 1.
* The second complaint is the rejection of the Candlelight Party's list of candidates not to run in the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 2 due to the lack of quality of the list of candidates. Therefore, the NEC has decided to delete the entire list of candidates of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 1.
Mr. Som Solida continued that this issue is not the fault of each candidate, but the fault of the Candlelight Party itself, which did not fill in the correct documents that came with the application for registration of political party candidates at the office. Sangkat Toul Svay Prey 1.
Mr. Som Solida also stated that the forgery of documents by stakeholders of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey 1 may face more criminal charges related to forgery of public documents, but this is not the responsibility of the NEC. Mr. Hun Many supported the task of the CPPCC to mobilize intellectuals to volunteer for joint activities for the benefit of the nation.
