Russia holds large-scale military exercises in disputed archipelago with Japan after suspending World War II treaty negotiations
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's military has launched a large-scale military exercise involving more than 3,000 troops in the disputed archipelago with Japan after talks to seek an end to World War II treaties. 2 Officially between the two parties is suspended. This was released by Interfax news agency on Saturday, March 26, 2022.
The exercise comes after the Russian Foreign Ministry this week announced the official suspension of peace talks to end World War II with Japan over Tokyo sanctions against Moscow over the Ukraine war crisis.
Japan claims the former Soviet Union illegally occupied four islands there shortly after Japan declared World War II in August 1945, but Moscow argues its actions are legitimate. .
