Following is the announcement: Mr. Hun Many inaugurated the Memorial of the former Apheap Dam in Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province.
(Kampong Speu): Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency, this morning, March 26, 2022, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the monument of remembrance of the former Apap Dam called Department 401, located in Trapeang Peuk Village, Kat Phluk Commune, Bor Seth District. Kampong Speu Province.
This is the place where the genocidal Pol Pol has been used as a prison and killed more than 20,000 innocent people. Every year on May 20, people come from Kampong Speu, Kampong Cham, Kandal. Takeo and Kampong Chhnang always come to celebrate the memory of their relatives who died here.
It should be noted that in the Southwest Zone, there are many Khmer Rouge detention centers established since the early 1970s, such as the Kraing Ta Chan Security Department in Tram Kak District, Takeo Province, and M-15 in 32 areas, 13 in Omlaing District, and M-99 in the province. Kampong Speu.
According to an interview with Sok Mao, a former survivor of Department 401, when the Khmer Rouge first arrived, he saw the prison compound surrounded by large trees and barbed wire. Prison location.
In fact, Sok Mao, whose father was a commune chief during the Sihanouk and Lon Nol eras, was arrested by the Khmer Rouge from Saang district, Kandal province, and sent with his mother and two nephews to 401. In addition to the Khmer prisoners, there were also Vietnamese, who were then Viet Cong soldiers.
The last prisoner was killed on arrival without being questioned. The killing of Vietnamese prisoners at the time coincided with the expulsion of Vietnamese troops by the Khmer Rouge, as well as the general purge of Cambodians with ties to Vietnam during the year, especially when Vietnamese troops withdrew from Cambodia after the Paris Agreement between North Vietnam and the United States.
