The riel was reissued by the National Bank of Cambodia on March 21, 1980, 42 years ago. After the reprinting of the currency, after the Cambodian currency was completely abolished during the Khmer Rouge regime, the National Bank of Cambodia launched a series of campaigns and campaigns to increase the stability of the riel.
