Ministry of Interior Disclosure of Results of Workshop on Dissemination of Anti-Financing Law on Mass Destruction and Related Legal Documents
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 25, 2022, the Ministry of Interior organized a workshop to disseminate the Law on Anti-Financing of Mass Destruction and Related Legal Documents via ZOOM Video under the chairmanship of Mr. Bun Hon, Secretary of State Ministry of Interior, with a total of 377 participants, including professional officers of relevant units under the Ministry of Interior, as well as representatives from 147 local associations and non-governmental organizations.
The workshop shared the content of the anti-financing law on the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction, focusing on evasion and impunity, and the implementation of UN Security Council sanctions. At the same time, participants also exchanged views on the content of the law and the legal framework, procedures of law enforcement and the performance of individual reporting duties.
(Kampot): Mr. Men Pheakdey, Director of the Macro Data Management and Analysis Department of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that despite Cambodia's difficulties caused by the spread of Kovid 19 disease, microfinance operations in Cambodia are still operational and operational. By high responsibility always. During the impact of Kovid 19, banks and financial institutions also reorganized their loans to protect their clients.
Remarks by Mr. Men Pheakdey, Director of Macro Data Management and Analysis Department, National Bank of Cambodia, during the dissemination workshop on "Microfinance Sector in Cambodia" on March 25, 2022 Objects in Cambodia ”to stakeholders in Teuk Chhou, Kampot province.
He added that in order to strengthen the important role of the microfinance sector, the National Bank of Cambodia has carried out various activities and campaigns aimed at raising financial literacy to the public, promoting responsible lending and strengthening lending principles. Professional ethics.
He also asked for help to promote and educate people to borrow money from legal institutions, as well as use loans to target and comply with payment obligations. In particular, the relevant departments should thoroughly examine the financial situation of the people before issuing a certificate for applying for a loan.
He also asked local authorities to continue to report and co-operate in taking action against illegal savings or lending without proper permission in order to prevent local people from suffering and incurring debt. Exploitation of informal traders.
(Battambang): Mr. Soy Sokhan, Secretary of State of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation and Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, chaired a meeting to discuss the technical team on the possibility of restoration and development of Battambang Airport Class 4C on March 25, 2022.
Mr. Soy Sokhan said that based on the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has instructed the relevant ministries and provincial administrations to study the feasibility of rehabilitating Battambang Airport after being abandoned for many years.
He added that after the study, there are some problems that need to be solved by solving the problem of people living in the airport, the expansion of the runway, and more repairs need to be done because they have been left behind. Years ago.
Mr. Sok Lou expressed his support for the development of this airport into 4C to attract foreign and domestic tourists to travel directly to Battambang and to participate in the development of Battambang to grow further. And after the 4C Airport came into being, an achievement emerged.
He said that on behalf of the provincial administration will always cooperate to solve problems that affect the development of the airport in Battambang to make the airport appear in this agricultural land. 107 Former CNRP Members in Koh Kong Province Join CPP
(Koh Kong): 107 former members of the Cambodian National Rescue Party (CNRP) have volunteered to join the political life of the Cambodian People's Party under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The announcement of the inclusion of members of the Cambodian People's Party was made on the afternoon of March 25, 2022, under the presidency of Duke Ly Samet, representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party.
Duke Ly Samet met with 107 members of the former CNRP and other parties in Koh Kong province who volunteered to join the CPP in contributing to the betterment of Cambodian society. The leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Duke Ly Samet emphasized that joining politics with the CPP was the right decision because no political party now has a clear policy to lead the country like the CPP. No, that is, they do politics for the benefit of their families and serve foreigners only, without considering the well-being of the people.
On the contrary, the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party are always in solidarity with the people at all times, solve various problems for the people and never run away from the people, no matter what the circumstances.
"We have peace, stability, we have things like today, it is not a coincidence, but it is a good fate that Cambodia has Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, Samdech never made the people "Every class is disappointed." The tycoon called on party members, old and new, to work together to keep the peace, and not to allow any unscrupulous people to destroy it.
