Russia's missile strike on Ukraine has a 60 percent failure rate, according to US officials
WASHINGTON: The United States estimates that Russia's missile strikes on some specific targets in Ukraine have a failure rate of 60 percent. This was released by Reuters on Friday, March 25, 2022.
Reuters made the report based on exclusive sources it obtained from three US officials who were aware of the assessment, which could explain in part why Russia failed to achieve its military goals. Russia's offensive against Ukrainian troops has been halted by Western officials, who say it is stuck in almost every battle.
The three US officials, speaking on condition of anonymity, did not provide evidence to support the allegations, and did not specify why Russia's missile attack had such a high failure rate. Russia's Defense Ministry has not yet commented, but the Kremlin has said Putin's special military operations are proceeding as planned.
