Russey Keo District Unity Command raided a gambling place, confiscated a fishing game machine and 3 computers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ek Khun Doeun, Chairman of Russey Keo District Administrative Unity Command and District Governor, assigned Mr. Sou Sarath, Deputy Director of Khan Administration, to lead a force to crack down on a gambling place, confiscating a fishing game box. Two units and a computer while the overseer and the player run away.
According to Mr. Sou Sarath, after completing the raid operation, the Khan Administrative Unity Command sent evidence related to the crime, including a fishing game machine and two computers to be stored at the Khan Police Inspectorate to continue the procedure. . Press and Quick Reaction Unit: "When you see war, you understand the meaning, thank you for peace" (Video inside)
This video shows the deepest meaning and importance of peace that arises from the win-win policy of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo in the context of the war in Ukraine.
As people all over the world have been watching the war in Ukraine, everyone is deeply saddened and sympathetic to the people of Ukraine, especially women, the elderly and children who have fled the horrors of war. Shown daily.
Skyscrapers, houses, shops, airports, roads and infrastructure were engulfed in flames and destroyed by missiles. The lives of soldiers and civilians were tragically killed. Faced with all these tragedies, the President of Ukraine himself finally declared peace and considered peace very important for his country and its people.
At this point, we can understand without a doubt that peace is a universal value that human beings around the world aspire to. Peace is truly priceless.
This is why the Cambodian people have been giving so much value to peace and are so grateful to the founders of peace in Cambodia. Most Cambodians still vividly remember the end of the Cambodian war on the 29th. December 1998 Under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which brought complete peace throughout the country.
Calling for peace while the flames of war are burning is sadly outdated, and more broadly, "when you see war, you understand the meaning of 'thank you for peace.' When we see the war, we are grateful to the founder of peace, Techo Sen, who the Cambodian people continue to respect, love, support and believe in protecting and maintaining the hard-earned peace to last forever.
Watch the video: A disabled veteran, a member of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Preah Vihear Province, received a house as a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Preah Vihear): A house, a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, was led by Major General Chan Sopheaktra, Commander of the Provincial Military Operations Area and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Preah Vihear Province. The team handed over to a disabled veteran and his family living in Thomcheat village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province on March 25, 2022.
On this occasion, Major General Chan Sopheaktra sent a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, as well as Mr. Prak Sovann, Honorary President of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Preah Vihear Province. Always consider the well-being and living conditions of our Cambodian veterans in Preah Vihear province.
Lt. Gen. Chan Sopheaktra thanked the Provincial Military Working Group, the Provincial Armed Forces Working Group, the Deputy Chief of the District Armed Forces and local authorities, along with about 90 people, for helping to build a house. Our veterans now.
(Siem Reap): A senior official of the Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority said that the authority will cooperate with the Government of the Republic of India to repair and save the Kuk Temple or the Great Hermitage (N17) built of old sandstone. It is dilapidated and is being repaired.
The signing ceremony of the MoU took place during the 28th Plenary Meeting of the International Committee for the Coordination of Protection, Conservation and Development of Angkor Historical Site (ICC-Angkor) at Sofitel Angkor Phokitra Hotel, Siem Reap, chaired by Lok Chumteav Dr. Prof. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts.
Mr. Phan Nady said that the characteristics of the Sambor Prei Kuk group of temples are that most of the temples are built of brick, but the signing of a memorandum of understanding with India at this time is focused on the project to renovate the Kuk temple or the Maha Eisi hermitage temple, which is made of sandstone and has a similar style. Together with the temples of India just made India interested in the restoration project.
Senior Interior Ministry official: Too many drug detainees raise concerns about prison management and security
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pao Hamphan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, said that more than 54% of the total number of detainees involved in drug offenses raised concerns about the management and security of prisons.
A senior official of the Ministry of Interior said this on the occasion of the representative of Samdech Krala Hos Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, presiding over the meeting to disseminate the 2022 work direction of the Ministry of Interior, the work results in 2021 and the work direction in 2022 and the action plan. 2022 of the General Department of Prisons on the afternoon of March 25, 2022.
"Meanwhile, detainees involved in drug offenses make up 54.44% of the total number of detainees, which raises concerns about the management and security of prisons." This is an addition of the Ministry of Interior.
To solve the above challenges, Mr. Pao Hamphan mentioned Samdech Krala Hom's instructions on some important measures as follows:
* Efforts must be made to continue developing infrastructure in prisons, especially those with dilapidated old buildings that could pose a security and safety risk in those prisons.
* For detainees who have used illegal drugs, the General Department of Prisons shall cooperate with the relevant ministries and institutions to conduct medical examinations and develop programs to rehabilitate those detainees. At the same time, a drug control center for drug offenders in Loen Chey district, Pursat province, must be established to co-organize educational programs for inmates to transform themselves into good citizens in society.
* In order to improve vocational education for prisoners, the General Department of Prisons must study, research and establish industry and agro-industry in prisons.
* Examine the framework requirements for each correctional center and prison to organize prison guards in accordance with the size and role of each correctional center and provincial capital.
* The General Department should study the system of procedures for the integration of released prisoners into the community and the mutual information of prisoners after their release.
* The General Department of Prisons shall consult with the Ministry of Health to examine the feasibility of providing medical equipment and medicines for prison health posts and to strengthen the capacity of prison medical staff. At the same time, prisons must take care to strengthen health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 to prison guards and inmates across the country.
According to Mr. Chhem Savuth, "It is noteworthy that the number of detainees has increased since 2017 after the Royal Government launched a plan to fight against illegal drugs and tighten law enforcement in 2021. "The number of detainees has decreased by about 1,200, equivalent to 3.17% compared to December 2020."
