(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia, the Royal Government's Office for Investment, has issued a notification on "Measures to Control the Use of Chemical Drugs in Investment Companies." This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News on March 25, 2022.
In the spirit of strengthening the control over the use of chemicals that can be combined into drugs according to the actual use of all companies.
1. Manage and use chemicals that can be combined into drugs for use in its production line in accordance with the technical specifications and standards of use of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
2: Use chemicals that can be combined into drugs for the purpose that it requested and prohibit the sale or business to other companies.
3. There are clear technical experts in chemistry to manage and solve the problem of using chemicals that can be combined into drugs for its production line.
4: There is a clear record of the amount imported, the amount used and the amount of chemicals that can be combined into drugs for easy verification.
5. Make monthly, semi-annual and annual reports on the import, export and use of chemicals that can be combined with drugs to the relevant authorities.
The notice states that the company will face loss of motivation as well as other penalties in accordance with the laws and regulations in force in case of non-compliance or improper compliance with the above guidelines. . China calls NATO claim to support Russia's war in Ukraine false
