Chinese Foreign Minister visits India for first time since border dispute in 2020
New Delhi: Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi will meet with his Indian counterpart in New Delhi on Friday after arriving in the Indian capital under the auspices of the Indian Foreign Ministry. This is the first visit by a top Chinese official since the border dispute between the two countries in 2020. This was released by Reuters on Friday, March 25, 2022.
Prior to his visit to India, Wang Yi also visited Pakistan and Afghanistan this week and plans to continue his visit to Nepal. Sino-Indian relations, a longtime rival, have been strained since June 2020, when the two countries were embroiled in a border dispute that left 20 Indian troops dead and four Chinese troops dead.
