(Phnom Penh): The Chom Chao flyover and subway, which is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, is 100% completed and is scheduled to be officially inaugurated on March 31, 2022 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, after being temporarily allowed to pass by for almost a week.
This was confirmed by the Phnom Penh Capital Administration this morning, March 25, 2022, while the district authorities, together with other relevant authorities, arrived at the location of the flyover and subway Chom Chao to prepare for the ceremony. Go what was planned.
Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, on March 14th, led the professional officers as well as the contractor for the construction of the flyover and subway, inspected the construction site once and decided to let the people pass through. Temporarily on March 20.
It should be noted that the Choam Chao flyover and subway is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, contracted by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC), with a construction period of 30 months and a construction budget of approximately $ 22 million.
Roads and subways are curved roads connecting traffic from Veng Sreng Road to National Road 4 with a total length of 130 meters (13 meters of subway and 117 meters of underground road) 8.5 meters wide for one-way traffic. Two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles. The surface road is the main road connecting traffic from National Road 4 to Veng Sreng Road with a total length of 235 meters and a width of 8.5 meters for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles.
The subway is a 470-meter-long, 8.5-meter-wide lane from National Road 4 to the Russian Federation Boulevard for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles. Safety speed 40 km per hour for 8.5 meters wide road. 25 km / h for 5.25 m wide and 5.5 m wide.
The bridge will be 100 years old, equipped with lighting poles, road network around the flyover and underground water reservoir, as well as automatic pump motors. It should be noted that the flyover and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout officially opened the construction site on June 29, 2018 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Ministry will officially launch the geographical mark of "Mondulkiri Prey Honey" next week, collect 100 tons of honey a year for 2-3 million dollars
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce will officially inaugurate the geographical mark of "Mondulkiri Wild Honey" on March 27, 2022 to provide intellectual property protection to the Mondulkiri Wild Bee Conservation Association and To prevent the counterfeiting of the geographical mark of "Mondulkiri Wild Honey" in the national and international markets.
The inauguration ceremony of the geographical mark of "Mondulkiri Prey Honey" is scheduled to take place at Sen Monorom Park, Sen Monorom City, Mondulkiri Province in the presence of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce.
Chan Lalin, an official of the Cambodian Institute for Rural Research and Development (CIRD), told Fresh News on March 25 that after "Mondulkiri wild honey" became a geographical brand, it would further boost the brand's reputation. Well-known in national and international markets, increase value-added and improve the livelihood of the people in the Mondulkiri wild honey collection area.
He stated that after "Mondulkiri wild honey" became famous and well-known, the market of "Mondulkiri wild honey" was bigger than before, now the wild honey market in Mondulkiri province is Expanded to almost 25 provinces, most of which are sold and distributed in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, and after the geographical mark, this product is also planned to be exported to international markets.
According to the geographical indication book "Mondulkiri wild honey", the collection of Mondulkiri wild honey confirms the origin of geographical indication, except in some districts or municipalities in Mondulkiri province, such as Koh Nhek, Pichrada, Orang, Keo Seima and Sen Monorom city.
All members of the association must take care to protect the biodiversity in the community forest, especially in the area where bees live, to prevent smoke, wildfires and loud noises that disturb and affect the bees' livelihoods. The use of chemical pesticides is strictly prohibited in areas where bees live and in community forests.
