During the inauguration of National Road 51, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that when there were no problems, they did not talk about peace, they talked about democracy and human rights. For Cambodia, it is also about democracy and human rights, but Cambodia gives priority to peace, if there is no peace, there is nothing, there is no respect for human rights.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Now the world is shouting for peace. When there are no problems, they do not talk about peace, they talk about democracy and human rights." "For us, we are also talking about democracy and human rights, but we give priority to peace, without peace there is nothing, there is no respect for human rights until there is a violation."
The Prime Minister cited the example of the effects of the war in Ukraine as a long-term solution because of the scale of the devastation and the use of unexploded ordnance. Obviously, as in Cambodia, landmines and unexploded ordnance have not yet been destroyed.
Because of this peace, Cambodia has changed its face and developed in all areas, whether it is infrastructure, economic, trade, compensation, which is growing day by day, so the people of Cambodia must work together to maintain peace. It is difficult to find this, but not a handful of people can come and destroy it, as Samdech Techo once said.
