Peace brings national achievements to flow! This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Inaugurates National Road 51
(Phnom Penh): Mlup Sok Santepheap has given people the opportunity to live in peace and there is a growing demand. Only the road and bridge infrastructure system requires the Royal Government to be constantly built to meet the needs of the people and to promote national economic growth.
As of the end of 2021 and the beginning of 2022, the achievements of many roads and bridges have been inaugurated by the Royal Government, which is a clear demonstration of the Royal Government's high attention on the construction of infrastructure.
On the morning of Friday, March 25, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, together with the Economic Adviser of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, inaugurated National Road No. 51, an important road for the transportation of goods and People's travel by connecting between National Road 4 and National Road 5.
In 2003-2004, National Road No. 51 was already built as a two-layer paved road (DBST). During 2009, the road was badly damaged due to a sharp increase in consumption and transportation activities of all kinds, including overcrowding. Perform annual repairs and maintenance using the national budget only.
Due to the interconnection of the main road network, especially National Road No. 4 and National Road No. 5, the number of traffic and all kinds of transportation from day to day has increased significantly. It should be noted that in 2017, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to allow the repair and restoration of this road by paving with AC rubber as well as widening the width of the road.
The project has constructed 20 corner drains, 67 round drains, 97 side drains, including installation of traffic signs, traffic signs, kilometer poles and other road safety equipment.
The Senior Minister emphasized that "National Road No. 51 is another new achievement and a noble bond born of the friendship and comprehensive cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the People's Republic of China to the people." Kandal and Kampong Speu provinces, as well as people across the country for general and long-term use.
The Minister of Public Works and Transport said that under the wise leadership and clear vision of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who is a win-win political operator, a leader, a founding father and a symbol of peace, Samdech Techo has sacrificed everything. In order to bring complete peace and real political stability to the motherland of Cambodia.
The Minister continued that the peace that all Cambodians are achieving is indeed the most important foundation that has given the general opportunity for Cambodia to be able to restore and develop the country in all areas should be proud of, especially the people. People who are employed, have a job, have an income, have the right to abundance, live in prosperity and without fear, and can travel freely near and far as they wish.
