The Ministry of Health celebrates the 24th World TB Day under the theme "Investing to end the TB epidemic is saving lives"
The ceremony was presided over by Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, and was attended by Ms. Li Ailan, Director of the World Health Organization (WHO) in the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Ms. Nancy Islick, US Agency for Mission and Working Group. Too many.
Cambodia has already achieved the Millennium Development Goals related to reducing morbidity and mortality from TB four years ahead of schedule. Cambodia's success in eradicating TB is something that only a small number of countries can achieve.
In this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia still has a high rate of morbidity and mortality due to tuberculosis compared to some other countries and there are still many people who have not yet received services. This requires us to step up our efforts to further reduce the morbidity and mortality of TB in line with the Sustainable Development Goals of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the world.
