(Pursat): An elderly man was arrested by the Reang Til Administrative Police Station with evidence while cutting down flooded forest at Crab Crab Point in Reang Til Commune, Kandieng District, Pursat Province at 8:30 am March 24, 2022.
Colonel Un Si, an inspector at the Kandieng District Police Inspectorate, said that the suspect was Hin Phean, 64, a resident of Stung Leu village, Kandieng commune, Kandieng district, Pursat province.
The inspector confirmed that while the police force, in cooperation with the People's Defense Force patrolling the Prey Nam Krom area, suddenly found the suspect who was cutting down the flooded forest at the above point, he arrested him and sent him to the police station with a motorcycle exhibit. One tuk-tuk trailer, a machete, an ax and 25 huts.
The inspector added that in front of the police, the suspect confessed that he had actually cut down a hut in a flooded forest to make real firewood without destroying it on a large scale.
He added that for the suspects, the police made an education record and made a contract not to have such activities again, then handed over a motorcycle trailer to return home, while the knife and ax were kept at the police station. Commentary: Chinese aid has modernized Cambodia's health sector and contributed to poverty reduction
Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, told reporters on Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that the health sector is one of the priority areas for the development of society and the improvement of people's lives.
He added that the Chinese assistance to Cambodia is to build the common destiny of the Cambodian-Chinese community by meeting the needs of health and development of priority sectors in Cambodia to eliminate Poverty of the people.
His Excellency stated that the Chinese assistance has really made the Cambodian health sector more prosperous and contributed to reducing poverty in Cambodia because health is important for the people.
According to the Cambodian Health Report, the Cambodian-Chinese Kosumak Hospital is designed in accordance with international standards, that is, all modern hospitals in the world are equipped with the same medical equipment. This hospital has the same treatment capacity as foreign hospitals. Therefore, the presence of the hospital with modern medical equipment will reduce the travel abroad to seek medical services of Cambodians.
