(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, March 24, 2022, the Ministry of Information organized an award ceremony for 14 journalists who were evaluated as journalists who have been active in the field of information. These 14 journalists have worked in the media for five different periods: 1970, 1980, 1990, 2000 and 2010.
The 14 journalists selected for the award, including for the 1970s, include Chet Sorn, editor-in-chief of Phnom Penh Thmey newspaper and administrative director of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, and Prohm Say, editor-in-chief of Khmer Civilization.
For the 1980s, there were Teav Sarak Mony, editor-in-chief of Rasmei Kampuchea, Pech Bunra, editor-in-chief of Hang Meas TV, and Chea Sundaneth, director general of FM102.
For the 1990s, there were Soy Sopheap, director general of Deum Ampil, Moeun Chhean Narith, deputy editor-in-chief and descriptive columnist for the Khmer-Times newspaper and journalism professor at the Institute of Journalism, and Chun Sophal, reporter for Angkor Thom magazine.
For the 2010 decade, Mr. Pak Seangly, Environmental and Social Journalist at the Phnom Penh Post; Mr. Van Saray, Deputy Director of Media at Fresh News; Cambodia and Ms. Nhek Srey Leak, Editor-in-Chief of New Media 25 Capital-Provinces.
The Journalist Incentive Award is an award organized by the Ministry of Information in collaboration with Brown and New Press.
Mr. Prum Seila, a representative of the Brown Press Unit and a member of the Journalism Incentive Award, said that the selected journalists underwent a thorough review and evaluation by a five-member committee from the Ministry of Information Fresh News. Recent News and Brown News.
Mr. Seila said that the selected journalists are journalists who have created works to promote and improve the information sector. He added that the award is not only about the value of the award, but also about their work, which has contributed to the promotion of the media.
Mr. Phos Sovann, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of Information and Audiovisual, emphasized that the Journalist Incentive Award is an award commemorating the dedication of the physical and mental strength of the 14 journalists who participated in The height of the information sector in Cambodia.
Minister of Information Khieu Kanharith, who presided over the award ceremony, welcomed the increase in the first Cambodian Journalist Incentive Award. The Minister considers this program to be a good program to connect journalists from one generation to another.
The Minister encouraged the organization of this program in order to contribute to the professional development of journalists.
In this program, the Minister of Information and a well-known former journalist also gave some tips to improve the information profession in Cambodia. The Minister said that the profession of journalism in a democratic society is an important contributor to the decisions of the national leaders and the people.
The minister also pointed out that journalists are like air in a ball. Good wind makes the kick straight to the target. In this regard, the Minister wants journalists to strengthen their knowledge in order to improve their professional career as journalists.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith also reminded the media about the values of professional ethics. The minister said that ethics is an armor to protect the dignity of journalists.
Mr. Prohm Say, representing the award-winning journalists, expressed his great pleasure for organizing this event. He sees this program as an encouraging contribution for journalists.
