(Pursat): The Cambodian Red Cross provided some first aid training and skills to 25 volunteers in Bun Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province to act as a first aid agency and cooperate with officials. Authorities to assist local people in the event of an accident or disaster.
The 25 Red Cross volunteers are veterans, families and children of veterans living in Bun Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, while the total population of this newly established village is 628 families.
Not only that, there is also training in health and first aid by Mr. Tep Rom stated that this first aid is very important and the Cambodian Red Cross is very attentive to this work because when People in danger at the local level are the Red Cross volunteers who are closest to the people, so will be able to rescue them first.
Ms. Men Neary Sopheak continued that not only the training of health and first aid, the Cambodian Red Cross also inspires volunteers to help people who have a difficult situation such as people with disabilities or no children. Close to - Therefore, the Cambodian Red Cross volunteers in this village must know how to unite or work together to help the planting work or transportation of those who have a difficult situation.
Keo Srey Mom added that her husband was a fighter who had lost his life in battle and left behind three sons and daughters. Despite the hardships of supporting her family, she is still strong enough to support her family and support the villagers.
The Cambodian Red Cross branch in Pursat province plans to visit and inspect the work of volunteers in this village every two months to solve their shortcomings, for example, if they have problems and do not have the skills to solve them. The Red Cross trainers will continue to train them to develop their capacity to become quality first responders in the community.
