Indian Ambassador: Cambodia is a close friend and ready to assist the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces according to practical needs
On the morning of March 24, 2022, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), received here this morning a meeting with Dr. Dwayyani Kupragade, Ambassador of the Republic of India to Cambodia.
Dr. Dave Yanikou Bragerde thanked the Commander-in-Chief for allowing the meeting and congratulated and supported the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as the host of the 19th Meeting of the Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces. .
The Ambassador highlighted the close cooperation between the Cambodian and Indian Armed Forces, especially in the field of peacekeeping operations, and that in the future, India is ready to respond to the needs of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and request a feasibility study. In establishing the Indian Military Attachment in Cambodia.
In response, General Vong Pisen informed the Ambassador of India about the current situation in which the challenges of Kovid 19 have been alleviated and the country's economy has been reopened.
General Vong Pisen emphasized that the relief of the Kovid 19 epidemic was not accidental, but was due to the skillful leadership and change of all the current tactics of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, combined with Involvement of civil servants, citizens and support from friendly countries.
Regarding the relationship, the Commander-in-Chief highlighted the diplomatic ties between the two countries over the past 70 years, in which Indian military cooperation has provided material and financial support, especially training for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to become rich troops. Ability to complete missions under the framework of the United Nations.
