Senior official of the Ministry of Social Affairs: Human trafficking is rampant in the form of transnational crime and in organized countries
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that human trafficking has been occurring everywhere in the form of transnational and organized crime, and that this crime has had an impact. Negative to individuals, families and communities, especially at the national, regional and global levels.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has been working to develop, compile, disseminate and implement policies, strategies, plans, bilateral and multilateral agreements, and mechanisms aimed at combating and minimizing human trafficking and human trafficking. Within the national, sub-regional, regional and global framework.
He pointed out that the Ministry of Social Affairs, which has been mandated by the Royal Government to protect and provide support services to victims, the Ministry has actively worked and achieved many achievements in the protection of victims of human trafficking. Develop policies to prevent human trafficking, strengthen cooperation and enhance partnerships.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State would like to thank the leaders and professional officers of the Department of Anti-Human Trafficking and Victim Integration, relevant ministries, institutions, national and international development partners, especially Ratanak International, for their financial and technical support. Set up this procedure.
This year, the participation of the Royal Government of Cambodia, communities, youth groups, public and private institutions, international organizations, media institutions and the people of Cambodia across the country to show their activities and will to contribute to building a prosperous and prosperous future. Good health for everyone.
Miss Meas Soksophea, a famous singer in Cambodia, said: "Nature calls for us to show our will and act together. "If we do not act as a rule now, humanity, wildlife and the planet we love will suffer even more than the situation that has already happened."
"Now is the time for us to act towards building a sustainable society and planet for all," she added.
Seng Teak, Director of WWF, said: “Natural resources and ecosystems provide the foundation for sustaining human, animal and biodiversity as well as essential elements for sustainable economic development. . It is the duty of all of us to take care of the natural resources and the planet that is our common home. "Together we can build a future where people and nature can live in harmony with each other."
Sustainability is an important topic for everyone. The consequences of climate change and the loss of natural resources are affecting our lives as well as the survival of all species of animals and biodiversity on the planet. Sustainability is becoming an essential element of the standard of business operations for the private sector: business owners, entrepreneurs, employees and all customers.
Sustainability principles for business operations are a key element for long-term development. Clear priorities need to be set to ensure that human health and the importance of ecosystem quality are prioritized in global, national and institutional development plans, both public and private.
"The future of our planet depends on what we are doing today in society, and it is clear that we all have a role to play in solving the problems that humanity is facing," he said.
Young people can play an active role in protecting nature and improving our environment. Young people can adopt new ways for their daily lives to contribute to reducing the impact on the environment. They can make homes, schools and youth institutions more sustainable by embracing environmentally friendly activities, recycling some materials for reuse, as well as contributing to water and electricity savings.
"The participation of young people starts with their own youth in improving hygiene, saving water and electricity, planting trees at home and in their community," said Chin Sonita, President of Earth Youth.
"Encouraging young people to participate in protecting the environment not only helps young people change their attitudes, but it can also be a role model for family members and the community to encourage them," she said. "They have more responsibility to protect the environment and natural resources for building a better future."
Economic growth and environmental protection must go hand in hand. Protecting nature and the environment is important for social, economic and sustainable development, as it provides us with all the resources we need to produce a wide range of materials, goods and services, as well as create employment opportunities for money. Family income.
Cambodia has been making continuous efforts to protect and conserve natural resources and ensure the sustainability of the environment, the quality of the environment is ensured, and natural resources are well preserved for the benefit of mankind for generations to come. Cambodia has been implementing its long-term strategic plan to achieve carbon neutrality by 2050.
Cambodia is committed to implementing the National Forest Monitoring System and the Environmental and Social Safety Information System for the implementation of the Greenhouse Gases Reduction from Deforestation and Degradation (REDD +) project, and aims to reduce the rate of deforestation. By mid-2030, the forestry and land use (FOLU) sector is in line with Cambodia's REDD + strategy. ”
