When it comes to Ukraine war, some may immediately say that nuclear war or World War III could erupt. Such an understanding is unreasonable, as it is based on the principle of "collective security" enshrined in Article 5 of the NATO Charter, which states that an attack on a member state is tantamount to an attack on a member state. The entire military bloc will require all member states to respond.
Of course, ethically, if our allies are threatened or abused, we must come to the rescue. But friends and siblings must clearly divide the benefits. Article 5 of the NATO Charter is also linked to the national interests and the constitutions of each member state. In the United States, for example, the Constitution states that the President has no right to declare war, only Congress has the right to declare war.
For Western experts, Western leaders are considered "rational people", but for Putin, they see it differently.
Lt. Gen. Seng Thearin: The Army is proud of the next generation of leaders and supports the candidacy of Dr. Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister
(Battambang): Major General Seng Thearin, Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the 5th Military Zone, stated that the Army is proud of the leadership of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army. He added that the army is also satisfied and fully supports the election of Dr. Hun Manet as the future prime ministerial candidate.
Major General Seng Thearin said this at a seminar to summarize the results of military and security work in 2021 and the direction of implementation in 2022 of the Battambang Provincial Military Operation Area on Wednesday, March 23, 2022.
During the ceremony, Major General Seng Thearin praised and highly appreciated the soldiers of all subordinate units who have made efforts to successfully complete all tasks assigned by the leadership.
In this workshop, Lt. Gen. Seng Thearin also presented the achievements and leadership of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet to the Battambang Provincial Military Operations Force. Mr. Seng Thearin stated that Dr. HUN Manet not only had the skills to lead and manage the work of the army, but also participated in the operation of the fight against Kovid 19 with high responsibility.
Mr. Seng Thearin stated that, under the direction of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Dr. HUN Manet led the forces to set up 19 Kovid treatment centers in Phnom Penh and other provinces. The establishment of a Kovid 19 treatment facility is an urgent response in the operation of Kovid 19.
Lt. Gen. Seng Thearin said the army was proud of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, their leader. He added that the army also fully supported the election of Dr. Hun Manet as the future prime ministerial candidate.
