Meeting to review the work results for the year 2020-2021 and work directions for 2022 of the Ministry of Public Function
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 23, 2022, Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Public Administration Reform Committee, presided over the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for the year 2020-2021 and set the direction. Jobs for 2022 of the Ministry of Public Works.
Speaking at the event, Minister Prum Sokha expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the leaders and all members of the working group of the Ministry of Public Works for participating in organizing this meeting to be well and attentive. Highly strive to implement health rules in a new normal path in the context of Kovid-19 disease.
Despite the impact of the Kovid-19 outbreak, the Minister noted that in the past two years, 2020 and 2021, the public sector has achieved the following significant achievements:
1. Striving to maintain the regular functioning of civil servants contributes to the smooth operation of public administration mechanisms at all levels, especially the management of civil servants data to ensure regular payroll.
3: The practice of living and working of civil servants in the new normal path of the Kovid-19 context to participate in the national movement to fight and control Kovid-19, such as: the strict implementation of health measures "3 prevent 3 do not vaccinate" Protect everyone, volunteer to donate personal salary to the Kovid-19 Foundation, contribute to saving money and means of work, etc.
4: In addition to the core work, civil servants at all levels have worked hard to spend time outside of working hours and personal means to work on the ground to understand the actual situation and the effectiveness of public services to the people in accordance with the strategy of the fourth phase of the Royal Government.
5. Maintaining international relations, strengthening cooperation to continue to contribute to the development of institutional capacity and human resources.
These achievements can be achieved depending on the following key factors:
First, the wise direct leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the field of public functions.
Second, good cooperation from ministries and institutions at the national and sub-national levels in the management of public functions.
Third, the work ethic and responsibility of civil servants throughout the country and especially of the Ministry of Public Works, especially in the circumstances of the risk of complications caused by Kovid-19.
Along with the past achievements, Minister Prum Sokha also highlighted some challenges and tasks that need to be addressed in order to improve the quality of work management of public functions.
As a target for 2022, the Minister has identified the four priority missions to be achieved as follows:
First, effective and equitable public service to the people
Second: Strengthening the institutional capacity and quality of civil servants with professional conscience
Third, the promotion of meritocracy in public administration and
Fourth, the development and modernization of infrastructure to serve the public service sector.
