Samdech Techo Prime Minister compared the power given to the ministries and institutions like a sword when Samdech handed over the sword but refused to cut it back to Samdech as a cutter instead.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks came as a surprise to the relevant ministries and institutions, including the sub-national authorities in charge of the Tonle Sap natural resources, which have led to alarming crimes against natural resources and the destruction of fish stocks.
Speaking at the closing ceremony of the 2021 work review meeting and the 2022 work direction of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I still say the same thing when it comes to the sub-decree of any ministry. " The power for its ministry means that it takes the sword from the prime minister until the prime minister gives the sword when it is cut down and gives it back to the prime minister."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is transferring more power to the sub-national level (provincial level), so all provinces must exercise those powers responsibly. Samdech asked, "We have transferred more power to the province, but if the province does not know how to take responsibility, what to do with the power?"
Regarding the crackdown on natural resource destruction in the Tonle Sap Lake, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the relevant ministries, institutions, armed forces, the National Police and the army, as well as provincial authorities, must crack down and eliminate all fishing crimes on the Tonle Sap Lake. If the perpetrators of fishing are not cracked down, there will be no need for provincial governors, ministers, police chiefs and military officers.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I commend the efforts of the leaders of the institutions as well as the provincial authorities on the Tonle Sap Lake, led by His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, who have worked hard for the Tonle Sap. "We have been reduced to more than 60,000 hectares."
Samdech Techo further stated that regarding the issue of flooded forest land, if the state does not take measures to reclaim the land, it cannot be taken back, and even when the order is issued, it is difficult for the people, but this is It is in the national interest, and if it lasts from year to year, the Tonle Sap land will not be much left.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further stated that the issue of flooded forest land has been resolved after the government adjusted some areas on the map area 2 in Kampong Thom province, and in addition, the flooded land was transferred back to the state. More than 60,000 hectares, and these areas are targets for replanting of flooded areas.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on November 28, 2021, issued a strict order to the relevant ministries and institutions and the provincial governor of Tonle Sap Lake to prevent and crack down on illegal logging. And land grabbing along the Tonle Sap Lake, especially in Kampong Chhnang province.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also issued a decision to establish a working group to inspect and investigate the encroachment on flooded forest land in Tonle Sap area in Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom provinces immediately. .
Regarding the case of cracking down on illegal fishing, officials and authorities confirmed to Samdech Techo Hun Sen that it was not possible to catch the perpetrators of illegal fishing because there was a previous incident that made the perpetrators aware and drove the boat at high speed to escape. .
This serious reaction of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on Wednesday afternoon, March 23, 2022, on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2021 and the work direction of the new year 2022 of the Ministry. Agriculture, forestry and fishing.
In this regard, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia confirmed that the governor of Pursat province reported that he gave a name and reported to crack down on fishing offenses, but officials did not say that the perpetrators ran away. Claim that the perpetrators use the boat faster than the authorities.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if the perpetrators of this fishing crime are not completely suppressed from the Tonle Sap Lake, the future of the Tonle Sap Lake will be exhausted for fish to eat.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia underlined that the loss of flooded forest on one side, the loss of fish on the other side, now more than 60,000 hectares of flooded forest must be replanted to protect our Tonle Sap Lake, especially not to continue encroachment on forest land The Tonle Sap Lake is definitely flooded again. Samdech Tha, if not prevented in time, it is clear that the crime of encroaching on the flooded forest land around the Tonle Sap Lake will spread continuously.
At this point, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the suppression of illegal fishing, encroachment on the forest is the leading force of the provincial board of governors because all power has been handed over, so it must come forward to work to suppress these crimes without waiting. At the same time, each province must prepare its own plan to crack down on illegal fishing.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mocked officials and authorities for cracking down, but those who set small nets never cracked down on 1 ton of fishing boats. As for cracking down on the same wood, only small loggers can crack down on big timber traders.
It should be noted that regarding the crime of fishing, especially the encroachment on the flooded forest land around the Tonle Sap Lake, on November 28, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, chaired an emergency meeting to Put in place immediate preventive and repressive measures.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's order came after the Royal Academy of Cambodia, led by Dr. Sok Touch, conducted a study on the Tonle Sap Lake, which found serious problems with logging and encroachment on flooded forest land, especially in Kampong Chhnang province. That needs to be addressed and action taken immediately.
