(Phnom Penh): During his first visit to Myanmar, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, did not request to meet with Aung San Suu Kyi. However, Myanmar military leader Min Aung Lan has vowed to consider allowing the special envoy to meet with Aung San Suu Kyi in the future once the court proceedings are completed.
Speaking to reporters at Phnom Penh International Airport, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon paid a courtesy call and held talks with General Min Aung Lan on the first day of his three-day visit on 21 to 23 ago.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon claimed that during a courtesy call with General Min Ong Lang, he discussed some issues, recalling Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request. He said that Min Aung Lan's answer this time was more open.
During the meeting, Mr. Prak Sokhon replied to General Min Ong Lam, "We are here to respect ASEAN principles, which means that we will not interfere in Myanmar's internal affairs, if this is Myanmar's internal affairs, let Myanmar solve it first." "
He added: "With this, General Min Aung Lan said that in the future may consider the proposals made, not just Aung San Suu Kyi, because there are others. "Upcoming visits will be considered."
He described the military leader's promise as an opportunity to shed light on the issue of dialogue with all parties involved in the mandate of the special envoy and for the sake of national reconciliation. Participation from all parties and so on.
Since the coup on February 1, 2021, Aung San Suu Kyi, along with several politicians and officials from her party, have been detained, including one who was sentenced to death. Terrorism.
