Microfinance plays an important role in Cambodia's economic and social development
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kith Sovannarith, First Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that although Cambodia is in the context of the outbreak of Kovid 19, the microfinance sector will continue to grow and play an important role in Contribute to the restoration and development of the Cambodian economy in the context of living in a new normal path.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith made this remark while attending a dissemination workshop on "Microfinance in Cambodia" in Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province on March 23, 2022.
He attributed this achievement to the efforts of the National Bank of Cambodia under the support of the Royal Government and the cooperation of banking and financial institutions.
He stressed that although the microfinance sector has made great progress in the past, the sector still faces some major challenges that need to be addressed by all stakeholders, continuing to help promote and educate people to borrow money. From a legal institution and use the loan to target and comply with the repayment obligations.
He added that, in fact, through the dissemination workshop on the microfinance sector in Cambodia "organized to prevent people from suffering and indebtedness from exploitation by informal traders.
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said that in line with the call of the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia, the members of all 121 associations have expressed their commitment to solve problems with customers gently and win-win. Especially during difficult times due to the negative effects of Kovid 19.
He said that these financial institutions have set a common goal for their customers to succeed and continue to use financial services effectively, adhering to the principle that the success of customers is the real success of the institution. .
