This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting to review the work of the old year and raise the work direction of the new year of the Ministry of Agriculture.
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of Wednesday, March 23, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2021 and the work direction of the new year 2022 of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. And fishing.
The two-day conference reviewed and discussed vigorously the achievements and challenges of the previous year. The conference also discussed vigorously to set effective work directions for the benefit of the nation and its people.
Below are some of the work results that the Ministry has achieved in 2021.
As of 2021, the Ministry has established a total of 643 community forestry communities covering an area of 522,273 hectares, of which 536 communities on an area of 449,475 hectares have been issued. The Ministry has signed 449 community forestry agreements. Covers an area of 372 175 hectares and approved 106 community forest management plans covering an area of 72,620 hectares.
