Research: Tobacco companies continue to use illegal advertising strategies to reach young people in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): According to research conducted by researchers from Dearkin University in Australia with the Cambodian Movement for Health (CMH), a public health work organization in Cambodia, tobacco companies Continue to use illegal advertising strategies to target young people in Cambodia.
Dr. Mom Kong, executive director of the Cambodian Movement for Health, said the study showed that more than half of the samples in the study recalled tobacco companies' illegal advertising strategies in Cambodia, including: Both advertising at retail stalls and online. A representative of the tobacco company went to contact them to provide cigarettes and other free goods.
Not only that, they also mentioned illegal private advertisements in various locations in Phnom Penh, such as in cafes, restaurants, bars, even during the Royal National Festival of Cambodia.
In this study, under the Law on Tobacco Control, these tobacco advertising strategies have been banned in Cambodia since 2015, he said. On the contrary, this research provides clear evidence that tobacco companies in Cambodia continue to violate the law frequently in public places throughout Phnom Penh.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has made significant progress in reducing tobacco use. However, a 2019 UN study estimates that about 15,000 Cambodians die each year as a result of tobacco use, with an annual expenditure of about 3% of GDP. Of the annual. Studies have also shown that smoking can increase the risk of serious health problems among people with COVID-19.
To address the burden of tobacco use on the Cambodian people, the new research highlights the importance of increasing controls and enforcement, banning tobacco advertising and promotion, as well as increasing fines. For tobacco companies that continue to violate the law in Cambodia. Export of trout from Cambodia to China, officials claim to fill the gaps and wait for the final decision from the Chinese side
(Phnom Penh): After the last meeting between Cambodia and China at the end of January 2022, Cambodia is looking forward to the results from the Chinese side on the decision to export Cambodian trout to China. From Cambodia has already filled in the documents and shortcomings required by the Chinese side. This is according to Mr. Hav Viseth, Deputy Director General of Fisheries Administration, told Fresh News on March 22.
Mr. Hav Viseth said, "As for the official results on the export of Cambodian trout to China, my team and I have been waiting for a response from the Chinese side as well. The documents required by the Chinese side to improve the shortcomings of fish farms and fish processing enterprises have been completed and sent to the General Administration of Customs since the third week of February, but the results. However, that is waiting for the same.
Please be informed that the Chinese side has temporarily agreed to allow 3 fish farms and 1 fish processing facility to be able to export, but must correct the shortcomings required by the Chinese side before the two sides sign a joint protocol to Allow Cambodian trout to go to China. But now those shortcomings have been corrected and submitted to the Chinese side, waiting for a final decision.
