(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 23, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2021 work review meeting and the 2022 work direction of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
On the occasion of closing the conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a 50-minute speech, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the agricultural sector in 2021 has grown significantly, the total rice yield reached more than 12.2 million tons, an increase of 11.6% compared to 2020, the use of machinery for plowing Weed up to 99.42% and rice surplus of more than 6.94 million tons or about 4.44 million tons of rice, horticulture reached more than 4.36 million tons and industrial crops reached more than 19 million Tons.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in 2021, family and commercial animal production increased by 11.2% compared to 2020 and ensured 87% meat supply.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the value of total agricultural exports for 2021 is about 5 billion US dollars, an increase of 25% compared to agricultural exports in 2020, in which the export of rubber products. Earned more than 610 million US dollars over last year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that currently Cambodia's agricultural sector is a priority sector that ensures food security, nutrition and exports, which need to be further invested in the construction of physical infrastructure to support agriculture, irrigation, transportation and logistics, agricultural credit, research and development. Development of new varieties, promotion of modern techniques.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Instructs the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Relevant Institutions to Strive to Implement the "Agricultural Development Policy 2021-2030" Under the Coordination of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee to Transform Cambodia into Agriculture Modern, competitive, climate-resilient and sustainable environment.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed all relevant ministries and institutions to prepare an action plan to implement the "Strategic Framework and Program to Restore and Promote Cambodia's Economic Growth in Living with Kovid-19 in the New Orbit for 2021-2023".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to promote and promote the effective development of all forms of aquaculture in accordance with the "Strategic Plan for Aquaculture Development 2016-2030" to ensure the supply of local fish meat and export quality and safety. And maintain market price competition. Strengthen the capacity of fishing communities to become fisheries-free fishing communities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is necessary to strengthen the management and protection of fisheries conservation areas, to maintain the protection of flooded forests and mangrove forests, and to take transparent measures for all illegal trade in fishery resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the preparation of amendments to the Law on Fisheries must be completed to strengthen the management and implementation of the fisheries sub-sector and legal documents related to the fight against illegal fishing without reports and without permission.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wondered what the provincial governors around the Tonle Sap Lake and the relevant ministries and institutions were doing to cause the people to encroach on the Tonle Sap Lake conservation land.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praises the working group led by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara for the confiscation of the Tonle Sap Lake Conservation Land.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Ministry of Agriculture has many ministers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen issues an order to eliminate all fishing crimes on the Tonle Sap Lake.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen orders the elimination of corrupt traders in the destruction of fish on the Tonle Sap Lake.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the national television to re-broadcast Samdech's comment on the order to eliminate fishing lots.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it was not because of the reason for cracking down on fishing crimes that he did not use the excuse to create fishing lots that Samdech had canceled.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends the use of helicopters to crack down on fishing offenders.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen orders the handcuffing of fishing offenders without a policy. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the authorities can only crack down on minor crimes, but not big crimes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that forest crimes can be cracked down on, but small and large forest crimes cannot be cracked down on.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if the perpetrators of fishing were not cracked down, there would be no need for a provincial governor, a minister or a police chief or a military chief.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that many of the Royal Government's efforts were buried because of corrupt officials conspiring with the perpetrators.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to continue to strengthen and expand community forests through agro-forestry and animal husbandry systems, forest and wildlife management, forest restoration. Continuing to amend the forest law with the support of ensuring environmental sustainability in line with the principle of "green development" in response to climate change, aiming to minimize the negative impact on economic growth and social life.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to increase private sector investment in all agricultural value chains, establish agro-industrial processing zones for export, expand the implementation mechanism of "contract agricultural production" more widely.
* Samdech Techo stated that the relevant institutions, the Rural Development Bank and the Sub-National Administration of Agriculture must cooperate in providing loans to small and medium-sized agricultural processing enterprises, which the Royal Government has just announced on the use of new additional funds of 100 million US dollars.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, as the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair, led a delegation on his first three-day working visit to Myanmar from March 21 to 23, 2022, at the invitation of the Group. State Administrative Council of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon further stated that the first visit of the Special Envoy was welcomed and considered as a positive and important step in the implementation of the ASEAN Five-Point Consensus Agreement in the Agreement with the Parties. The side of the State Administrative Council also expressed a consensus.
The Deputy Prime Minister also stated that during the Special Envoy's visit to Myanmar, many important insights were gained for the process of reducing violence, the closeness of ideas and positions of stakeholders, as well as finding ways. And solutions to deliver humanitarian aid to those most in need.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon stated that the Cambodian side is still willing to help and want to meet with other parties to help solve the problem of Myanmar, but the various actors of Myanmar are not yet ready to solve this problem. No, this is the hardest part when trying to reconcile a partner who does not want to reconcile is the hardest.
The Special Envoy further stated that the great benefit of this first visit is to confirm the ASEAN expectations of the people of Myanmar and the international community and to get a lot of information that will help the plan of the envoy's next visit. Special.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon considered his first visit to Myanmar as the special envoy of the ASEAN chair should be called an "exploration visit". At the same time, he also acknowledged that what he planned in the plan and the reality of the visit was not completely successful, and this visit did not exceed expectations, but is not bad.
