Despite the obstacles and difficulties, under the clear vision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, one of Cambodia's outstanding former diplomats, the relationship between Cambodia and South Korea has improved year by year. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "This is the result of the cooperation we have received. That is the benefit of establishing diplomatic ties between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, which I myself have to strive for. "I am very proud to be the founder of the re-establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea."
So far, Cambodia and the Republic of Korea have been reunited for 25 years. Through this well-developed relationship, it has brought many benefits for the country and the people of both countries.
After the re-establishment of diplomatic ties, the trade volume between the two countries has increased more than 17 times to reach 1 billion US dollars a year, with about 300 Korean companies investing, he said. Directly in Cambodia in various sectors such as garments, finance, construction and agriculture.
He added that since the re-establishment of diplomatic relations with Korea in 1997, Korea has been implementing more than 900 cooperation projects on grants and concessional loans. Millions of dollars in areas such as infrastructure, health and education. In addition, Korea plans to implement a larger ODA project worth up to $ 150 million.
The Ambassador emphasized that the good friendly relations between Cambodia and Korea also contributed greatly to the creation of jobs and the collection of international currency for Cambodia. Through the export of labor under the current authorization system, about 45,000 Cambodian workers are working in the Korean industry honestly and have been recognized by Korean employers.
