Samdech Techo Prime Minister confirmed that the choice of location for the construction of the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Bridge is many, but there are only two good options, and Samdech decided to choose the second option.
Samdech stated that the first option is to build from Chroy Changvar across the Mekong River to Svay Chrum, if this option is used to create traffic congestion in Chroy Changvar. The second option is to build from the night market (Old Market Park) across the Tonle Sap River to Chroy Changva, then from Chroy Changva to Svay Chrum with two bridges.
Samdech Techo said that the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Bridge will be a modern bridge using cables to facilitate navigation on the two rivers, the Tonle Sap and the Mekong River, and when completed, this bridge will be able to attract both domestic and foreign tourists.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Cambodia-Korea Friendship Bridge, we built only one, but up to two bridges. In other words, we have helped solve the traffic problem of the two existing Chroy Changvar bridges. We built this bridge using high uninsulated steel ropes to facilitate waterway traffic. "I reaffirm with President Kim Jong Un and the current President of the National Assembly that we support this bridge."
He added, "I told President Mon Ji Ng that if this type of bridge grows in Cambodia, it will become something that attracts tourists, both in the city and abroad, because it is a modern bridge across the river without writing." "This is in the interest of establishing diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, and I must strive to do so."
