Kremlin accuses US of state-level theft, denying cyber-attacks
MOSCOW, March 22 (Xinhua) - The Kremlin on Tuesday rejected US warnings that it may be planning cyber-attacks in response to Western sanctions, saying Russia would not participate. In such an act of theft. This is according to the release by Reuters on Tuesday, March 22, 2022.
Russia denied similar allegations in February, when the United States blamed Russia for hacking into the websites of Ukrainian banks and governments.
US President Joe Biden on Monday told businesses to make sure their digital doors were closed to protect themselves against possible cyber-attacks by Russia.
Mr. Pan Sosak and Mr. Osman Hassan chaired a meeting of the Cambodian Halal Product Inspection Committee
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 22, 2022, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, Chairman of the Cambodian Halal Product Inspection Committee, and Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Mission and Vice Chairman of the Cambodian Halal Product Inspection Committee. Led the Cambodian Halal Product Inspection Committee and the Halal Product Expert Group on the progress of the Cambodian Halal Inspection Committee at the Ministry of Commerce.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that halal products play an important role not only for Muslims but also for the global market, both Muslims and non-Muslims.
He added that in the past, members of the CPPCC And halal product specialists regularly meet with developed countries in the field of halal, such as the 57-member OIC, which has a population of over 2 billion. Cambodian Halal Product Standards and International Recognition for Cambodia's National Halal Brands.
He also said that recently, some developed countries in the field of halal intend to invest in the field of halal Cambodia, hoping that Cambodia will establish a special economic zone for the production of halal products to serve the world market in the future. The future, too.
At the same time, he mentioned the growth of Cambodian enterprises applying for Cambodian halal certification because halal labels can help increase sales and exports of those halal products to domestic and international markets such as Thailand and Malaysia. Bringing a large number of their products to the world market and contributing a large part of their national economic growth.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak stated that halal products mean "clean and hygienic" and this halal sector is taken care of and promoted by the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the whole world. He added that the government has authorized the establishment of the Cambodian Halal Institution in order to raise food standards for the benefit of Muslims, as well as for non-Muslims, both in Cambodia and around the world.
He asked the members of the CPPCC Make every effort to ensure the use of the Cambodian halal logo, which is recognized by the Royal Government to ensure the quality standards of halal products and enhance the image of Cambodia.
