NEC Holds Public Hearing on Candlelight Party Candidates in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang
The hearing took place on the morning of Tuesday, March 22, 2022 at the NEC Press Conference Hall by the nine-member NEC Trial Chamber, chaired by NEC Chairman Prach Chan and Chairman of the Trial Chamber of the NEC. This public hearing is to resolve the complaint No. 051 in which the people rejected the list of candidates of the Candlelight Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
According to the NEC press release, after reviewing and considering all the facts and the law, the Trial Chamber of the NEC believes that based on Article 42 of the Law on Commune Council Election. Sangkats and points 6.6.3.5 of the Rules and Procedures for the Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate 2022, the CV and the declaration of approval of the candidates must be filled in by each candidate.
The decision of the Trial Chamber of the NEC was made public in front of the parties and their lawyers as a final decision to close the way for protests.
Dr. Kouch Mengly: Legalization of kidney transplantation is a good thing because going abroad for a kidney transplant costs a lot of money
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has instructed the Ministry of Health to study the possibility of kidney transplants in the country, but the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia does not allow the trafficking of kidneys.
After the announcement, Samdech Techo Prime Minister Dr. Kouch Mengly, a public health expert, praised and supported this announcement. He said that legalizing kidney transplants in Cambodia is a good thing because going abroad for a kidney transplant costs a lot of money.
Dr. Kouch Mengly said that in addition to the high cost of surgery, Cambodians who go abroad for kidney transplants also pay for travel and accommodation in other countries. This is for those who lack the ability to change.
He added that a kidney transplant is not a kidney transplant, but simply a new kidney is implanted from below to make it work to replace a damaged kidney, while in Cambodia there are many people who have the ability to perform kidney and organ transplants. .
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, some people have broken their kidneys and need to go abroad for kidney transplants, but since 2010, Cambodia has been able to do so at Preah Keto Mealea Hospital. Soldier] but just no publicity.
Speaking on the occasion of the inauguration of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Preah Kosomak on March 21, 2021, Samdech Techo added that Samdech used to provide financial support to more than 10 people with health problems who need to go for organ transplants abroad. And because they are healthy again.
Although Samdech ordered the Minister of Health to study the possibility of allowing legal kidney transplants, but Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, did not allow trafficking to be obtained from the families of patients or volunteers. .
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister at the newly inaugurated Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital, Preah Kosomak has the ability to perform kidney and liver transplants, as well as some other limbs.
Dr. Kouch Mengly also expressed support for the Royal Government, which wants to see kidney surgery performed under the strictest rules. He said kidney and organ transplants were also allowed by international law.
"Abroad, there are cases of illegal kidney and organ trafficking through kidnapping, and some poor people are willing to sell their kidneys for money," he added. This is because the law enforcement is still loose.
(Phnom Penh): The installation of "QR Code" on license plates has greatly contributed to eliminating the use of fake license plates or incorrect license plates, increasing state revenue and contributing to the search for tax evaded vehicles. .
The use of fake license plates makes it difficult for the state to control vehicles, loses national revenue, and also makes it easier for criminals to cause insecurity in society. To eliminate the problem of using fake license plates or flying horse license plates, which is also a growing problem in Cambodian society, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has also devised ways to close this problem.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the Minister who has linked the leadership and management of the Ministry with the digital system in the age of modern technology, has used this technology to solve many complex problems within the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, such as providing vehicle registration services. Provide and renew driver's license.
The prominent minister in service and management reform linked to the technology system also devised strategies to eliminate the use of fake license plates or flying horse license plates. Finally, in July 2017, the "QR Code" system was also installed on the license plate of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
On the morning of Tuesday, March 22, 2022, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, together with General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, led a traffic police force to search for fake license plates on vehicles traveling on National Road No. 1.
Traffic police were deployed and asked for the cooperation of car owners to check the license plates. The specialized police force used the phones connected to the system provided by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to scan each license plate to verify the accuracy between the vehicle and the license plate.
Many cars were called by the traffic police to check, but they did not find any cars with fake license plates or the wrong car. During the operation, a car was found to have a different color of the sticker than the registered vehicle. Sealing or spraying paint different from the original color of the registered vehicle is an act prohibited by law.
General Him Yan said that since the Ministry of Public Works and Transport introduced strict measures on vehicle control by installing QR Codes on vehicles, the use of fake license plates has been reduced to a minimum. Not only that, this system also helps the police force to manage traffic safety, maintain security, order and fight against other crimes.
"This system has helped us to control the vehicles," said General Him Yan. "We can control vehicles, we can control safety, security issues, both security and traffic issues."
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol pointed out that the use of QR Code on the license plate has helped reduce the forgery of license plates, help customs authorities find tax evading vehicles and also contribute to the collection of revenue for the state.
Separately, the Sub-Decree on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Road Traffic Law stipulates that the use of license plates on other vehicles that are not registered together is illegal, and the use of cars with Scotch or change the color is different. Original colors registered with the Ministry are also illegal.
In the sub-decree, it is stated that the person who uses the license plate of a vehicle that is different from the original one or deletes the license plate or breaks the license plate, loses the license plate or puts other materials or objects to hide the license plate is fined 120,000 Riels. Anyone who changes the color of the vehicle without permission or closes the color incorrectly according to the vehicle identification card will also be fined 120,000 Riels.
For Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, until now, the use of fake license plates has not been completely eliminated. The senior minister called on all car users to obey the law and use license plates properly.
General Him Yan claimed that the police force continued to act like rain, raiding the streets to find fake license plates.
