(Kandal): The Phnom Penh Autonomous Port on Tuesday morning, March 22, 2022, opened the construction site of cold storage to support the export and import of goods that need cooling.
The groundbreaking ceremony was presided over by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol considers that the cold storage warehouse at LM17 container terminal in Kandal Leu village, Banteay Dek commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province will contribute to supporting Cambodia's growing export and import sector through the terminal transfer service. And international standard refrigeration warehouses.
The senior minister added that the cold storage water warehouse will provide more than 36,000 cubic meters of cold storage space, which can fill the current shortage of more than 25 percent to meet the growing market demand for farmers. Cambodia and local farmers, agribusiness companies, food processing companies, pharmaceutical companies, retail companies, as well as hotels and restaurants.
Mr. Her Bavy, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port, stated that the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port has decided to cooperate with Khmer Colchen Co., Ltd. to build this cold storage warehouse, believing that the company's project will benefit Phnom Penh Autonomous Port, especially to the economic growth of Cambodia by contributing to the development of the logistics sector in Cambodia.
In addition, the growth of transit goods is also gaining momentum through the provision of cold storage services for both export and import goods such as fish, meat, agricultural products, pharmaceuticals, cosmetics and more. This project will help create more jobs and improve the living standards of the people in this area.
He Bavy hopes that this investment project will provide more benefits to investors, traders, businessmen and the general public who wish to use the company's services to facilitate the export and import of goods between Cambodia and the world.
