(Phnom Penh): The Department of Environment of Phnom Penh Capital Hall held a training course on reducing plastic waste by implementing strategy (4R) to disseminate to students and youth 4A + 4 in the morning of March 22, 2022 at the building. Royal University of Phnom Penh.
The training was conducted in the presence of Mr. Kith Chankrisna, Director of Marine Plastic Waste Reduction Project, Mr. Kien Tak, Associate University of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, Mr. Keat Rainsy, Director of the Department of Environment, Phnom Penh and more than 200 students. People and relevant officials.
In addition, Mr. Keat Rasey would like to call on students as well as people to reduce the use of plastic for a clean environment.
According to Mr. Kien Tak, all students on the campus of the Royal University of Phnom Penh have placed a lot of trash cans. Good hygiene.
On this occasion, Mr. Kith Chankrisna said that in Cambodia today, more than 10 million plastic bags are used per day, and one plastic bag is not easily dissolved, it is used for 300 to 500 years.
He also called on all citizens, students to participate in the proper storage of garbage. Garbage is a challenge, so call on all citizens to reduce their use of plastic.
At the same time, Mr. Kith Chankrisna reminded all people to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 disease, the new type of omega and the implementation of "3 do not and 3 prevent" measures. Obstacles can not stop the progress of Angkor Hospital for Children
