Tbong Khmum Provincial Election Commission Holds a Meeting to Disseminate Procedures for Commune / Sangkat Council Elections of the 5th Mandate
(Tbong Khmum): Before the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 is approaching, on the morning of March 21, 2022, Tbong Khmum Provincial Election Commission held a meeting on draw to determine the order. Numbering the list of candidates to be put on the ballot, the placement of agents of political parties, election observation and distribution of voter information cards for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Keng Bonna, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, Mr. Sok Chhin, Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Election Commission and Mr. Heang Sophal, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Election Secretariat.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Sok Chhin said that all political parties that have to compete for Commune / Sangkat Councilors must come and fill out the required documents in accordance with the law, in which all candidates must fill out a resume in writing. Hand because all candidates must at least know how to read and write Khmer clearly.
On that occasion, Mr. Keng Bunna, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, stated that Tbong Khmum Province has 11 political parties running for election, while 59 communes and political parties have already drawn the numbers for the remaining communes / sangkats. Numbering for the upcoming election.
Mr. Keng Bunna commended the Tbong Khmum Provincial Election Committee for its good conduct in conducting election procedures for all political parties to run for office, campaigning, tagging and arrests. Lottery to determine the number of communes in Tbong Khmum province and some other work, although there are a few problems, but also solved smoothly.
In addition, he also advised all political parties to comply with the procedures and the NEC. Separately, local authorities, especially in communes / sangkats, must take turns to provide public services to the people in a timely manner and, moreover, to ensure that the election process is completed smoothly and in accordance with the election law.
Please be informed that the Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate 2022 will be held on June 5, 2022, in which for the Commune / Sangkat in Tbong Khmum Province, there are 64 candidates and representatives of political parties. 11 parties.
ARDB State Bank launches $ 50 million special financing program to support vegetable, fruit, animal husbandry, aquaculture and agricultural processing
(Kampong Thom): Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (ARDB), on March 21, 2022, began to disseminate the Royal Government's special financing project of $ 50 million to support Growing vegetables, fruits, animal husbandry, aquaculture, processing of agricultural products, lentils, Pailin, mango and cashew.
The launch of the second phase of the Royal Government's Special Financing Project will take place in the provinces around Tonle Sap Lake, Preah Vihear and Oddar Meanchey provinces, and Kampong Thom province will be the first province to launch the project.
During the meeting held at Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Agriculture, Dr. Kao Thach explained to the farmers about the purpose and objectives of the second phase of the Special Government Financing Project through the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank.
At the same time, Dr. also mentioned the credit policy in this special financing project, in which the interest rate is only 5.5% per annum for investment capital and 5% per annum for working capital. In particular, collateral is highly flexible and can provide credit up to 80% of collateral.
Dr. asked the farmers to use the capital received from the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture to target and know how to find information about the market and produce to target and market demand.
The Royal Government always pays close attention to the lives of farmers. At the same time, the agricultural sector is a priority in the context of Kovid 19, so Dr. encourages farmers to form a community and produce under agricultural contracts to ensure the supply of market access and profit.
He advised the farmers to cultivate according to the Food Safety Principles (GAP) and compile a safe vegetable production block by planting in a net house if possible because it is very productive.
On that occasion, Dr. Kao Thach presented souvenirs to 5 model farmers who received credit under the special program of the Royal Government, in which each received 1 mobile phone and provided funds for each participant. 20,000 riels as well.
