(Banteay Meanchey): An AK rifle with eight bullets left over from the war was found by two elderly men and handed over to the village chief. This happened at Reaksmey Meanchey village, Toul Pong commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province.
According to the police, the two men who picked up the gun were named Som Lean, a 44-year-old man living in Reaksmey Meanchey village, Toul Pong commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province, and Ming Chhin Pros, a 57-year-old man living in Reaksmey Meanchey village, Toul Pong district. Malai, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Prior to the incident, the two went to pay for fishing nets on the border of O'Chrov and Malai districts, Banteay Meanchey province. Arriving at the stream, the two of them laid down their nets for a while and then set up the nets to find fish in the nets at that time. While preparing the net, they found an AK-47 rifle made in 1965 with a number of eight bullets.
Authorities said that after seeing the gun, the two called to tell the village chief Reaksmey Meanchey. At that time, the village chief arrived at the stream and took the gun home and handed it over to the authorities to prevent any incident. Thai rice exports expected to exceed 8 million tonnes this year
BANGKOK: Thailand's rice exports are expected to top 8 million tonnes this year, driven by a weaker baht and rising demand in global markets. According to the Bangkok Post.
Rapid aging of Thais affects economic growth
