This statement by Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made during the ceremony to announce and officially launch the National Program for Democratic Development at the Sub-National Level 2 (2021-2030) on the 21st March 2022 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the decentralization and deconcentration reform is to strengthen good governance, which is the core of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy for the past three mandates to reorganize the public administration structure and management system at the level of Sub-national, based on the principles of democratic development.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highly appreciated the leaders and civil servants of ministries, sub-national administrations, development partners and civil society organizations who have worked hard to implement the decentralization and deconcentration reform process and other important reforms. Of the Royal Government has achieved continuous success.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia said this on the afternoon of Monday, March 21, 2022, on the occasion of presiding over the launching ceremony and implementation of the National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development, Phase 2, 2021 to 2030, abbreviated as "KC II".
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that the success of controlling the Kovid 19 epidemic was due to the transfer of roles and powers to the sub-national level.
"At the grassroots level, there is a huge increase in jobs and the two years of successful experience in the fight against Kovid is the success of the division of labor and the transfer of more power to "Basics."
Such assessment was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the launching ceremony and implementation of the National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development, Phase 2, 2021 to 2030, called "NEC Second "on the afternoon of Monday, March 21, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "On behalf of the Royal Government, I would like to express my appreciation and appreciation to the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD) for completing "The role of leading and coordinating the overall work of the decentralization and deconcentration reform program has been a proud achievement."
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highly appreciates the leaders and civil servants of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, development partners and civil society organizations who have participated in the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration reforms and other important reform programs. The Royal Government has achieved success in a row.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decentralization and deconcentration reform is to strengthen good governance, which is at the core of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy for the past three terms to reorganize the public administration structure and management system. At the sub-national level, based on the principles of democratic development.
In this ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has now gained enough experience to continue the deepening reform of the sub-national administration to contribute to the national economic recovery after the Kovid 19 crisis with the agenda of social development. National economy until 2030.
Therefore, in order to achieve the planned goals and ensure the implementation of the National Program for Democratic Development at the Sub-National Phase II, on behalf of the Royal Government, please provide the following recommendations:
* First, to continue to improve the efficiency and sustainability of the management of the reform work must continue to clearly define the roles, powers and responsibilities for the provision of public services that have been transferred from the national ministries to the administration. Sub-national level, especially between each level of administration to develop policies and services in each sector.
* Second: To further strengthen the sub-national administrative institutions, to further strengthen the sub-national administrative institutions through the reorganization of the structure and management system of each sub-national administration to provide timely services. Population and local economic development based on the potential of each locality, efficiency, transparency, accountability, competition and social equity.
The Phnom Penh Capital Administration must organize its management structure and functions in accordance with the characteristics of a large city, universally called Metropolitan City, in order to ensure that all challenges are met in line with population growth and urban services.
For the system of governance of sub-national administrations, the council, which is the first body, shall be formed by election to represent the voice and interests of the people within the jurisdiction of each sub-national administration and have a decision-making role in The framework of authority determined by law to meet the needs of the people in the jurisdiction and can also monitor the performance of the Board of Governors in the implementation of its decisions.
The second body is the Board of Governors, which is appointed by the national level to work with the Council of Sub-National Administration to manage the day-to-day affairs, to implement the council's decisions, and to represent the Royal Government and Ministries and institutions involved in security, public order and law enforcement in their jurisdiction.
* Fourth, the financial resources of the sub-national administration must continue to strengthen the management of revenue collection with transparent expenditure management. All institutions, both national and sub-national, need to reduce unnecessary spending, including unnecessary public investment projects, to ensure the stability of the national budget, which is struggling with Kovid-19.
Capital-provincial tax branches must work closely with each capital-provincial administration to collect various tax revenues. At the same time, it is necessary to strengthen the audit of financial inspections to ensure that the financial resources of the sub-national administration are managed, managed and used in accordance with the laws and regulations.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Monday afternoon, March 21, 2022, presided over the launching ceremony of the second phase of the National Program for Democratic Development at the Sub-National Level. 2021 to 2030, abbreviated as "KC II".
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen gave a speech for about 30 minutes, the following are the main remarks of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the leaders and civil servants of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, development partners and civil society organizations who have participated in the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration reforms and other important reform programs of the Royal Government. Successively continued.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decentralization and deconcentration reform is to strengthen good governance, which is at the core of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy for the past three terms to reorganize the structure and administrative system of democracy in Sub-national level, second phase.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there should be a clear division of roles, authority and responsibility for the provision of public services, which are transferred from national ministries and institutions to sub-national administrations, especially between each level of administration. To develop policies and services in each sector.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the NCDD must continue to strengthen its implementation in line with other key reform programs and must coordinate with relevant ministries and institutions to review and revise laws and regulations. Relevant to the policies and developments of decentralization and deconcentration reforms.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the NCDD needs to study appropriate options for establishing specific institutional mechanisms at the national level, which are permanent mechanisms to ensure effective leadership, coordination, and monitoring of sub-national administrations. In accordance with the laws and regulations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the success of controlling the Kovid 19 epidemic was due to the transfer of roles and powers to the sub-national level.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is necessary to further strengthen the sub-national administrative institutions by reorganizing the functions, structure and management system of each sub-national administration to provide timely services to the people and development. The local economy is based on the potential of each base to be effective, transparent, accountable, competitive and socially equitable.
* Samdech Techo stated that on behalf of the Royal Government, he would like to express his appreciation and appreciation to the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD) for its leadership and coordination role. In general, the decentralization and deconcentration reform programs have achieved proud results.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration must organize its management structure and functions in accordance with the characteristics of a large city, universally called Metropolitan City, to ensure that all challenges are met in line with population growth. People and city services.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is necessary to continue to promote the preparation and implementation of information technology systems and digital governance systems in each sub-national administration to improve the efficiency of internal administration, sub-national administration and communication. With the people and ensure the provision of public services to the people quickly, timely and transparent.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the leaders and civil servants of ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, development partners and civil society organizations who have worked hard to participate in the implementation of the decentralization and deconcentration reform process and other important reforms of the Royal Government. Achieve continuous success.
* Samdech Techo calls on relevant ministries and institutions at both the national and sub-national levels, development partners, civil society organizations, the private sector and all stakeholders to continue to provide support and cooperation with a high sense of responsibility to promote social development. The national economy improves the living conditions of Cambodian families, both now and in the future.
