(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee in collaboration with the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (OHCHR) on March 21, 2022, organized the 6th Consultative Workshop on the Draft Law on "Organization and functioning of the National Committee for Human Rights of Cambodia."
On that occasion, Mr. Keo Remy stated that with the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia on the field of human rights, the CCHR was allowed to Make this draft law.
He also asked all participants to comment on the key input so that the working group could be included in the draft law. The purpose of this consultation workshop was to collect input from representatives of people with disabilities in the Kingdom of Cambodia to ensure transparency and participation from all stakeholders.
He said that a series of consultations to make the draft law when it is released to be transparent and accepted by all institutions. As Cambodia raises this national human rights body, it will no longer have to ride a horse, but will be assessed by the Association of National Human Rights Institutions, and if it is evaluated well, it will be based on the Paris Principles, referring to pluralism.
Mr. Keo Remy confirmed that this is the sixth time that the CHRC has consulted with local and institutional consultants, and will have visited the grassroots to meet with people in the provinces, including non-political parties. Seats in the National Assembly to receive views, opinions and other input to make this draft law better.
Mr. Chet Chealy stated that the preparation of this draft law aims to establish the National Committee for Human Rights of Cambodia, which is an independent and neutral national body to work in the field of human rights.
Hong Kong to lift flight bans from nine countries in April and cut transit time (Video inside) (Hong Kong): The Hong Kong government said on Monday that Hong Kong will resume international flights from the United States. Britain and seven other countries also announced the easing of restrictions on Kovid 19 protection measures. This is according to the publication of CNA on March 21, 2022.
The length of the visa period on foreign passengers will also be reduced to seven days, while the previously imposed flight ban will be lifted from April 1. Continue.
Hong Kong has imposed an international flight ban since the outbreak in early January this year on nine high-risk countries, including the United States, Australia, Britain, Canada, France and the United States. India, Pakistan, the Philippines and later Nepal.
It should be noted that the principle of laxation at the hotel, which is currently 14 days, will be reduced to 7 days if their test results are negative on the 6th and 7th. After that, they are allowed to monitor their health at home or at their own place for another 7 days. The school will also reopen to students from April 19.
Social security gaps will be eased in stages starting on April 21. The restaurant will be open after 6pm, while public gatherings can accommodate four people, up from two previously. Clubs, bars and beaches will be allowed to open in the second phase, when people can walk out without a mask, while today everyone in Hong Kong has to wear a mask.
