Ministry of Labor Announces Progress of Joint Labor Dispute Resolution at NagaWorld on March 21
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 21, 2022, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training continued to chair the 4th Labor Dispute Resolution Meeting between Former Employees and NagaWorld Company, which was chaired by Mr. Tes Rukhaphal. Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the DAC With representatives of the workers and employers as well.
1: Ask to bring the point of claim back to work before discussing other points of dispute by asking the employer to provide a response to this demand. If the employer does not agree to discuss this, it will lead to further stalemate.
2: So far, there are about 200 workers who continue to demand to return to work.
3. So far, about 300 working workers have agreed to resign in exchange for about 200 workers demanding their return to work. This option allows employers to complete their layoffs and allow workers who want to return to work to return to work. Therefore, ask the employer to consider the option of exchanging workers.
4. It is unfortunate that the employer does not discuss the options of the exchange settlement. Workers' representatives will continue to submit this request in writing to the employer for further answers.
5. If the employer does not have a solution to the exchange request, the workers' representatives will not be able to attend the next meeting.
Representatives of NagaWorld:
1: Propose to raise the third and fourth points of dispute of Arbitration Order No. 012/21 dated 10 September 2021 to discuss in advance that it will provide more benefits to most employees than the first point involved Only a small group of staff. However, if the workers' representatives continue to raise the first point of dispute before the employer agrees to discuss.
2. In the internal restructuring project, the company has checked many conditions and specific, and the company uses its discretion to decide by going through legal consultation. As for the workers' representatives, it means that the unions want to be responsible for running the business on behalf of the company.
4: The choice of exchange between workers who want to resign from work and workers who want to return to work, the employer will not consider.
After a lively discussion and presentation of legal aspects related to the payment of severance pay of the Labor Inspector, the two sides agreed to schedule the next meeting on Wednesday, March 23, 2022 at 14:00. : 30 minutes.
Although no agreement has been reached, the Ministry of Labor will continue to coordinate and set the date for the next meeting in accordance with the role set by law as well as the demands of the parties.
Once again, the Ministry requested the two sides to have a high level of mutual understanding in resolving this labor dispute, to continue to work closely with the competent authorities and relevant parties peacefully and to maintain security and public order. According to the legal procedure, if the negotiations still can not be resolved, the next procedure is that both parties can file a complaint to the court to find a final solution.
