Economy Minister Concerned over Russia-Ukraine war, rising oil prices could have a negative impact on Cambodia's economy and garment exports
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, said that the Russia-Ukraine war and the rise in oil prices could affect the growth of the garment sector by reducing demand. Orders for Cambodian products that depend on exports to international markets, although the garment sector has shown positive signs of recovery.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said this at the launching ceremony of the "Development Strategy for the Garment, Footwear and Bag Production of Cambodia 2022-2027" on March 21, 2022 via video.
He said that according to the latest assessment of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the garment sector could achieve a good growth rate of 8% in 2021 from a decline of -4.4% in 2020 and is expected to achieve growth. At 8.1% in 2022, reflected by the increase in external demand, especially in the US market, coupled with the reversal of orders from Vietnam and Myanmar in the near future.
On March 21, Duke Ly Khun Thai, honorary president of the Footwear and Travel Products Association, told Fresh News that the war between Russia and Ukraine would increase the import of raw materials for production, which would make it more expensive. To affect the cost of production leading to order disruption.
"It could be that they would be able to reduce orders if oil and raw materials went up," he said. "The buyer puts it at the same price, the factory can not sell it to him, so the order will be stuck."
Duke Sang Kong, president of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, said that improving international trade facilitation and reducing logistics costs were indispensable in reducing business costs.
He said that according to the study, Cambodia's logistics costs are higher than many countries in the region, especially Vietnam. Currently, Cambodia has more than 1,200 garment factories and employs about 800,000 workers. This is according to the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
According to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, Cambodia's garment exports in 2021 will be worth 11,389.6 million US dollars, an increase of about 1505 million US dollars, equivalent to 15.2% compared to 2020. .
