In a joint conference after meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the night of March 20, 2022, Mr. Ky Sida said that the spirit of peace that the people of Cambodia adhere to is an example that the world should learn from this spirit.
"Every time I visit Cambodia, I think of the value of peace," he said. I would like to express my respect for the Cambodian people for the spirit of not giving up until the country is rebuilt from the devastation caused by the civil war. "We should learn from the Cambodian spirit because in today's world there is a threat to the peaceful lives of the people."
Cambodia suffered the most devastating aftermath of the March 18, 1970 coup. Even more tragic, the Democratic Kampuchea regime, known as the Khmer Rouge regime, wreaked havoc on the lives of the Cambodian people.
Although the regime was overthrown on January 7, 1979, the flames of war did not go out. Cambodia had to wait until the end of 1998 for the flames of war to be completely extinguished, bringing about national unity, territorial unity after the win-win policy set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the national leader.
The Royal Government, led by Samdech Techo and Cambodian dignitaries, as well as the Cambodian people, has worked hard to build Cambodian society from the flames of war to its current prosperity. Japan is an important country that has provided cooperation in all fields to rebuild Cambodian society.
In an important working meeting on March 20, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also shared some views with Mr. Ky Sida regarding the value of peace. Samdech Techo, the leader who is named as the founder of peace in Cambodia, confirmed that Samdech informed Mr. Kishida that in order to find peace, it is not possible to use war to put out the flames of war.
Under the shadow of peace prevailing in Cambodia, Kishida expressed high hopes for Cambodia's economic growth. He announced that Japan will continue to help boost investment through supply chain strengthening programs and smart Cambodian human resource training programs to become high-level industrial human resources.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on March 21, 2022 announced the official implementation of the "Cambodia Garment and Footwear Development Strategy 2022-2027" to promote the development of the garment sector in Cambodia. It ranks first and contributes about 70% of Cambodia's exports.
In the "Cambodia Garment, Footwear and Bag Development Strategy 2022-2027", the Royal Government has set out five strategic measures to support the achievement of the objectives and vision set by the Royal Government and address the challenges. Of Cambodia.
The five measures include:
1: Continue to strengthen human resources to increase productivity and increase career paths for workers 2: Continue to improve working conditions and welfare of workers and employees 3: Promote domestic and foreign investment in high value-added industries and Focus on high-value and unique products 4: Attract investment in the link industry and 5: Promote market diversification for garment and footwear exports.
He said that the Ministry of Commerce is ready to cooperate to implement this strategy effectively to promote domestic investment and promote the garment, footwear and bag manufacturing sector in Cambodia, so that this sector can add Add value to the local value chain more and especially to develop the skills of our workers better.
The Ministry of Commerce will also cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions in formulating policies that respond to new issues and address the requirements of buyers or importers regarding labor standards, environmental issues, and consumption. Renewable energy, etc. aims to maintain the market and help make the Cambodian economy resilient and sustainable development.
