The director of the department confirmed that out of 234 vehicles inspected by the team, 3 vehicles were found to have broken cages, 10 vehicles were transported with non-technical specifications, 27 vehicles were missing documents, and the number of rear axles was removed. 05 units, 6 fake driver's license documents and license plates and 8 wrong driving licenses.
