Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Two Great Achievements from Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, presides over here this morning the launching ceremony of the National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development Phase II. 2 (2021-2030).
Through the first phase so far, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng highlighted that the two major achievements that Cambodia has achieved in response to the vision of decentralization and deconcentration reform, including:
* First, based on the political consensus, we have organized direct and indirect elections in accordance with the principles of multi-party liberal democracy to establish a regular council at all levels of sub-national administration according to the mandate. Defined in the law on the election of each council.
Commune / Sangkat Funds Municipal / District Funds are also established and transferred to those administrations for management, administration and use under their sole discretion to support operations in the provision of services and implementation of local development projects within the framework of Its general mandate and conditional financial resources are also gradually transferred to the sub-national administration in accordance with the functions transferred to it.
The restructuring of the management system of sub-national administrations has changed the accountability that each sub-national administration must be primarily accountable to and directly to the people within its jurisdiction and accountable to the Royal Government and institutions. National on compliance with the Constitution, laws and regulations.
* Second, we have achieved the improvement of the efficiency and quality of public service delivery and local economic development through the gradual transfer of functions and resources in priority areas to sub-national administrations. In the past, 20 ministries and institutions in various priority sectors have participated in the process of transferring functions and resources to sub-national administrations at each stage.
Through the transfer of functions, coupled with the authority and resources, including financial resources, assets and human resources, to the sub-national administration, the sub-national administration has gradually become a competent and capable institution in Responsible for organizing, managing and managing the provision of public services and the implementation of development projects to serve the interests of the people according to the actual needs of each locality.
Based on the great achievements of the past, it is clear that the determination of a clear vision and the concerted efforts of the Royal Government for decentralization and deconcentration reform is the right decision. For the past two decades, there has been a steady improvement in the provision of public services, local economic development and effective participation in poverty reduction.
