Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Ministry of Health to consider legalizing kidney transplants in the country but not to allow trafficking (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of the 21st In March 2022, the Ministry of Health was instructed to study the possibility of legal kidney transplants in the country, as Cambodia has the capacity to make the transplant legal.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that some people had broken kidneys and needed to go abroad for kidney transplants, but since 2010, Cambodia has been able to do so at Preah Keto Mealea Hospital . Possibility to exchange, but just no advertising.
The speech of Samdech Techo Prime Minister was made on the occasion of the inauguration of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosomak (Monk Doctor) which was built and equipped with a budget of more than 80 million US dollars as a government grant. China.
Samdech said, "Some of our people have gone abroad, which costs a lot of money. I do not know what we should do about this in the future, because if we do not change, he will change." "Abroad, should we solve this problem in our country by giving the possibility to become legal, please consider this issue."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Samdech has provided financial support to about 10 people with health problems who need to go abroad for organ transplants, as they have improved their health.
Please be informed that Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosomak is equipped with modern medical equipment and has beds for up to 400 patients. Prof. Dr. Tan Sokun, Director of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Preah Kosomak, said that the hospital has nine operating rooms and is capable of orthopedic surgery, head transplantation, kidney transplantation, heart surgery, lung surgery and can change organs such as the kidneys and liver. Original.
