The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said that within the framework of ASEAN-Japan, Samdech reaffirmed his support for the ASEAN-Japan Summit for the 50th Anniversary of ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation in Japan. 2023.
The Prime Minister further stated that "His Excellency Ky Sida and I also confirmed that we will work closely to take ASEAN-Japan relations to the next level at the ASEAN-Japan Memorial Summit."
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in addition to bilateral cooperation, the two Prime Ministers also exchanged views on promoting the existing good cooperation between the two countries in the multilateral framework and on regional and international issues.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia also thanked the Prime Minister of Japan for supporting Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN this year and reaffirmed the cooperation for the success of this chair.
The proposal was made during a joint conference between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Japanese Prime Minister Kishida Fermio, which was held at the Peace Palace in Cambodia on the night of March 20, 2022, after the meeting between the two leaders. .
"In order to further promote economic cooperation, including the expansion of bilateral trade and increase Japanese investment in Cambodia, I have asked the Prime Minister of Japan, Kishida Fermio, to help buy Cambodian products, especially agricultural products," he said. "Cambodia's priorities to do more."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks were met with a positive response from Mr. Ky Sida to the new Cambodian Investment Law and agreed to further expand Cambodia's investment climate through bilateral investment agreements and public-private sector meetings.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Mr. Kishida Fermio and Samdech were happy even though during the Kovid-19 crisis, the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan remained close to nearly 2 billion US dollars. Japanese investors in Cambodia rebounded in 2021 after a sharp decline in 2020.
Cambodia is Japan's eighth largest trading partner in ASEAN. In 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan will reach about 1.7 billion US dollars.
Cambodia's exports to Japan include clothing, footwear, furniture, cosmetics, paper, stationery, leather, animals, metals, and more.
In particular, the goods that Cambodia imports from Japan include: machinery, cars, meat, electrical appliances, furniture, paper, cotton, fabrics, all kinds of plastic products, sports equipment, all kinds of spare parts and so on.
This request was made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen when the Prime Minister of Japan paid an official visit to Cambodia at the invitation of Samdech. He will pay a two-day visit to Cambodia.
After the bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said in a joint press conference, "I also asked Japan to increase the quota for accepting Cambodian trainees and skilled workers. "His Excellency the Prime Minister of Japan hopes that when the situation of Kovid disease improves, more skilled workers and interns will continue."
In addition, the joint statement also stated that the two Prime Ministers agreed to increase the exchange of intellectuals between the Government of Japan, the Bank of Japan, the Japan Brain Bank, the Asian Vision Institute (AVI) and the Cambodian Institute for Cooperation and Peace (CICP). The two Prime Ministers shared the view that they will continue to cooperate on human resource development for the Cambodian administrative system.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister welcomed Japan's decision to recruit skilled workers and technical interns from March 1, 2022. In particular, Prime Minister Kishida expressed the expectation that many Cambodian skilled workers and technical interns will travel to Japan in a row when the situation of Kovid-19 improves.
In this regard, the two Prime Ministers acknowledged that the development of the payment system of the National Bank of Cambodia "Bakong", supported by Japanese companies, is an innovative effort leading the region and the world. Recognize the importance of supporting this effort.
Speaking at a press conference after the summit, Japanese Prime Minister Kishida Famio said, "We will start new cooperation in the fields of energy, security, digital economy and cyber. Let me give you an example: the Bakong digital payment system of the National Bank of Cambodia was developed in collaboration with a Japanese enterprise. "Japan will continue to support promising projects in the future, such as the Bakong project."
During the fruitful meeting, the Prime Minister also praised Japan for its contribution to achieving a smart city in Cambodia, and the two Prime Ministers agreed to work together to achieve more in the field. This.
