(Siem Reap): The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) has organized its Central Committee Meeting for 3 days from 18 to 20 March 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. HUN Manyi, President of the CPPCC And in the presence of Mr. and Mrs. Vice President and members of the Standing Committee, as well as members of the Central Committee and distinguished guests at the Sokha Conference Hall, Siem Reap.
The purpose of this meeting is to monitor and monitor the progress of the work on the decisions of the General Assembly, strategic plans and other programs of the CPPCC. Implemented in the past, as well as to set priorities and direction activities, continue to seek additional input to seal the work plan in line with the actual development of society, and also to gather to strengthen and expand solidarity in the family of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia.
The topics of discussion discussed above are all important topics that respond to the past actions of the CPPCC. Has been actively fulfilling and reflecting the priority work in line with the vision of the institution to continue the mission to participate in various development processes in all sectors in the country.
In addition to the above results, according to the Articles of Association and Internal Rules of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Chapters 4, 5 and 16, the Central Committee meeting decided to elect 9 more members of the Central Committee, and 3 of them Mr. Chea Somethy, Mr. Keo Piseth and Mr. Ke Suon Sopheap were elected as members of the Standing Committee of the CPPCC Central Committee.
At the same time, the current Central Committee meeting also reached an agreement to organize the National Congress of Representatives, which is scheduled to be held on November 26 and 27, 2022, with the General Assembly being organized. As a committee to amend the statute to fill the role of honorary chairman, as well as to pave the way for the appointment of members of the Central Committee more widely and better.
