The two Prime Ministers will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern. At the end of the meeting, the two Prime Ministers will hold a joint press conference. A joint statement between Cambodia and Japan will be issued after the meeting. General Commission of National Police Disseminates Training Course on "Standard Operating Procedures for Investigating Crimes and Money Laundering Offenses"
The dissemination of the training course "Standard Operating Procedures for Investigating Crimes and Money Laundering Offenses" was conducted in the following 5 sessions:
After the dissemination to the specialized departments and the Capital-Provincial Police Commission, then the leadership of the Capital-Provincial Police Commission will continue to disseminate to its police officers.
The contents of this standard operating procedure focus on the following:
A. Understanding the source of the offense: Judicial police officers must understand the source of the offense that results in the offense so that the judicial police officer has a basis to investigate money laundering offenses.
B. Preliminary conditions for the investigation of money laundering offenses: Judicial police officers must analyze and evaluate the notion of money laundering offenses based on the offenses of the source of the above offenses, requiring a pre-operational asset search and identification of assets. Original.
C. Techniques for investigating money laundering: Judicial police officers must understand the techniques of the investigation, including the investigation of suspects, the beneficiaries of the offenses, the determination of the consequences of the offenses, the determination of assets and the techniques for receiving Get information to support those investigations.
D. Action on the property of the suspect: Judicial police officers, after identifying the property of the suspect, must take immediate measures to take action on those assets, such as seizure of evidence, suspension of account transactions by the intelligence unit. Cambodian finance and so on.
E. Case building: After gathering information that may be based on the assessment of money laundering offenses, the judicial police officer shall make a synthetic report and send the case to the court. In case the judicial police officer is not able to gather enough information, the judicial police officer can attach additional request with the synthesis report to the prosecutor to issue an order to temporarily detain the property suspected to be the result of a crime.
Separately, for the dissemination of this training course, the working group is preparing a dissemination plan to other implementing officers under the General Commission of the National Police.
The visit of the Prime Minister of Japan took place on March 20-21, 2022 at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
During the visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Prime Minister Kishida Fumio will hold bilateral meetings to discuss strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries, including in the areas of trade and investment, education, infrastructure, defense and security, and social rehabilitation. Economic recovery after the crisis of Kovid-19 and other sectors.
The two Prime Ministers will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern. At the end of the meeting, the two Prime Ministers will hold a joint press conference. A joint statement between Cambodia and Japan will be issued after the meeting.
During the visit, Mr. Kishida Fumio will lay a wreath at the Independence Monument and at the shrine of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk "His Majesty the King" of Cambodia. The Prime Minister of Japan will also pay his respects at the shrine of two former Japanese officials who lost their lives in the United Nations mission in Cambodia.
Kishida Fumio's official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia underscores the two countries' strong commitment to promoting and strengthening the existing good relations and strategic partnership and cooperation between Cambodia and Japan. Both within the bilateral and multilateral frameworks for the mutual benefit of both countries. This is the remark of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
Through the relationship that has improved from year to year, the visit and visit of the King of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Prime Minister, as well as senior officials. Of the Japanese government in succession.
Among them, His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni paid four royal visits to Japan, in 2010, 2014, 2018 and 2019, to attend the coronation of the new Emperor Narohito.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, a leader and a key figure in the improvement of Cambodia-Japan relations, has traveled to Japan most of the time, up to 23 times. There were four official visits in 2007, 2013, 2015 and 2017.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs, pays an official visit to Japan in September 2018.
In February 2022, Dr. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, was also invited to visit Japan. Dr. Hun Manet's visit is considered to be the most special visit as Japan took a special plane to transport Dr. Hun Manet and the delegation directly.
Separately, a Japanese delegation also visited Cambodia. Among them are four former prime ministers: Abe Shizo, who visited in 2013, Noda Yoshihiko in 2012, Koizumi Junichiro in 2002, and Obiji Kezo in 2000.
Prince Akishino attends the cremation of His Majesty the King in 2013. Emperor Naruhito, during his reign, paid a royal visit in 2012.
Japanese Prime Minister Kishida Fimio also visited Cambodia in 2014 when he was Japanese Foreign Minister. During the visit, he inaugurated Aeon Mall 1.
In addition to the visits mentioned above, many other senior Japanese government officials have also visited Cambodia.
