Mr. Pen Sovichet said that if the situation of negotiations to end the Russia-Ukraine war to improve, oil prices will fall, but if the market continues to rise, oil prices in Cambodia will have to sell to international markets.
"We see a third round of mitigation talks open to the evacuation of refugees, and we hear that the easing of the crude oil ceasefire fell to almost a hundred last week. So, if the situation changes for the easier, oil prices will fall, but if the market continues to rise, the price of crude oil, of course, our country, which imports refined oil for consumption, we will inevitably sell at international oil prices. No, ”he said. Mr. Pen Sovicheat added.
