(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the Council of Engineers of Cambodia, made eight recommendations to achieve the vision and continue the mission to improve the engineering profession in both quantity and quality. In line with current and future technological developments.
At the Closing Ceremony of the General Assembly, summarizing the results of the five-year work of the second mandate and the implementation plan for the third mandate 2022-2027 of the Board of Engineers of Cambodia, Mr. Ith Sam Heng recommended to the entire General Assembly, including:
1. Strengthen the registration of engineers to be recognized as National Professional Engineers, ASEAN Young Engineers, ASEAN Engineers and ASEAN Outstanding Professional Engineers.
2: Establish a management system for registering engineers in a virtual system (online) to easily manage professional data in the preparation of vocational training plans.
3. Promote the preparation of legal documents related to the field of engineering in accordance with the Mutual Recognition Agreement on the field of engineering in the ASEAN region according to the development of technology and current and future needs.
4: Maintain and disseminate more widely the legal documents and benefits on the registration of engineers.
5. Prepare sub-decree on engineer ethics in order to promote the honor, dignity, integrity and responsibility of engineers in the engineering profession to ensure safety, quality and efficiency, as well as to protect the public interest.
6: Prepare, edit and update the media better and more timely on the website of the Board of Engineers of Cambodia, social media and telegram system to provide comprehensive information.
8: Prepare well to host the 40th Conference of the ASEAN Engineering Federation to be held in November 2022.
He said Cambodia needed to promote social and economic development to catch up with its regional and other countries in the world. These views clearly reflect that engineering education is the key to successful social development.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng emphasized that the Royal Government has been increasing its leadership mechanism to make this engineering institution a strong center that can contribute to the Royal Government in planning a sustainable social development.
It should be informed that the General Assembly summarizes the results of 5 years of the second mandate and the implementation plan for the third mandate 2022-2027 of the Board of Engineers of Cambodia was held on the afternoon of March 18, 2022 at the Hyatt Regency Hotel, Phnom Penh. There is also the election of the Secretary General and Deputy Secretary General of the Board of Engineers of Cambodia of the third mandate.
The Ministry of Labor announces some progress in resolving labor disputes between former workers of NagaWorld and employers after both parties agreed to meet today (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on March 19, 2022 This issued a notice of some progress in resolving labor disputes between former NagaWorld workers and employers.
Unions and workers' representatives:
1: Thank the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and relevant authorities for facilitating the workers' representatives to be temporarily out of jail to participate in the negotiations.
2. Demand that the charges against the 15 workers be released on bail.
3. Required to consider workers who want to return to work and check the payment in accordance with the law.
1: Thank the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and relevant authorities for facilitating this meeting.
2. It is unfortunate that the workers 'representatives promised not to hold further protests to allow for the possibility and create a good atmosphere for the meeting, but the workers' representatives did not keep their promises.
After a lively discussion and presentation explaining the procedure for resolving labor disputes, the two sides agreed as follows:
1: According to the legal procedure, it is not possible to send this dispute back to the Arbitration Council.
Representatives of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will present legal aspects related to the payment of severance pay.
Agree to determine only the points of dispute contained in Arbitration Order No. 012/21 dated September 10, 2021 for discussion.
Once again, the Ministry of Labor requested that both parties have a high level of understanding in resolving this labor dispute, continue to work closely with the competent authorities and relevant parties peacefully, and maintain security and public order. According to the legal procedure, if the negotiations still can not be resolved, the next procedure is that both parties can file a complaint to the court to find a final solution.
