According to a report from Civil Aviation, only five airlines are currently flying between Cambodia and China. Among them, 3 domestic airlines and 2 Chinese companies.
According to the Secretary of State for Civil Aviation, before the 19-Kovid Crisis, Cambodia had six airlines carrying air passengers to 34 major Chinese cities with a total of 220 flights a week. .
In particular, Chinese airlines that flew in and out of Cambodia before the outbreak of Kovid 19 had up to 16 airlines, carrying air passengers from 18 major Chinese cities. There are a total of 195 flights a week.
