The provincial governor also reminded and strengthen the mobilization to expand the membership of the Battambang Red Cross branch on the occasion of the Cambodian Red Cross Day so that they can contribute to support humanitarian work to help the vulnerable, the elderly, the disabled and orphans. Britain decides to shut down Russian RT over alleged links to Kremlin
LONDON (Reuters) - Britain's media regulator on Friday revoked the license of Russia's RT television channel to broadcast in the UK, citing its links to the Kremlin. This is according to the publication of Reuters on March 18, 2022.
The British Broadcasting Corporation (Ofcom) said in a statement that RT had received funding from the Russian government for conducting military operations in Ukraine and cracking down on independent media. According to the authorities, RT TV was evaluated as not being able to act as a responsible media outlet, so it decided to revoke RT's broadcast license.
"We note that the new law in Russia also considers any independent media with anti-Russian tendencies, especially in connection with the war in Ukraine, to be illegal," Ofcom said in a statement. RT, meanwhile, called the decision "unfair."
The Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia chaired the ASEAN Capital Market Forum Online Meeting
The ACMF sets out goals for sustainable development and ensures that ACMF members benefit from market development and help the economy recover from the effects of the 19-Kovid epidemic.
The meeting noted the launch of the first edition of the ASEAN Taxation for Sustainable Finance (ASEAN Taxation) on 10 November 2021 by the ASEAN Taxation Board.
ACMF, together with the ASEAN Insurance Regulators Association, the ASEAN Financial Integration Committee (SLC) and the ASEAN Committee for Capital Market Development, established the ASEAN Reform Council in March 2021.
Following the publication of the first edition of ASEAN Taxation, the ASEAN Taxation Board will consult with stakeholders from the public and private sectors to gather additional input for the development of the next edition of ASEAN Taxation.
As of the end of February 2022, US $ 22.8 billion in cash has been raised from the market through the issuance of the Green Bond, the ASEAN Social and Sustainable Bond standards, all of which are subject to Used in 2017 and 2018.
At the same time, the ACMF has been finalizing the development of the ASEAN Sustainability Bonding Standards and the ASEAN Sustainability and Responsibility Fund Standards to be adopted in 2022.
At the same time, the ASEAN Securities Regulatory Forum welcomed the progress of the ACMF Securities Market Development Program. The meeting noted the success of the training program on sustainable finance, which was launched in December 2021 with the participation of more than 40 senior officials of ACMF members.
During the meeting, Mr. Sou Socheat emphasized that "Improving the environment is the main goal of CCHR. As President of ACMF. "We want to make sure that all ASEAN members can benefit from developments in capital markets through capacity building and information exchange."
He added that capacity building is one of the key priorities of the ACMF Action Plan 2021-2025, which also includes growth promotion and sustainable economic recovery. Strategy.
The meeting welcomed the organization of the ASEAN Awards for Corporate Governance, which is scheduled to be held in September 2022.
The Meeting commended the progress of the work related to the Corporate Governance Assessment as discussed and agreed at the 36th Meeting and the ACMF's efforts to strengthen the implementation of the Corporate Governance Assessment through the organization of Necessary Qualification Requirements
ACMF would like to thank the Sustainable Financial Institutions of Asia (SFIA) and the Council of Industries under the Joint Sustainability Finance Working Group for their continued support and efforts to develop the ASEAN Sustainable Capital Markets.
The ACMF meeting is comprised of 113 heads of securities regulators from 10 ACMF member countries, the Asian Development Bank, the ASEAN Secretariat and the Asian Sustainable Financial Institutions.
The meeting ended smoothly and fruitfully with a joint commitment to environmental sustainability and recovery of ASEAN capital markets.
