General Vong Pisen, on behalf of the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, welcomed the delegation's visit and highly valued the visit, which highlighted the historic close ties between the two countries' armies.
General Vong Pisen highlighted the military cooperation between the two countries in the past and expressed his deep gratitude to the Party, Government, People's Army of Vietnam, which has always provided a lot of support and assistance to Cambodia.
General Vong Pisen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen has always adhered to peaceful coexistence with neighboring countries, friendship, cooperation and development and will continue to strengthen and expand operations in the future. Existing closer and stronger in the long run for the harmony of the two countries.
With this visit, General Vong Pisen also requested the Vietnamese People's Army to continue to train human resources in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, as well as help build some bases.
In response, Lt. Gen. Nguyen Tinh Cuong expressed his gratitude for the warm welcome from His Excellency the Commander-in-Chief and said that Than Ki was his first visit after being appointed Chief of Staff of the Vietnamese People's Army.
Lt. Gen. Nguyen Tinh Cuong emphasized that 2022 is the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between the two countries and also the 45th anniversary of the Day of Remembrance of the Road to the Overthrow of the Genocidal Pol Pot Dam. The two armies must continue to work together to develop in all areas.
He also mentioned the maintenance of security and order along the border and the training of officers, which is important that the two countries' armies must cooperate as they have done in the past in accordance with the agreement. Between the two countries' defense ministries.
