BERLIN: Germany will lift a large number of restrictions imposed to prevent the spread of Kovi 19, although daily cases in the country soared to a new high this Thursday. This is according to the publication by Reuters on Friday, March 18, 2022.
German Chancellor Olaf Scholz said after talks with 16 German state leaders that the daily case record of nearly 300,000 cases was not good news, but a cancellation. Or ease some restrictive measures must be taken to ease the burden on the state health sector.
As of March 20, the requirement to wear a mask will be lifted at certain locations in buildings such as schools or shopping malls, but in clinics and health care centers there is still an obligation to wear a mask. The leaders of 16 German states will have the right to reintroduce measures in areas where severe outbreaks have been reported or in hospitals with high numbers of patients.
