Tax chief leaks from the arrest of a candidate for the opening of a company that makes air bills worth more than $ 80 million to defraud the state tax (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation On March 17, 2022, the arrest of a fraudster who ran for office to open an air invoice company worth 89 million US dollars to embezzle millions of dollars in tax evasion.
The minister confirmed that the fraudster was an employee of a restaurant whose name was Bun Chhlat, and that he and his accomplices had issued 992 bills worth $ 89 million in taxes and were also linked to the Chinese.
The minister explained that the people created fake bills to deduct value added tax (VAT), which is the state's tax money, and used the bill to defraud the tax on profits owed to the state.
Mr. Kong Vibol's breakthrough was made on the occasion of attending the special program on income tax, capital gains tax, ECT for e-commerce of the General Department of Taxation on March 17, 2022.
According to the Minister, the General Department of Taxation has found that there are no less than 200 companies associated with Bun Chhlat's company.
As this March is the deadline for announcing the annual income tax, Kong Vibol called on enterprises that are required to declare taxes to refrain from using invoices as in the case above, as tax evasion is not possible.
