(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) presented the contents of the meeting with stakeholders on the closure of the initial list of candidates at the NEC, the submission of receipts and the resolution of disputes on the list of candidates. First.
According to the content, after the completion of the registration period of candidates of political parties and all complaints have been resolved, the NEC has assigned the NEC to post publicly at its headquarters the list of candidates. First, at least 3 days.
The purpose of this posting is to give eligible voters in the commune / sangkat the right to file a written objection to the NEC about the first candidate or list of candidates within 3 days after the posting date. Public.
Please also be informed that the posting of the first list of candidates must be done according to the case of each commune / sangkat, not all over the country on the same day as the posting of the first voter list.
This means that if a commune / sangkat has resolved all the political parties that have applied for the registration of candidates for the commune / sangkat election, it must post the first list of candidates of its commune within 3 days after The solution is complete.
Citizens who have the right to vote in the commune / sangkat have the right to file a written objection to the NEC about the first candidate or list of candidates within 3 days after the date of public posting.
Complaints shall be filed against candidates or lists of candidates of any political party that do not meet the conditions as stated in articles 35, 36, 37, 39, 40, 41 and 42 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election.
The NEC shall hold a public hearing no later than 3 days after receiving the complaint, with the NEC providing information to the political party that submitted the list of candidates, objections or representation and providing information. To the complainant and to publicly announce the date, time and place of the hearing.
In case the NEC approves the objection to the candidate, the NEC shall reject the candidate by deleting the candidate who has been objected to but retaining the consent of the political party to register the candidate.
However, if the NEC agrees to the objection to the list of candidates, the NEC shall reject the list of candidates of the political party that has the objection, delete the list of candidates and reject the certificate of registration of the candidate of that political party. .
Please note that if there is no objection to any of the initial candidate list, that first candidate list will become the official candidate list. Based on this official list of candidates, the NEC must draw lots to determine the order of the list of candidates to be placed on the ballot in accordance with the NEC regulations and procedures.
