Ms. O Vandin explains the health effects after recovering from Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 19 Vaccination, this morning, March 17, 2022, came out to explain and explain some of the health effects after recovering from the disease. Kovid 19. Ms. O Vandin's comment was made in response to a number of questions, especially for those recovering from Kovid 19.
Ms. O Vandin gave a detailed explanation, which is as follows:
This case depends on the individual organ with which the response and evolution are not the same, especially the state of the individual's antibodies responding to the disease and also depends on the condition in which the individual has undergone a mild illness or disease. Too serious.
Scientists have not yet been able to confirm the extent of the significant effects on the individual body recovering from Kovid-19 and for how long. To have a clear study in the future.
For Kovid-19, especially the new omega-3s, please be aware that its potential for invasion of the human body can not be overlooked, and Kovid-19 is not a flu. Normal and rather not a very common disease, although it is mild, in large part due to the effects of large-scale irrigation in the community.
Do not forget that our bodies may be affected to a greater or lesser extent after being infected with Kovid-19 if we do not have strong defenses. The third dose of Kovid-19 vaccine, or booster dose, will now strengthen the immune system to prevent serious invasions on individual organs and save lives.
In order to increase the body's immune system and avoid the consequences of this deadly disease, I would like to encourage and encourage your attention now, go to the third dose or boost dose. Everyone who has been given a single dose of Johnson Johnson should go and get the booster dose.
