General knowledge: Is the sunrise event at the top of Angkor Wat a coincidence or not?
(Siem Reap): Experts of the Apsara Authority say that the natural phenomenon of the solar system, called "equinox" simply means that the duration of day and night equal to the event of the sunrise at the top of the temple. Angkor Wat, which can be clearly seen from Tarach Prison, will take place on March 21, 2022.
* Is the sunrise event at the top of Angkor Wat a coincidence or not?
Archaeologist and Head of the Department of Preservation of Temples in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology of the APSARA Authority, Mr. Im Sokrithy, said that for 2022, the sunrise at the top of the Angkor Wat temples of this March will be on March 21 is about 6:30 a.m., a special event.
The archaeologist also confirmed that the special event of the sunrise at the top of Angkor Wat for 2022 may occur twice a year, on March 21 and once on September 22. Again.
Although special events like the Sunrise and Sunrise at the top of Angkor Wat occur twice a year, the phenomenon is not the same. In 2019, the sunrise on the central peak of Angkor Wat occurred on March 20, early in the morning, as can be seen from the central gate of Tuk Reach Prison (the main gate). West) During the period from 5:50 to about 7 am.
