(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, this morning, March 16, 2022, chaired a meeting to review and evaluate health achievements in 2021 and set the direction for 2022 in the context of living with Kovid-19. The new normal course that this meeting takes place at the Ministry of Health.
The health sector is a priority sector that has contributed significantly to the socio-economic development and poverty reduction in Cambodia by improving the health status of the Cambodian people, which provides opportunities for people to participate. Actively in socio-economic activities to improve living conditions.
He asserted that Cambodia had succeeded in the national Kovid-19 vaccination campaign, both at baseline and in a dose, to build a truly strong community and well-managed public health risk levels, despite community outbreaks. Still happening.
The Minister commended all civil servants and health workers for their efforts to overcome obstacles and difficulties in order to expand the provision of quality health education, examination, care and treatment to our people in all geographies throughout the country, especially in health posts and Health centers in rural areas.
He appreciated the support and cooperation from local administrations and relevant institutions at all levels, active community involvement and partnerships with the private sector, financial and technical support from national and international development partners and NGOs, and progress. Other sectors will make a significant contribution to the progress of the health sector in 2021, especially the joint efforts and mobilization of available resources to prevent and curb the spread of Kovid-19.
The health sector has continued to promote the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 for "Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency" of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 6th legislature of the National Assembly, under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The comprehensive and long-term vision of the Royal Government of the 6th Legislature (of the National Assembly) is to continue to promote the sustainable development of the health sector to improve the health and well-being of all Cambodians, especially the poor and vulnerable. Women and children aim to contribute to the economic, social and development of poverty reduction in Cambodia.
In response to this ambitious vision, health officials at all levels must continue to implement key health interventions to drive progress in reproductive, maternal and child health programs, combating infectious diseases, combating non-communicable diseases and strengthening and expanding programs. Strengthen the health care system.
In addition, based on the experience of the strengths and weaknesses of the Ministry of Health in implementing the 2021 plan, the Minister is confident that the health sector will achieve many new achievements and progress in the implementation of the implementation plan. 2022 and beyond.
