Stung Treng Provincial Administration Holds a Meeting to Summarize 2021 Work Results and Raise Work Directions
(Stung Treng): On the morning of March 16, 2022, Stung Treng Provincial Administration organized a meeting to review the work results for 2021 and raise the work direction for 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Phay Bun Chhoeun, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group. Local Stung Treng Province.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng Province, presented a summary report on the results of the meeting to review the work results in 2021 and the work direction in 2022, and then Mr. Phay Bunchhoeun provided some important guidelines to the meeting.
Mr. Phay Bunchhoeun stated that the strengthening of peace, political stability and security of public order, especially to increase cooperation among the competent forces, authorities and inspire the participation of the people in the implementation of the policy. Security »To prevent and crack down on theft, robbery, illegal gambling, gangs in all localities throughout the province.
The implementation of decentralization and deconcentration reforms will continue to strengthen the management, management and implementation of functions already transferred from the national level with a high degree of ownership and responsibility, as well as innovation to ensure the implementation of these functions in a consistent manner. According to the minimum standards of service delivery and policies for each sector.
He said that the management of natural resources and the settlement of land disputes, the management of natural resources, forestry and the settlement of land disputes are the relevant tasks, roles and responsibilities of the ministries and institutions in formulating the policy framework and legal framework. Security management and development of border areas continue to strengthen and expand good cooperation with the relevant authorities and competent forces of neighboring countries.
Socio-economic development pays attention to supporting and facilitating agricultural and business investment activities throughout the province, especially providing support and favors for the development of agriculture and agro-industry, which are the main priority areas of the province.
Providing public services and solving local challenges Strengthen the provision of services at the OWSO at the provincial hall to make it easier for people to receive services at the same place, as well as monitor and support the operation of the OWSO. Single entry and citizen office at the municipal administration to ensure the provision of these administrative services.
Finally, Mr. Phay Bunchhoeun reminded to strengthen the implementation of measures to fight against Kovid-19 and to strengthen the working system, labor relations, solidarity and internal unity, in which the Chairman of the Council and the Governor of the district. To be the core in strengthening the internal working system of its council and board of governors in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.
