(Sihanoukville): Japanese Ambassador Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, and Mr. Noguchi Yasushi, Commander of the 1st Mine Clearance Division of the Japan Navy Self-Defense Forces, this morning, March 16, 2022. He was allowed to visit Ream Naval Base and meet with the Commander of the Cambodian Maritime Space, Admiral Ouk Seiha.
As the ship approached the port of Ream, both the Japanese Ambassador and the Commander of the Japanese Navy were paying close attention to the development of the Ream Sea Base, with about three ferries equipped with injectors. Act on the sea about 300 meters from the beach in this Ream sea base.
Admiral Ouk Seiha also brought the Ambassador and Commander of the Japanese Navy Self-Defense to inspect the workshop where the Navy was repairing the ship.
In particular, during the meeting, Admiral Ouk Seiha provided information directly on the development of the Ream Sea base, such as improving the capacity of factories for repairing ships and building a port with a deeper water depth for large ships. Can park and so on.
Admiral Ouk Seiha emphasized that "as Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh have repeatedly stated that the development at Ream Naval Base is to strengthen Cambodia's defense, not Threaten any country. Countries inside and outside the region are all friends of Cambodia. "Cambodia does not need to be an enemy to any country, this is Cambodia's foreign policy."
Admiral Ouk Seiha also welcomed the Japanese support and protection at the Ream Naval Base. During the meeting, he also asked Japan to help develop the capacity of the hospital at Ream Sea Base, which provides medical services not only for the army but also for the people in the area.
Both Ambassador Mikami Masahiro and Commander-in-Chief of the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Forces expressed their appreciation for Admiral Ouk Seiha's open-mindedness, providing straightforward information on infrastructure development at sea. The Ream.
The Commander of the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Force also expressed the expectation that the Cambodian Navy, especially the Commander of the Ream Maritime Space, would give him the opportunity to visit the sea base later when the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Ship enters. Come to Cambodia. He also hoped that the Cambodian Maritime Army would have better cooperation with the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Forces for the benefit of both countries.
As many as 400,741 cases of Kovid 19 are reported daily as the East Asian country seeks to further narrow the social security gap, despite the onslaught of omega virus infections. This is according to the publication of CNA on March 16, 2022.
According to the Associated Press, South Korea recorded the highest number of deaths due to Kovi 19 on Tuesday, with 293 deaths.
South Korean health officials say the medical response remains stable after efforts to expand resources by 30 percent of emergency rooms nationwide for the treatment of COVID-19 patients. But they warned that pressure on the hospital system could increase in the coming weeks.
More than 62 percent of South Koreans have received the booster dose. Recently, the South Korean Ministry of Health has eased restrictions on catastrophic measures, border controls and does not require the issuance of a certificate of vaccination or a negative test by an adult upon entry. And allow more people to receive treatment at home.
