Phnom Penh Forestry Administration Inserts 1,000 Rare Tree Species at Wat Phnom Historical Resort
(Phnom Penh): Officials of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration have put a sign on a tree at the historical site of Wat Phnom in order for national and international tourists and the next generation to know about luxury wood.
On the morning of March 16, 2022, Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration District, led the officials under the supervision of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration District, said that the tree signage was written in Khmer and Latin letters. In order for national and international guests to get to know the luxury wood species in Cambodia.
He added that under the guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, he instructed the Forestry Administration to inspect and maintain trees, not only at Wat Phnom, but all trees in Phnom Penh. .
At the same time, Mr. Koam Seiha confirmed that the trees support the environmental flag and help maintain green habitats in the area of Wat Phnom as well as in Phnom Penh.
He added that the Governor of Phnom Penh has always advised the Forestry Administration to take care of all trees and to love and care for trees as we love and care for our children, because trees are very important for human life, animals and biodiversity. All kinds, especially it is a wind barrier, flood barrier and bring rain to increase human livelihood.
This morning, about 100 of the more than 1,000 trees in the resort site were marked with more than 50 different species, all of which are rare local species, such as Beng Thnong. Koki, Chheuteal, Neang Nuon and many other types of mountain trees.
In addition, Mr. Koam Seiha also called on people to maintain and plant trees in their homes for the benefit of the environment and for future generations to know about rare trees, especially trees. Help create oxygen in the atmosphere and absorb carbon dioxide, which facilitates daily life. Volunteer doctors of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum visit and give gifts to people with 19 Kovid in Chamkarmon
