Ministry of Labor Invites Representatives of Former NagaWorld Employees and Employers' Representatives to Resolve Labor Disputes This Afternoon
(Phnom Penh): A meeting to coordinate the settlement of labor disputes in the case of NagaWorld Limited will be held at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training at 2:30 pm on March 16, 2022.
Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, confirmed to Fresh News that during the meeting, the Commission for Resolving Strikes and Demonstrations in All Matters summoned representatives of former NagaWorld employees and representatives of employers to attend. The meeting aims to mediate and seek solutions to disputes and grievances of former NagaWorld employees and employees.
He said the push for the meeting was in line with the spirit and commitment of eight former NagaWorld employees who had pledged with the ministry to represent NagaWorld staff and employees in resolving the dispute. This work and protest is in accordance with legal procedures, especially regarding the payment of compensation, termination of joint employment contract.
It should be noted that on March 14, 2022, 8 former employees applied to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to be temporarily out of jail to act as a representative to resolve labor disputes with NAGA WORLD. By law, they promised not to protest, which would endanger public order and national security.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has been working tirelessly to resolve labor disputes between NagaWorld and its laid-off workers. From December 18 to 27, 2021, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, through the Committee for Resolving Strikes and Demonstrations in All Matters, invited the parties to the dispute to negotiate seven times.
Biden plans to announce $ 800 million in additional military aid to Ukraine
WASHINGTON: US President Joe Biden is expected to announce an additional $ 800 million in military aid to Ukraine, which is battling Russian troops. This was released by CNN on Wednesday, March 16, 2022.
The announcement of military aid, scheduled for Wednesday, will increase US aid to Ukraine to $ 1 billion and $ 2 billion since Biden was sworn in as president last year. January 2021.
According to the White House, the military aid package includes anti-tank missiles. But so far, the Biden administration has remained opposed to Zelensky's proposal to establish a no-fly zone in Ukraine, which he sees as necessary to prevent Russian bombings.
Both NATO and the United States have said that the establishment of a no-fly zone in Ukraine could lead to a direct conflict with Russia, which is a risk of a world war. But Washington has warned it will take immediate action to prevent NATO territory from disappearing. Myanmar to accept Thai baht for cross-border trade transactions
(Myanmar): Myanmar will begin accepting Thai baht for cross-border trade transactions and is also looking at similar plans to use Indian rupee for the same trade. According to Reuters.
Myanmar's military-controlled government has already said it will also accept the Chinese yuan as the official trading currency.
"By reducing our reliance on the US dollar, we will reduce the risk of immediate exchange rate fluctuations due to external geopolitical factors," Myanmar's Ministry of Commerce and Investment said in a statement. The two ministries added that the measure would help reduce inflation caused by a stronger dollar.
The move will also support the economic recovery, the statement said. Despite the rise in energy prices, Myanmar should see a modest GDP growth in the fiscal year ending October 2022, the statement added.
Myanmar's economy has slowed since the military overthrew an elected government a year ago and launched a bloody crackdown on the opposition.
Thailand is Myanmar's second largest trading partner after China, the statement said. Trade in the fiscal year 2020-2021 was $ 5.3 billion. Myanmar's main exports include gas, metals and garments, products imported from Thailand, including machinery, transport equipment and manufactured goods. According to Reuters.
