The following is the full text of the Prakas of the Ministry of Economy: Samdech Techo urges the strengthening of cooperation between the Cambodian and Japanese peacekeepers
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his deep satisfaction with the excellent cooperation between the Cambodian and Japanese peacekeepers. Samdech Techo asked the two countries' peacekeepers to further strengthen this cooperation.
The Prime Minister welcomed and welcomed the Japanese ships docked in Cambodia. Samdech Techo highlighted that the docking of the two Japanese Navy Self-Defense Boats marks the 30th anniversary of the completion of the peacekeeping mission in Cambodia and the success of the cooperation in the peacekeeping mission between Cambodia and Japan.
Samdech Techo expressed his observation that Japan's role in the peacekeeping mission has played an increasingly important role. Samdech Techo also reminded of Japan's peacekeeping mission in Cambodia 30 years ago. Samdech Techo stated that the mission not only helped to bring peace to Cambodia, but also contributed to the progress in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pride in the cooperation of the Cambodian and Japanese peacekeepers. Samdech Techo also encouraged the peacekeeping forces of the two countries to continue cooperating to ensure security, peace and respect for international law.
After the courtesy call and discussion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also hosted a dinner for the Japanese commander and crew.
It should be noted that two Japanese naval self-defense ships and about 200 crew members docked in Cambodia this morning, Tuesday, March 15, 2022, to celebrate the 30th anniversary of Japan's peacekeeping mission in Cambodia.
The presence of the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Ship and its crew at the port of Sihanoukville was warmly welcomed by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, directly at the port.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh emphasized that despite the development of Cambodia in all fields over the past 30 years, the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia will always remember and appreciate the participation of the Japanese Self-Defense Forces peacekeepers. Came to complete the mission in Cambodia for the first time.
Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, highly appreciated the efforts of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to achieve peace and development today through the tragic past and difficult path. .
The Japanese ambassador expressed his confidence that the docking of the Japanese Self-Defense Fleet is an important co-operation that will contribute to achieving a "free and open Indo-Pacific policy."
Admiral Ouk Seiha, Deputy Commander of the Navy and Commander of the Naval Base, said that from 2000 to the present, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port has welcomed 12 Japanese naval self-defense ships. Lifting equal to 27 units. Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly instructs the Ministry of Rural Development to continue to expand and strengthen the implementation of the Rural Development Strategic Plan.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, instructed the Ministry of Rural Development to continue to expand and strengthen the implementation of the Rural Development Strategic Plan 2019-2023.
This instruction was made on the occasion that Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2021 work review meeting and the 2022 work direction of the Ministry of Rural Development on the afternoon of March 15. 2022.
In this conference, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly instructed the Ministry of Rural Development to continue to expand and strengthen the implementation of its Strategic Plan for Rural Development 2019-2023, focusing on four key strategic programs, including:
1: Development of physical and communication infrastructure 2: Improving the living conditions of rural communities 3: Diversification of rural economic activities and 4: Strengthening institutions, capacity development and human resources.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly emphasized that these programs must continue to be implemented in all aspects and cover the whole country in order to contribute to the reform programs of the Royal Government.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly also told the Ministry to continue to study, research and develop the construction, repair and improvement of rural roads through new technologies in response to the reduction of raw materials such as red gravel, sand, mountains, etc.
At the same time, we must continue to strengthen the use of rural roads more effectively, ensure quality through maintenance and repair, especially efforts to prevent and suppress overweight transportation on rural roads. This was further confirmed by Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly.
Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, said that despite the context of the Kovid epidemic, the work of repairing, restoring, maintaining and improving rural infrastructure has been a proud achievement.
Ministry of Tourism Chairs a Working Group Meeting to Evaluate and Manage Phnom Penh's Safe Tourism Destinations
(Phnom Penh): On March 15, 2022, the Ministry of Tourism organized a meeting of the Executive Working Group to Assess and Manage the Safe Tourism Destinations in Phnom Penh, chaired by Mr. Chea Bora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the Executive Working Group to Assess and Manage Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh Safe Tourism Destination Area.
The program was conducted by remote video (ZOOM MEETING) with the participation of members of the Executive Committee of the Director of the Department of Health of Phnom Penh, Director of the Department of Tourism of Phnom Penh, Khan Administration, officials and relevant units under the administration of Phnom Penh, a total of 112 people.
On the other hand, the Secretary of State also confirmed that through Resolution No. 019 Pillar. Dated 11 March 2022 on the Establishment of an Executive Working Group to Assess and Manage Phnom Penh's Safe Tourism Destinations to Study, Evaluate, Monitor, Compile Reports / Documents and Update Target Situation and Market Sources in Accordance with Local and Global Changes .
The meeting commended the establishment of an executive working group to evaluate and manage the Phnom Penh Safe Tourism Destination Area and agreed to set out a number of work directions, including:
* Continuing and promoting the international tourism market assessment work that should be absorbed at this stage, currently the tourism market is really the most acute and narrower competition.
* Continue to cooperate and be consistent with the relevant parties, especially the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and Immigration, to widely disseminate all the policies that have been achieved and put forward by the Royal Government, especially all the principles that are facilitated. Tourist travel.
* Continue to strengthen the implementation of tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures for tourism businesses that have been implemented in the past, we can not "go back" is not to reduce the conditions for implementation.
* The Secretariat shall collect and summarize the report of the achievements of the working group on a monthly basis and must make it regular. Pakistan rejects India's interpretation of missile launch
