Top trade official: Russia-Ukraine war has not affected Cambodia's exports and imports unless oil prices rise
(Phnom Penh): Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that the war between Russia and Ukraine has not affected Cambodia's exports and imports, except for oil prices. Increase.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat made the remarks at a press conference at the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership: Impacts, Challenges and Future Growth for East Asia and ASEAN on March 14, 2022 at the Hyatt Regency Hotel.
"I want to let the public know that the war between Russia and Ukraine has not had any effect on Cambodia, except for oil prices," Pen Sovicheat said at the press conference.
Mr. Pen Sovichet emphasized that Cambodia continues to export to Russia as usual and continues to import to Russia normally without any impact.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat said that the price of oil is something that the Royal Government pays attention to and hopes that the Russia-Ukraine war will end soon, so things will return to normal soon.
According to data from the Ministry of Commerce, the trade volume between Cambodia and Russia in 2021 was more than 94.18 million US dollars, an increase of more than 30 million US dollars, compared to 63.81 million US dollars in 2020. . According to the data, Cambodia exported more than $ 59.54 million to Russia, while imports from Russia amounted to $ 34.64 million.
