The following is the speech of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: Minister of Rural Development: The Royal Government has been paying high attention to rural development.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, on March 15, 2022, stated that the Royal Government under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, has been paying attention Put high priority on rural development work.
This statement was made on the occasion of Dr. Ouk Rabun presiding over the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of 2021 and the work direction of 2022 of the Ministry of Rural Development this morning, March 15, 2022.
Dr. continued that this has been making progress in all areas, especially the rural situation in Cambodia has improved significantly and has been contributing to improving the living standards of rural people.
The Minister of Rural Development also said that despite the huge demand and limited resources, we recognize that rural development work has not yet been adequately met in terms of both quantity and quality, despite partners. Many development and civil society organizations have been actively contributing to the Royal Government.
At the same time, the Ministry recognizes that living standards, health and sanitation, education and rural community values are still low, which is the gap between rural and urban / urban areas and between rural and rural areas. While the average per capita income for 2021 nationwide will reach US $ 1,730, in most rural areas it will be less than US $ 1,000.
At the same time, the Minister of Development stated that 2022 is the fourth year of the implementation of the Strategic Plan for Rural Development 2019-2023, which the Ministry of Rural Development has set the main policy objectives is to "improve the quality and value of life. Of the rural people with the economic, social and cultural environment ”by defining the four pillars as the priority program:
1: Development of physical and communication infrastructure, 2: Improving the living conditions of rural communities, 3: Diversification of rural economic activities, and 4: Strengthening administrative support services and general affairs.
He said that the implementation of the Rural Development Strategic Plan for the past three years, the Ministry of Rural Development has achieved remarkable results in many years, despite the epidemic situation of Kovid-19, and Actively contributing to the changing livelihoods of rural people in an economic, social, cultural and environmental environment.
In fact, people in rural areas have the opportunity to engage in additional occupations such as raising livestock, growing vegetables, making handicrafts, doing business, and providing lucrative services to increase their family income in addition to farming.
