The main purpose of the formation of this military alliance was not only to curb the influence of Soviet-led communist ideology, but also to expand the influence of liberal ideology.
According to NATO's website, countries wishing to join the alliance must meet certain political, economic and military standards.
NATO requires countries wishing to join to meet certain conditions, including:
* Relevant countries must adhere to democracy.
Relevant countries must progress towards a free market economy or capitalism.
* The military forces of the country concerned must be under the control of the civilians, not under the authority of any leader or commander.
* Relevant countries must have good relations with their neighbors and respect the sovereignty of their neighbors.
* Last but not least, the countries that want to join NATO meet the above criteria, but still have to wait and see if all NATO member countries vote for everyone or not? This means that if a member state does not support the participating country, it will not be able to join NATO.
