(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, confirmed that the flyover and subway of Choam Chao roundabout, which is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, so far the whole site has achieved about 98 to 99 percent. There are only five days left to complete the temporary transit for the people.
Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed this on the occasion of leading professional officials as well as contractors for the construction of the flyover and subway to inspect the actual situation on the afternoon of March 14, 2022.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's inspection of the actual situation is to accelerate the remaining work to be completed within the next 5 days to request the principle of temporary opening and to check the status of the official location of the opening of the flyover under Presiding over the upcoming Prime Minister Hun Sen. However, the Governor of Phnom Penh did not specify when the inauguration of the new achievement will take place.
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng also confirmed the delay due to Kovid 19 disease, which made the workers as well as the recipients of the construction delayed, however, the flyover and subway Chom Chao will be able to The people of Bal will pass temporarily in the next few days.
It should be noted that the Choam Chao flyover and subway is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, contracted by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC), with a construction period of 30 months and a construction cost of approximately 22 million US dollars. .
Based on the technical specifications of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, this construction site is divided into 3 parts:
* The first bridge is the main flyover connecting traffic from Russian Boulevard to National Road No. 3, with a total length of 408 meters and a width of 15.8 meters, with two lanes to two lanes to a slope of 4.5 meters and a maximum height of Traffic under the bridge is 5.5 meters.
* The second bridge separates from the main flyover, turns left, connects traffic from Russian Boulevard to Veng Sreng for one-way traffic, with one lane for cars and one lane for motorcycles, with a total length of 202 meters (40 meters of flyover, subway) 118 meters long and 44 meters long dirt road) 5.25 meters wide.
The bridge will be 100 years old, equipped with lighting poles, road network around the flyover and underground water reservoir, as well as automatic pump motors.
It should be noted that the flyover and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout officially opened the construction site on June 29, 2018 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprit. Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen.
TOKYO (Reuters) - Japanese Foreign Minister Yoshimasa Hayashi said at a daily news conference on Monday that the Japanese government could use its expertise and experience to help resolve leaks. Radioactive material or other nuclear incidents if this happens in Ukraine. This is according to the publication of the Russian newspaper RT on Monday, March 14, 2022.
"If there is a disaster in Ukraine, during the current war situation, Japan can share its skills and experience gained from dealing with radioactive leaks at the plant," the senior Japanese official said. Fukushima nuclear power plant in 2011. Last week, Japan just celebrated the anniversary of the Fukushima power plant disaster.
In the past, the safety of Ukraine's nuclear power plants has become a topic of international concern after reports of fighting near the sites.
