In the first two months of this year, Cambodia approved 37 investment projects with a total investment of nearly 2.4 billion USD.
The report of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News, states that in the first two months of 2022, Cambodia has approved investment projects in various sectors will be able to create jobs for tens of thousands of people.
Most of these 37 investment projects include: garment factory construction projects, fruit packaging processing plant projects, tire production projects and many other projects.
Tycoon Lim Heng stated, "We see that the registration with the Council for the Development of Cambodia for investment projects is still increasing. Not only that, the new nursery companies at the Ministry of Economy and Finance have also seen an increase. "This increase is seen as a good sign for Cambodia."
Tycoon Lim Heng said that while some countries in the region, which enjoy the same tariffs as Cambodia, are facing political crises as well as the spread of Kovid, turning orders from those countries to Cambodia. To establish new factories in Cambodia.
At the same time, Tycoon Lim Heng also mentioned that Omikrong disease, if the disease is very widespread, it will affect the production line of Cambodia due to the sick workers or staff, however, he said. We must all implement three measures, not three defenses.
Oknha Lim Heng continued that the leaders of the Royal Government have vaccinated the whole country, which can control the situation of Kovid and reopen the economy in all sectors, and he believes that this vaccination measure is very important, as Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the vaccine Is economic.
In addition, Tycoon Lim Heng emphasized that the nationwide vaccination and control of the Kovid epidemic will give foreign investors confidence who are looking at Cambodia, especially Chinese investment, to return. Gradually, there will be more new investment projects.
