Tycoon Try Pheap builds 12 coast guard towers on Ochheuteal beach and hand them over to Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration for use in rescuing and protecting tourists
(Preah Sihanouk): Duke Try Pheap built 12 coast guard posts along Ochheuteal Beach and handed over to the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration for use in rescuing and protecting the people and tourists. Who goes to visit the beach.
The handover ceremony of the 12 towers was held on March 14, 2022, presided over by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Duke Try Pheap.
The 12 towers were built of solid Khmer-style tiled roofs standing on the beach, at a cost of US $ 72,000 donated by Duke Try Pheap as a bond for the provincial administration. All together.
During the reception from the then-tycoon Try Pheap, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that in the past, Ochheuteal beach was privately used and there was no public space, but after the efforts of the Royal Government, the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development Cambodia, as well as the Sihanoukville provincial administration, has made the beach more than 16 kilometers long and more than 4 kilometers west for national and international visitors.
He said that after the opening of public spaces along the coast, now the provincial administration has received the help of 12 more towers, which will facilitate the Coast Guard to be a permanent stand ready to rescue and protect safety. To people and tourists who visit the beach.
Meanwhile, the governor of Kouch Chamroeun province also called on the beach cleaners and coast guard to come and get the fourth dose to increase the immunity of everyone.
Please be informed that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Royal Government has improved some coastal roads and infrastructure in Sihanoukville and was led by Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the Committee. National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia.
