General Kun Kim and his wife also prayed to the sacred objects in the world and the merits of the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks to help nurture and take care of the soul of Akka Moha Upasak Lim Chhun to go to death.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Vanna, Secretary of State, Deputy Minister of Public Works and Transport, Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, presided over the opening ceremony of the Six Sigma Theory Training Course A total of 170 people.
The training course held on March 14, 2022 at the Ministry was attended by 27 trainees, 26 secretaries of state, 10 undersecretaries of state, 10 directors general, 39 deputy directors general, 43 department heads and public department heads. And transport 25 people.
This training course is organized by Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport in order to strengthen the efficiency of leadership, institution / unit management, increase the capacity to lead and manage the institution, increase revenue and profit, reduce time and reduce costs and increase skills. Solve the problems of the officials in each unit better with the participation of Mr. Ros Vanna as a trainer.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, Mr. Ros Vanna emphasized the importance of the support and commitment of the management, especially the participation of all stakeholders in the unit / institution from the lowest level to Reach out to the leadership of that unit / institution to successfully implement this Six Sigma philosophy theory as well as to integrate this theory into a culture of that organization / institution.
At the same time, the Secretary of State requested all participants to pay high attention and commitment to absorb the knowledge and experience from this program to apply in their unit more effectively and further confirmed. That he will try his best to present in detail the main theories to all participants so that this training can be successful as planned.
Please be informed that this training is divided into 3 courses for different target groups, including: The first course is prepared for the leadership from the director of the department, the director of the department to the Secretary of State, the second course is prepared for the deputy director of the Department of Public Works and Transport in the 25 capitals. Provinces and the third session is prepared for the deputy director of the department.
Groundbreaking Ceremony for a New 3,000-Meter DBST Road in Sangkat Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang City
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovanrith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, at the groundbreaking ceremony for the 3,000-meter-long DBST road in Kampong Chhnang commune on the morning of March 14, 2022, said that peace is the first choice that people Citizens want.
He said that there is peace, there is development, and there is a way, there is hope, which is the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The provincial governor said that the Kampong Chhnang provincial administration reopened the new 3,000-meter-long DBST asphalt road through three villages in Kampong Chhnang commune to make it easier for people to travel again after the road was damaged. Damage caused by previous floods.
At the same time, the provincial governor also requested the local people to help install sewers in front of their respective houses to release rainwater from flooding the road, which led to the damage to the rubber road, which leads to unusability. Long lasting. In particular, after the construction of this paved road, the provincial administration will plant peacock trees and arrange carola on the sidewalk to turn Kampong Chhnang into a beautiful city to attract tourists.
During the ceremony, Mr. Yin Saven, Governor of Kampong Chhnang City, also reported that the new rubber road to be repaired is 3,000 meters long, 8 meters wide and 5 meters wide on DBST. Three villages, Damnak Popoul, Sre Pring village and Trapeang Chiksa village in Kampong Chhnang commune, are funded by the Kampong Chhnang provincial administration.
In addition, on the sidewalk behind the provincial hospital and behind the provincial education school, there are also a number of slums built on the sidewalk, which must be involved in repairing the road above.
The Governor of Kampong Chhnang called on the Electricity Company, the Cable Company and the Water Supply Company to cooperate in inspecting their relevant power lines, cables and water pipes in order for the above road repair work to be successful. As for the people living on the above streets, they have to install a 6-meter-wide sewer in front of their houses for everyone.
On this occasion, Ms. Ke Chanmony, Member of Parliament for Kampong Chhnang Constituency, Mr. Long Chhun Lay, Chairman of Provincial Council, also visited and distributed food gifts to more than 100 families with the provincial governor and his team. Get 50 kilos of rice, a stick of fish sauce, a stick of soy sauce and a budget of 30,000 riels. As for the 25 widows, each of them received 100,000 Riels.
