(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the inauguration of Wing Sen Sok Branch and Independence Monument this morning, March 14, 2022, Mr. HUN Manet said that the growth of banking and financial institutions in Cambodia in the last 20 years This is an important contribution to improving the financial environment in Cambodia.
Mr. HUN Manet stated that the financial environment is recognized to play an important role in contributing to enable people as well as small and medium enterprises to access financial services quickly, easily and affordably as a guarantee. Expand the potential of economic activity in all sectors and reduce poverty in society.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Manet expressed his congratulations on the successes and achievements that the company will strive to achieve in the past 13 years, which is another proud achievement of local companies.
He added that the expansion into a commercial bank and the opening of two branches, which were officially announced today, also reflect the stability, resilience and market potential of the financial sector in Cambodia. Especially in the context of the global epidemic of Kovid-19, which has affected the socio-economic situation at the global, regional and national levels.
At the same time, Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Director General of Supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the expansion of the operating network of Wing Bank (Cambodia) MK through the opening of Sen Sok Branch and Vimean Ekareach Branch is a testament to this. Shows the growth of the banking sector in Cambodia, as well as the confidence of investors, both foreign and domestic, in this sector, despite the context of the Code-19.
He added that at the same time, the trend of Wing Bank (Cambodia) CMC has been significantly contributing to the improvement of the financial environment by providing responsible and professional financial services to the people. Cambodia.
Please be informed that Wing Bank will use modern technology provided by world-class partners to reduce the cost of banking operations and reduce the time for the credit process.
Takeo Documentation Center Meets Local Authorities in Tram Kak District's Lay Bo Commune to Discuss "Health and History Project"
(Takeo): The Takeo Provincial Document Center team visited Lay Bo commune hall in Tram Kak district, Takeo province to meet with local authorities. The purpose of the visit was to inform the authorities and to request that the local authorities cooperate in disseminating the project on "Promoting the Rights and Improving the Health of Khmer Rouge Survivors". .
The Takeo Documentation Center team also asked local authorities to search for 20 fourth-generation Cambodian volunteers to visit and listen to the stories of Khmer Rouge survivors in the commune where the volunteers were Live and provide information on medical check-ups and provide health check-ups for survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime.
The reason why the Takeo Provincial Document Center team decided to choose Lay Bo commune as a place for volunteers to go to work is because this commune is located near the provincial town of Takeo, which provides convenience for survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime to visit Health at Reaksa Sok Takeo Hospital.
With the aim of the above health project will provide opportunities for survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime in Takeo and other provinces throughout Cambodia to visit free health clinics at private clinics that are contracted with Documentation Center of Cambodia.
After the meeting of Commune Chiefs, First Deputy Chiefs, Second Deputy Chiefs, Commune Councilors, Commune Clerks, 25 commune administrative assistants and village chiefs in Lai Bo commune expressed their satisfaction with the health project for survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime. In Lay Bo commune, many Khmer Rouge survivors are facing health problems and are unable to get medical check-ups.
