Leaking gas tank, igniting a garment handicraft, destroying some materials in Por Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out due to a leaking gas tank, causing a fire in a garment factory and destroying some equipment in Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Sen Chey.
This incident happened at 7:30 AM on March 12, 2022 at a garment handicraft in Thmor Koul 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to a report by Colonel Prohm Yorn, the director of the office, who told Fresh News that after receiving information from residents that there was a fire burning in the garment industry, he immediately ordered the fire brigade. Firefighters stationed at the location of Por Sen Chey district hall to dispatch fire trucks to intervene.
In that, Colonel Prohm Yorn also ordered to the target station at Sen Sok district to help release two more fire trucks to help the location that is burning.
The Colonel continued that during the rescue operation, our specialized force used 3 fire trucks of the office, used 3 trucks of water equal to 12 cubic meters to completely extinguish.
According to the colonel, the fire destroyed a 6-by-16-meter galvanized stone and damaged equipment, including 10 sewing machines, a television, a refrigerator and a gas tank. Containers, some cloth and did not cause the fire to spread to the neighbor's house.
However, for this operation, our competent authorities managed at 8:00 am the same day. The fire did not cause any casualties.
