Children infected with bird flu in Siem Reap have recovered
(Siem Reap): A 1-year-old baby girl was diagnosed with bird flu in Siem Reap after some suspicious symptoms. The child has now recovered from his illness.
The director of the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, Dr. Kros Sarath, said on March 12 that the children infected with the bird flu had recovered and were no longer infected. He added that the patient lives in Trapeang Run village, Russey Lok commune, Chi Kreng district, Siem Reap province.
On March 11, doctors visited infected families and took samples from 13 people (seven females) and sprayed six houses with disinfectants. As for the house that got the bird flu and transmitted it to its children, it raised 20 chickens and 11 died. According to Mr. Krous Sarath, he confirmed that so far there are no new cases.
