Local police officers, along with villagers, began searching for the child victim. At 10:30 p.m., the girl's body was found, noting that there was an attempt to bury it.
This joint task force is under the leadership of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Sithi Loh.
The CUP added: "This mission still has many questions that we have not yet answered, but I believe that the joint team will find answers related to the actions that took place on the girl. I would like to ask the public, if there is information or see the victim while walking to school, please provide this information to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police or CPU.
Colonel Sao Saroeun, Poipet City Police Inspector, said that after receiving a complaint from the victim's family, he led the police force to search until night until the girl's body was found and taken away. Buried in a plot of land in Tumnup K5 village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, with stones and all the trees in a naked state.
Lt. Gen. Sithi Loh said that after finding the body of the victim girl, he also ordered the specialized police force in cooperation with the Poipet City Police Force to inspect the scene to autopsy the body and carry out the procedure by Take the utmost care to arrest the perpetrators and punish them according to the law.
