According to Pakistani Air Force officials, the object is under surveillance to determine its identity, but preliminary studies suggest it could be a supersonic missile fired from the air. Surface, but it is determined not to explode. The object traveled at an altitude of more than 1,200 meters at Mach 3 (three times the speed of sound) and flew 124 kilometers in Pakistani airspace before crashing.
