He said that the reserve land of the Ministry of Agriculture is 1914,2367 hectares. In the past, the provincial authorities and the Ministry have also cooperated to find a solution and prohibit some people from illegally occupying, but these people continue to oppress the occupation by refusing to listen.
Mr. Sevan Piseth, Governor of Sesan District, confirmed that in the past, provincial officials and local authorities in villages, communes and districts had instructed to stop the encroachment and to make a contract to return the land to the state with professional officials, but some also Have left and others continue to rule in breach of contract.
"Today, I would like you to cooperate with the team and implement the contract," he said. As for the people who have just moved here, they really do not have land to live on and grow real crops.
In this operation, the national and provincial working groups decided to establish a working group in cooperation with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, including the Armed Forces, relevant authorities to enforce the law to confiscate land from those people and hand it over to the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. And fishing for consumption.
