More than 20 families in Khleng Por village, Prey Moul commune, cut down trees on the mountain and sell them to traditional medicine teachers in Phnom Penh to earn money to support their families
(Kampong Chhnang): More than 20 families living in Khleng Por village, Prey Moul commune, Rolea Bier district, after farming in the dry season, they cut down trees on the mountain to sell to traditional medicine teachers in the city. Phnom Penh through brokers to earn money to support daily life.
Separately, every day, he and his two or three daughters cut only about 15 kilograms of dry medicine, two days can cut a bag of medicine equal to 25 to 30 kilograms. In 10 days, it can be sold for only 30 to 350,000 Riels to support the daily life of a family of 8 members, 2 parents and 6 children.
(Kampot): On the afternoon of March 10, 2022, Senior Minister Osman Hassan, Chairman of the Islamic Movement Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, inspected Kampong Kes High School in Kampong Kes Village, Trapeang Sangke Commune, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province.
The high school was also established in 2009 and started the study process from the 2011-2012 school year, and spent money on land acquisition, construction of buildings, infrastructure, and the cost of running a school meal for students (1 day). 3 times) which cost a total of nearly 2 million US dollars.
The high school, built on an area of nearly 2 hectares, has a total of 11 buildings, including: 2 3-storey school building, 1 3-storey administrative building, 2 4-storey student dormitory, 4 teachers' dormitory, cafeteria 1 student and 1 Surawa.
The school has a two-part curriculum, the General Education Program under the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and the Islamic Studies Program under the Annie Mash Center for Arabic, Mathematical, and Computer, sponsored by the Imam Safi'i Center in Matabesi.
In the school year 2021-2022, the school has a total of 44 staff, including 12 female staff, a total of 276 students, 124 female students from villages in Kampot, Kep, Koh Kong, Sihanoukville, Kampong Speu, Takeo, Kandal, Phnom Penh, Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum by receiving accommodation and meals at the school for free.
Students studying here can take the Malaysian Secondary, STAM SMU and other high school diplomas under the auspices of the Cambodian Islamic Council and can also apply for scholarships to study abroad.
To date, 27 students who have completed 12th grade here have received scholarships to continue their studies abroad, including Matabisi, Thailand, Indonesia, Turkey, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, the United Arab Emirates and Egypt.
At the same time, Senior Minister Osman Hassan reminded all children studying here to make efforts to acquire knowledge and skills to meet the needs of the private sector as well as the society needed to contribute to the development of the motherland.
This is according to the joint press release on the 11th meeting of the Joint Committee of Cambodia and the European Union held on March 10-11, 2022 in Phnom Penh at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia. Fresh News Received.
Luy David, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, chaired the meeting with Paola PAMPALONI, Deputy Country Director for Asia and the Pacific, EU Department of Foreign Affairs.
"The subcommittee meeting on trade and investment reviewed the Cambodia-EU bilateral trade and the investment climate in Cambodia," the statement said. "In 2020 and 2021, bilateral trade between the two sides will be worth 4.3 billion euros and 4.5 billion euros each year."
The meeting also discussed measures to revive the economy, bilateral trade and investment relations, as well as the temporary withdrawal of parts of the EU's trade tariff preferences under the EBA. Technical cooperation, market access issues, and ongoing efforts to further improve the business environment, including new investment laws and the diversification of the Cambodian economy.
