Wildlife Coalition in collaboration with the Ministry of Environment and Koh Kong Provincial Administration held a press conference on "Red Plus Cardamom Range Project for the Benefit of Sovann Baitong Community"
The press conference was chaired by Mr. Chuob Paris, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Red Plus Project Key Officer, Ms. Sou Vanna Gonlet, President of Wildlife Alliance and Mr. Sok Sothy, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, and other relevant partners on the afternoon of the 9th. March 2022 yesterday in Phnom Penh.
Speaking at the press conference, Mr. Chuob Paris said that the establishment of the Sovanna Baitong community by the Wildlife Alliance by taking into account the livelihood of the people is an effective measure to strengthen, protect and conserve natural resources while The ministry is also strengthening the role of people in other areas of protection and conservation of natural resources.
He added that the project has contributed significantly to the protection and conservation of natural resources by taking money from the development of agricultural crops in the community to help preserve the forest, a budget to help the community to help maintain. Forest.
According to Ms. Sou Vanna Gonlet, people who moved to live in the community of Sovan Baitong village, Kandol commune, Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province, under the Agricultural Development Project of the Wildlife Alliance received social land concessions. 25 meters and 600 meters long to make village land, plantations and land for various fruit crops to cut off their previous occupations that used to go into the forest to collect non-timber forest products, logging and hunting.
She emphasized: "This is the implementation of a project that promotes change in the lives of the people and for them to be stable because first: have land ownership, second: have a business, third: have Income and fourthly, safe for their livelihood.
"It is easier to live in the community because there are schools, hospitals and markets near the house where children can have the opportunity to finish high school and some even go on to university," she said. In Phnom Penh more.
Mr. At Nuch, President of Sovanna Baitong Community, said that Sovanna Baitai Community has shown its progress and growth over the years, starting in 2004. It was established with technical and financial support from Animal Alliance. Forest and assistance from the United States Agency for International Development (USAID), which has a population of just over 100 families.
He added that now more than 250 families are living and benefiting from the REDD +, Cardamom and Sovanna Green projects. Over the years, the community has been very successful, as in 2013, the community was established, many kinds of fruits and vegetables were planted, including: Durian, Sao Mao and so on.
At the beginning of 2017, Sovanna Baitong Handicraft Community was given responsibility for site management by the Wildlife Alliance for continuing to provide technical assistance.
