The Office of the Council of Ministers issued an official letter urging the resumption of the auction mechanism for importing live pigs to supply Cambodia as soon as possible to protect the interests of the people
(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Council of Ministers has issued an official letter to three ministers, including the Ministry of Economy, the Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Commerce, on the Royal Government's agreement to continue to organize a tender mechanism to import live pigs to supply Cambodia. Coming soon. This is according to the letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers, which was received by Fresh News on March 10.
The auction mechanism for importing live pigs is designed to protect the interests of both local farmers and consumers who eat pork daily.
The letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers states that "The Royal Government agrees to continue to hold inter-ministerial meetings with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Ministry of Commerce as soon as possible to review and discuss the continuation of the auction mechanism for importing live pigs for supply." Cambodia.
Regarding the issue of rising pork prices and setting up a bidding mechanism to import live pigs to supply local demand, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that Samdech has written to the Ministry of Economy and Finance to do this work as soon as possible to help farmers. It also helps consumers to control inflation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the Minister of Agriculture that Cambodia is a member of the World Trade Organization, a member of the ASEAN Free Trade Area, a member of the ASEAN Free Trade Agreement, China is a member of the ASEAN Economic Community, so Cambodia cannot take separate measures. The import and export goods.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in relation to the pork issue, it is not only possible to satisfy only a few farmers, but also to control inflation and market prices.
Please be informed that in order to protect both breeders and consumers who are daily pork eaters, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as the Economic and Financial Policy Committee, have initiated an auction mechanism to import live pigs for supply to Cambodia.
The Ministry of Economy states that the auction mechanism for importing live pigs supplied to Cambodia will be implemented only in case of shortage of pigs. In principle, the government always encourages local farmers to be able to supply enough pigs with reasonable prices without importation.
The establishment of this auction mechanism has been studied in detail by the Economic and Financial Policy Committee with independent experts in depth around the irregularities in the price of live pork and pork market prices in recent years. This. Mr. HUN Manet: The working group of the Cambodian People's Party always serves the people, unlike some corrupt political groups
