(Phnom Penh): Increasing taxes on high-risk products such as tobacco products is the best thing right now because it will give Cambodia a huge benefit, not just additional state tax revenue. It also reduces health costs and makes quitters healthier and more productive. This is according to a press release from the Southeast Asian Tobacco Control Coalition (SEATCA).
In addition to killing tens of thousands of people every year, tobacco has cost Cambodia about 2.7 trillion riels (US $ 663 million), or 3% of GDP. GDP). The current tobacco tax rate in Cambodia is only 25% - 30% of the retail price of cigarettes, which on average costs less than US $ 1 per pack, making it more affordable.
