(Phnom Penh): After spending a long time studying the challenges that lead to the loss of Tonle Sap fish from year to year, Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that if no action is taken Prevent crimes on the Tonle Sap Lake in time, at least two more years, the fish in the Tonle Sap Lake will be extinct.
The Tonle Sap Lake is known around the world as a lake rich in diverse resources, especially nicknamed the Cambodian Fish Tank. But in recent years the fish in the lake has been declining alarmingly. Regarding the decline of fish in the Tonle Sap Lake, officials did not seem to show any problems and solutions, they just said that the fish are not born to eat because people are born.
After a careful study under the spirit of fear that the Cambodian fish barn is disappearing, Dr. Sok Touch found that the reason for the decline in fish in the Tonle Sap Lake is not due to the increase in people eating like officials. No mention.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, there are a number of major reasons for the decline of Tonle Sap fish, such as the Tonle Sap water regime has changed due to the sharp decline in the Mekong River and less rainfall, making the Tonle Sap water. Smaller and shallower, deforestation, encroachment on protected areas, spraying of pesticides, poisoning of fish, and illegal use of fishing gear, nets, and the use of electric tools.
In the operation to investigate all these crimes, Dr. Sok Touch and his team had to sleep in the middle of the river and face corrupt officials who stopped the crime and illegal fishing groups. Mr. Sok Touch claimed that the operation to save the Tonle Sap Lake was a major challenge and threat to his life.
Mr. Sok Touch highlighted the solutions that need to be taken together to protect the resources in the Tonle Sap Lake, which is also a great natural resource of Cambodia. According to Dr. Sok Touch, to protect fish in the Tonle Sap Lake, there are four stages, including the removal of forest land, conservation area, which is a flooded forest area for spawning fish, stop farming, spraying rice because it poisons fish, stop Stop illegal fishing and stop deforestation.
