Stung Treng Provincial Governor Conducts a Meeting to Find a Solution to Confiscate the Ministry of Agriculture's Reserve Land from Invasion
(Stung Treng): In the afternoon of March 9, 2022, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng Province, chaired a meeting on finding a solution to confiscate the Ministry of Agriculture's reserve land from a small number of people who had encroached on it in Ban Bung village, commune. Ivory, Sesan District, Stung Treng Province.
The meeting was attended by representatives of the Ministry of Agriculture, Deputy Governors, provincial prosecutors, the three armed forces, Sesan district governors and other relevant departments.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang said that the reserve land of the Ministry of Agriculture is located in Ban Bung village, Phluk commune, which is now occupied by some villagers. Experimental agricultural crop varieties.
He said that the reserve land of the Ministry of Agriculture is 1914,2367 hectares. "In the past, the provincial authorities and the ministry have also cooperated to find a solution and prohibit the illegal occupation, but these anarchists continue to oppress the occupation by refusing to listen," he said.
Sovann Piseth, the governor of Sesan district, said that the people who came to occupy the land of the Ministry of Agriculture now have a total of 50 families, and these people are not local residents.
Mr. Sovann Piseth said that most of these people were migrants who had previously worked for the company's rubber plantations near the area and had illegally encroached on the Ministry of Agriculture's reserve land. Legal.
It should be noted that the results of the meeting to find a solution this afternoon, the Governor of Stung Treng decided to establish a working group in cooperation with the Ministry of Agriculture, including the armed forces and relevant authorities to implement the law to confiscate land from those people. Hand over to the Ministry of Agriculture for use.
