Japan provides over $ 1 million to Cambodia for community health and youth capacity building
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through its Embassy in Cambodia, has provided a grant of US $ 1,093,818 under the Japanese NGO Grant Project on Community Health and Sanitation and Capacity Building. Youth in Preah Vihear and Pailin provinces.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan and two representatives of the Recipient Unit at the Embassy of Japan on the afternoon of March 9, 2022.
In this project, KnK will continue to support young people, especially those who suffer from job insecurity, lack of life skills and drop out of school. For the third year of the project, two new community learning centers will be built, and four community learning centers, including two newly built community learning centers, will be equipped with study materials.
By providing better vocational training as well as close support to young people, they can acquire skills that help them lay a foundation for a better life in the future.
The Japanese NGO Grant Program has been in Cambodia since 2002 to support the activities of Japanese NGOs in their efforts to support the development and reconstruction of Cambodia at the grassroots level.
Since 2002, the Government of Japan has provided more than US $ 48 million for 145 projects focusing on primary education, health, agriculture and demining activities in Cambodia. General knowledge: How fast is the sound speed?
