"In terms of rice and tobacco, the Vietnamese side is just like us, which means that it produces tobacco rice for export like us," he said. Thus, he avoids too much competition between the private sector traders of both countries. "So every year, he has an agreement that sets 300,000 tons of rice and 3,000 tons of tobacco, which both sides have to source from each other."
He added that for exporters who want to get preferential treatment under this condition, it is necessary to apply for a Certificate of Origin S-Form from the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia.
Vietnam's Minister of Industry and Trade Nguyen Hong Dien has signed a circular setting out regulations on the import of rice and dried tobacco leaves from Cambodia for 2021 and 2022. This circular will be effective from April 15, 2022 onwards. This is according to the publication by the Vietnamese press on March 8, 2022.
For the export of dried tobacco leaves, exporters must present a license to import raw tobacco under the preferential tariff issued by the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam in accordance with the Decree dated May 15, 2018 and the circular of the Ministry of Industry and Trade. Vietnam.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat also said that in addition to rice and tobacco, there are also many goods from Cambodia that are exported at zero tariffs to Vietnam.
Mr. Oknha Hun Lak, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Rice Federation, confirmed that this agreement has been in place for a long time, usually every two years.
