(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 9, 2022, the police of the Internal Security Department of the Ministry of Interior, in cooperation with the Tax Department, sent four suspects to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action in connection with the fake case. Fraudulent embezzlement of millions of dollars through tax filing
This operation took place on March 7, 2022 at the company's office, located on Street 150, House 251C, Sangkat Toek Laak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, according to the order of the search order No. 2 KDCH. February 25, 2022 by Mr. Taing Sunlay, President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The operation was led by Brigadier General But Phin, Deputy Director of the Internal Security Department of the Ministry of Interior, with the coordination of Mr. Chhay Hong, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and Mr. Sok Heng, Deputy Director of the Tax Department of the General Department of Taxation. Both the authorities and the local authorities.
Sources revealed that the search of FatTag Business Solutions Co., Ltd. was carried out after the tax department investigated that the company owners conspired to falsify tax documents to embezzle the state's tax money. Millions of US dollars.
During the search, the police confiscated a number of exhibits, including computers, cameras, electronic devices, documents and stamps, and detained five staff members for questioning, including:
* First: Name: Hut Lyhong, Male, Chief Accounting Representative of the Company * Second: Name: Hul Sreyly, Female, 23 years old * Third: Name: Lem Rath, Female, 25 years old * Fourth: Name: Hong Chanvuthy, Male 47 years old * 5th: Name is Kot Sambath. They were sent to the Department of Homeland Security for questioning. As for the location of the company, the authorities have temporarily closed the Khlong Be afternoon.
