(Beijing): For nearly two hours, answered 27 questions from journalists related to all areas, such as the situation in Ukraine, relations between major countries and global governance. On March 27, Wang Yi, a member of the State Council and Minister of Foreign Affairs of China, gave an in-depth discussion on China's diplomatic initiatives at a press conference of the two National People's Congresss.
Currently, maintaining world peace is the most urgent task. Regarding the Ukraine issue, which the international community is most concerned about, China has outlined four initiatives in line with the full reality of the issue and called on the international community to focus on two major issues: Promoting peace talks and preventing the emergence of a large-scale humanitarian crisis.
At the same time, China has stressed that competition between major countries is not the theme of the era, and zero-sum competition is not the right choice. China is actively pushing for new international relations in order to provide more stability to a chaotic world.
It should be noted that the international community must unite, but must not be divided, must have dialogue, but must not be confronted, must not leave any country out of line and must not ignore any needs and suggestions. Responsible China will continue to adhere to true multilateralism, cooperate with all progressive forces in the world to jointly seek development and move forward!
