(Banteay Meanchey): On March 8, 2022, Brigadier General Sing Tum, Commander of the 51st Infantry Brigade, inspected the situation of people affected by strong winds in Samrong village, O'Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province.
On the evening of March 7, 2022, at 5:30 pm, mixed rain and strong winds affected and damaged people's houses in three districts in Banteay Meanchey province: O'Chrov, Thmor Puok and Phnom Srok districts. Damaged a total of 37 houses and 2 schools.
Joint forces, including the Intervention Force, the 51st Infantry Brigade, the Gendarmerie, the People's Defense Police and local authorities, jointly dismantled and rehabilitated the people.
Commander Sing Tum confirmed that the 51st Infantry Brigade, in addition to the core task of protecting the territorial integrity, was always ready to intervene with the means and equipment to rescue people affected by natural disasters 24 hours a day. 24 hours.
He added that Banteay Meanchey is a province that is often affected by strong winds and floods every year, so the army is always ready to rescue people affected. With the care of Dr. Hun Manet and she provided ten thousand zinc leaves stored at the 51st Infantry Brigade to help repair the houses of people affected by the strong winds.
Citizens and local authorities expressed their gratitude to Dr. HUN Manet and his wife for always caring for the well-being of the general public in times of hardship and disaster, and wished them good health and success in all their endeavors. To the motherland and the people forever and support Dr. Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister.
