Japanese Government Special Envoy: Samdech Techo's Visit to Myanmar Gives Greater Hope to Myanmar Citizens
(Phnom Penh): The Special Envoy of the Government of Japan, Mr. Yohei Sasakawa, expressed his strong support for the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and ASEAN Chair to Myanmar in early January 2022. Go here. The special envoy of the Japanese government sees Samdech Techo's visit as opening the door to problems and giving greater hope to the people of Myanmar.
Mr. You Hesasakawa said this during his courtesy call and discussion with Samdech Techo on Monday afternoon, March 7, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, told reporters that during the meeting, Yu Hesa Sakawa called Samdech Techo's visit to Myanmar a "heartfelt and practical action" to resolve the country's problems. Stuck.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth was quoted as saying, "100 meetings is not the same as one act: Samdech Techo's visit to Myanmar is locked and unlocked." "This is an action taken wholeheartedly, and it is an act of respect and giving greater hope to the people of Myanmar."
On January 7, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled to Myanmar, where he met with military leader Min Aung Lan and discussed a number of issues in line with ASEAN's five unanimous principles on resolving the crisis. Myanmar. The visit is seen as one of Cambodia's efforts to find a solution to Myanmar's problems, despite being seen as difficult and complex.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Mr. You Hesa Sakawa for seeing the value of his visit to Myanmar and considered the views of the Japanese special envoy to be the same as his views.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth quoted Samdech Techo as saying, "We have the same interest in Myanmar: stop the violence in Myanmar and bring gifts to the people who are most in need." "The more important direction is to bring democracy to Myanmar."
Samdech Techo also confirmed to Mr. You Hesa Sakawa that as the rotating chair of ASEAN, Samdech will make efforts to resolve the crisis in Myanmar.
Samdech Techo also requested Mr. You Hesasaka to continue working with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia and ASEAN Special Envoy on Myanmar issues.
In today's meeting, Mr. Youhe Sasaka also asked Samdech Techo to allow the Myanmar trainees to study the production of artificial limbs from Cambodia, which his organization has been training for a long time.
The Prime Minister welcomed and considered this an honor for Cambodia.
