The signing ceremony was held at the Embassy of Japan under the presidency of Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia between Mr. Huot Kea, Director of Kroch Chhmar OD Health Office on the afternoon of March 7, 2022. The ceremony was also witnessed by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the National Task Force for Local Assistance in Tbong Khmum Province.
Mikami Masahiro said that since 1991, the Japanese government has been implementing the Kusanoni program in Cambodia to directly assist local authorities and NGOs in implementing their projects.
"Kusanoni means" grass root "in Japanese, the ambassador said. In the last 30 years, the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia has contributed to more than 660 projects through the Kusanoni Grant. These projects have directly contributed to improving the quality of life of Cambodians at the grassroots level.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara thanked the Government of Japan through the KUSANONE Foundation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Japan for providing grants for 17 Kroch Chhmar District Referral Hospital project assistance projects focusing on surgical specialties. Urgent and serious illnesses such as traffic accident patients, pregnant women who need immediate caesarean section.
The hospital was built in 1966, the deputy prime minister said. At present, the hospital covers an area of 18,271 square meters. In order to meet the need to provide public health care services to the people, especially in order to facilitate access to medical examination and treatment services, Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration has proposed to upgrade the level of Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital from Level 1 (CPA1) to Level 2. (CPA2) to the Ministry of Health in 2021.
Through the development of the hospital to level 2 will provide surgical services to people in four districts, a total of about 469,308 people, including 239,467 women. Krouch Chhmar District Referral Hospital Level 2 will ease the burden for all motorbike riders who often spend about 40 km to travel to District 2 Referral Hospital, Chhlong District, Kratie Province and Level 3 Provincial Referral Hospital. Kampong Cham takes about 53 kilometers.
According to Dr. Huot Kea, Kroch Chhmar Referral Hospital is a central area with three administrative districts around it, with more than 400,000 people coming to receive services at this referral center as well.
