Letter to readers: Let's keep the peace together
(Phnom Penh): People all over the world, as well as Cambodians, have heard and known that the war between Russia and Ukraine took place, leaving many wounded and dead with artillery and attacks. By infantry missiles and tanks as well.
In addition to the loss of life, the war also caused severe economic damage, especially severe damage to some infrastructure, large buildings were burnt by gunfire, people on both sides were evacuated to safer places. Extremely frightening and dangerous.
If we look back at Cambodia by the end of the 1960s, the people suffered innumerable times due to the crisis of the flames of war, both civil war and with neighboring countries.
The tragedy of the war brought the people into the misery of the Democratic Kampuchea regime of Pol Pot, Ieng Sary, Khieu Samphan, Nuon Chea from 17 April 1975, who were brutal murderers. What is the national identity, what is the achievement that our ancestors have worked hard to build for more than 2,000 years.
Cambodians who have been through the flames of war and those who have not yet tasted the pain of war are always afraid of war again on Cambodian soil, despite some unscrupulous groups. Will be using the plan as well as evil tricks to drag the country into chaos, instability and into the flames of war because of ambition to seize power.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), stated that Samdech has shared his grief and hardship with each other so far. Should we abandon this achievement? The harmony of Cambodia today is born of Cambodia itself and the sacrifice of fresh flesh and blood of Cambodian veterans.
The Cambodian people throughout the country recognize the work of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in ending the civil war and building a full and lasting peace in Cambodia and in the process of building peace in Cambodia.
Peace is more precious than anything, peace is the most beautiful thing, peace gives hope and a smile to everyone. Those who have never experienced the hardships and pain caused by war may not value peace. Those who have been through violent conflict or the flames of war only know how precious peace is.
Samdech's personal experience of growing up and progressing through decades of civil war in Cambodia. Samdech was forced to drop out of school in 1970, when Cambodia was falling apart and war erupted. Samdech's childhood and adolescence, which should have been happy if the country was peaceful, but Samdech suffered only hardships and pain.
Later, in 1996, Samdech risked his life again to negotiate directly and persuade Khmer Rouge forces at their military bases to lay down their arms and rejoin the government under a win-win policy. Life, property rights, status and occupation.
This win-win policy pushed for a complete peace in Cambodia in 1998. This win-win policy also allowed the Royal Government to focus its full attention on national development while the Cambodian people accepted. Benefit and opportunities from peace and development. Cambodia has maintained peace for more than 20 years.
At the same time, Samdech Techo is determined to continue to protect and promote peace through the experience of Cambodia through the war and peace building. "No peace, no hope, no peace, no development, no peace, no respect "Human rights and no democracy." "Peace is a reality, not a vague dream."
Moreover, although Cambodia is small, Cambodia has contributed to the process of finding peace in the region and the world with goodwill, responsibility and honesty. Thank you for the peace "and remembered this word in everyone's heart.
Peace in our region and the world remains fragile and tense due to combined issues such as rivalries between superpowers, the rise of nationalism, terrorism, poverty and food insecurity caused by Climate change and the Kovid 19 pandemic.
These problems can destroy the progress of the people and the nation as a whole if we do not work together to solve and protect. Promoting peace is necessary for us today, but more importantly, we must work together to "make the world a better place for the next generation" and to keep the peace with the head of government. Techo Hun Sen to remain stable for a long time.
