Hok Leakena, a 12th grade student at Tamang High School, described learning some of the Khmer Rouge regime through her schooling. After attending this class forum, Leakena gained a lot of knowledge about the history of Democratic Kampuchea and the cessation of racism. "Preventing violence and genocide is very important to maintain peace in society and the country," Leakena said.
