International Analysis: Details of Chinese Government Work Report Encourage and Warm People
China's government employment report outlines key development targets for 2022, with GDP growth estimated at about 5.5 percent. Zhang Liqun, a researcher in the Department of Macroeconomic Studies at the Development Research Center of the State Council, noted that the 5.5 percent target was both positive and stable.
The Chinese government jobs report estimates that throughout the year, tax rebates and tax cuts will be reduced to about 2.5 trillion yuan. In the context of pressure in three areas: declining demand, affected supply and weak estimates, the Chinese government has increased the level of tax cuts and reduced government fees, as well as provided microfinance support. Enterprises and small enterprises.
At the same time, the tax to be repaid to the enterprise will be repaid directly to the enterprise in the sense of ensuring that the tax refund and reduction measures can be implemented to help the enterprise in difficult times and help the enterprise. There is revival.
Another important part of the Chinese government's work report is to ensure and improve people's lives. Netizens complained about the welfare provided by the government employment report to the people not only 30 Chinese yuan, but also the basic pension increase for retirees and the inclusion of critically ill or disabled people. Severe disability of the family near the minimum line of insurance in the minimum insurance, etc.
It can be seen that the stabilization of the social security system will be conducive to boosting economic development and will also provide new opportunities for China's economic development.
