The United Nations (UN) on Wednesday, March 2, 2022, convened an emergency conference to call on Russia to end its war of aggression against Ukraine. At the General Assembly, 141 of the 193 members voted in favor of ending the war of aggression in Ukraine. Five countries did not support it: Russia, Eritrea, North Korea, Syria, Belarus voted against.
Thirty-five countries abstained (in the middle) and 12 other countries were absent. Following the election, the United Nations issued a resolution calling on Russia to withdraw all its military forces from Ukraine immediately and unconditionally.
