(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Tbong Khmum, the first modern hospital on rural land, was completed and officially inaugurated on Monday, March 7, 2022.
In order to solve the problem that is a major concern in the lives of the people in this rural area, the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has considered and reached the decision to build a hospital with a high level of treatment in Tbong Khmum province. .
Under the strong friendship and financial support from the Chinese government and people, the construction of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Tbong Khmum province began in 2019. Cambodia's Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen (R) shakes hands with Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vinthean (R) at Tbong Khmum province on March 1, 2019. Finally.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said during the opening ceremony that the Tbong Khmum-Cambodia Friendship Hospital is equipped with modern medical facilities, not only to serve the people of Tbong Khmum. But also contributed to serve the people in the neighboring provinces such as Kampong Cham, Prey Veng, Kratie, Stung Treng, Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "This hospital is not only required by our bees. It will be part of a medical examination on the east bank of the Mekong River, partly from Prey Veng province, which borders Kampong Cham province. From here, not far to Chhlong, not far, we reach Kratie, it reaches Stung Treng, it reaches Ratanakiri, Mondulkiri, who can come to this location for medical examination.
Samdech Techo added, "China's equipment is becoming more sophisticated with other facilities that have become an important basis for health care and solving people's health problems." "With better infrastructure, people have better access to welfare services."
After the official opening of the construction site, the construction process was carried out with the utmost care and effort by the technical team and builders from both Cambodia and China. The process of building and equipping modern hospitals for the great hope of the rural people has been completed.
Tbong Khmum Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital was built on an area of 24,300 square meters on a total area of 55,815 square meters. The hospital has spent nearly $ 50 million in grants from the Chinese government and people. The hospital has nine interconnected buildings. It is divided into 5-storey hospital building, 5-storey maternity and pediatric ward, 2-storey medical building, administrative and residential building and 1 other building.
Dr. Keo Vannak, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department, emphasized that "the capacity of this building is a modern building and we have modern equipment at the international level that we equip in this hospital building."
"All facilities are equipped with the latest technology in our world," he said. "All systems in the hospital are controlled by state-of-the-art digital technology."
Ek Kheang, director of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Tbong Khmum, said the hospital could consult 600 people a day.
However, the hospital still faces a shortage of doctors who specialize in some serious illnesses and the use of state-of-the-art equipment. Currently, the hospital has been focusing on training doctors and also plans to request additional doctors from the Royal Government to be placed at the hospital.
With the presence of this hospital equipped with modern medical services, the hospital has also organized a service with high responsibility with reasonable prices for the lives of people in rural areas.
"The hospital management, as well as all the hospital staff, have organized a number of missions and visions to run the hospital. "Our mission is to provide quality health services, digital health, to care for the people with care, without discrimination, and to respect professional ethics." This is Mr. Ek Kheang's confirmation.
A hospital equipped with modern equipment and high technology for the first treatment on rural land in Tbong Khmum province will become an important place to save and save lives. This hospital will not only save patients faster than traveling to Phnom Penh, but will also contribute to reducing the cost of treatment and care compared to hospitalization in Phnom Penh.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, emphasized, "This Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Tbong Khmum can help our people to reduce the cost of traveling abroad as well as reduce the cost of travel to other places. Far away. This is a regional hospital, so people from other provinces next to Tbong Khmum can come and receive treatment and stay here.
Mr. Tim Thi, a resident of Tbong Khmum Province, also saw the values and important contribution of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Tbong Khmum in supporting and improving the well-being of people in the provinces far from Phnom Penh.
Tbong Khmum Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital is a sacred achievement that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, has given to the people of Tbong Khmum province in particular and in general for the Cambodian people throughout the country. The leaders and people of Tbong Khmum Province expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for always thinking of improving the well-being of the people by increasing the capacity and efficiency of medical services.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan thanked Samdech Techo, "On behalf of the provincial administration, on behalf of all the people in Tbong Khmum, I would like to express my sincere gratitude to the Prime Minister." He is always concerned about the public health of our people. In particular, in our province of Tbong Khmum also received love from Samdech Techo to the people like that and make us get this great achievement.
The comprehensive strategic partnership and full of deep emotion between Cambodia and China has led to many achievements on Cambodian territory for the benefit of the nation and its people. The modern hospital in Tbong Khmum province is also a valuable achievement born of the long-standing friendship between Cambodia and China.
Provincial leaders, authorities and people in Tbong Khmum praised the Cambodian-Chinese friendship and thanked the Chinese government and people for providing assistance to build this hospital to help improve the well-being of Cambodians and rescue. Life from disease and other plagues that threaten life.
Dr. Keo Vannak, Director of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department, said, "I would like to thank the Chinese government and people for their generous assistance to Tbong Khmum." "This is an opportunity for the benefit of humanity in the territory of Tbong Khmum province, which is important as a targeted aid to help the well-being of the people."
It should be noted that along with the inauguration of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Tbong Khmum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also inaugurated the school building, management building and dormitory building in Techo Sen Tbong Khmum Primary School and High School.
According to the report, the school building, office building and dormitory building in Techo Sen Tbong Khmum Primary and High School were built in 2018 by the Hun Sen Engineering Corps in Siem Reap and will be completed in 2020.
The buildings constructed include: 2 office buildings equal to 10 classrooms, 2 school buildings equal to 36 classrooms, 3 floors high. 2 apartment buildings equal to 40 rooms. There is also a volleyball court and two basketball courts in the school yard.
The building and infrastructure in the school cost about 1.3 million US dollars to build as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
