(Oddar Meanchey): A total of nearly 100 houses in Oddar Meanchey and Banteay Meanchey provinces were damaged by heavy rain mixed with strong winds. This is according to the local authorities who confirmed the incident on March 6, 2022.
In Oddar Meanchey province, there are 77 houses of affected people with open roofs and 2 collapsed houses in Koun Kriel commune, Samrong city, including Romduol Cheung Phnom village, Bos village, Kirivan village, Samrong Sen Chey 1 village, Trapeang Tao Chas village, Tumnup Chas Knong village. Trapeang Tao commune, Anlong Veng district.
In Banteay Meanchey province, this natural disaster caused damage to the houses of 13 families in Sambour village, Pong Ro village, Poi Char commune, Phnom Srok district, with the roof and pillars falling to the ground.
After suffering from strong winds, local officials and law enforcement forces came down to intervene and help prepare and repair damaged houses in the future.
