Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Inspects the Progress of Construction of a Statue of Indra on an Elephant
(Kampong Cham): On the afternoon of March 6, 2022, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, and his colleagues inspected the progress of the construction of the statue of "Indra Kong Leu Domrei Evaran" at the riverside park in Kampong Cham City. About the sandstone weighs more than 30 tons, not including the weight of the throne.
According to the administration of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall, up to now, the above historical statue has completed more than 70% of the construction, which the provincial administration plans to keep in the Mekong River Park in Kampong Cham in the near future to Promote the beauty of this tourist area as well.
Please be informed that the history of the statue of Indra sitting on an elephant, this iren is studied on the basis of the ancient Khmer style and synthesized three styles combined: Baphuon style, Angkor style and Bayon style.
As for the statue of Indra, it has been defined as "Peace, Victory", representing gratitude for the current peace under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
