China sets 2022 economic growth target for 30-year low
BEIJING (Reuters) - The Chinese government has set its growth target for the slowest pace in more than 30 years as signs of a slump in the real estate sector, austerity measures and global risks will continue to weigh on consumption. According to Bloomberg News.
China's economy began to slow in the second half of last year due to a slump in the real estate sector, an outbreak of Kovid-19 and declining consumer spending. The economic outlook has eased this year with rising geopolitical tensions as Russia's invasion of Ukraine has hurt financial markets and boosted trade. According to Bloomberg News.
Putin warns that the third person to create a "no-fly zone" in Ukraine is tantamount to joining the war
(Kiev) - Russian President Vladimir Putin on Saturday warned that Moscow would consider any third party declaring a no-fly zone in Ukraine to be involved in the same armed conflict. This was released by the AP on Saturday, March 5, 2022.
"In just a few seconds, we will consider that they are involved in today's military conflict, no matter what organization they belong to," Putin said at a meeting with a group of female pilots. According to Putin, the establishment of a no-fly zone is a threat to the Russian military.
According to many experts, Ukraine is not a partner of Russia, the world's second largest military power. But if the war continues, how will Putin decide? Naturally, no country can benefit from a protracted war. So how could the Russian-Ukrainian war end?
* Short-term war
In these two scenarios, with the support and assistance of the United States and its Western allies, the Ukrainian army will be able to fight back, preventing the Russian army from completely controlling Kiev and its territory. That is, the Ukrainian army, including its people, may take part in a guerrilla war or a rebel war against Russia.
* European War
Article 5, the core body of NATO on "collective security", states that an attack on a Member State is an attack on NATO as a whole, which requires all Member States to respond. Do not forget that last week, Putin ordered the Russian nuclear forces to be on high alert at all times.
* Diplomatic solution
Negotiations between representatives from Russia and Ukraine have already taken place twice in Belarus, and a third round of talks between the two sides is expected soon. The second round of talks did not yield any significant results in terms of fighting, but at least it seemed to be more advanced than the first round, with Russia and Ukraine agreeing to establish a humanitarian corridor for the people. Civil.
