(Phnom Penh): The Code of Conduct for the Banking and Finance Sector was officially launched by the Banking Association, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and the Federation of Finance and Technology of Cambodia this morning, March 4, 2022. Prevent excessive debt or reduce indebtedness of Cambodians and protect vulnerable customers.
He added that in this code, it is clearly stated that debt collection is highly ethical, there is no coercion to threaten customers, if customers have debts or loans can not be repaid, bank staff must study. In-depth study of the problems that customers have encountered. If the credit officer makes a mistake, he / she will follow the administrative measures according to the mistake, if the mistake is serious, it can lead to immediate termination.
He hopes that after the implementation of the Code of Conduct for the Banking and Finance Sector, growth in the banking sector in 2022 will be higher than in 2021.
Dr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that in 2021, 77.6% of customers borrowed from one institution, 18% of customers borrowed from 2 institutions, 3.7% borrowed from 3 institutions and customers Borrowing up to 4 institutions is 0.4%.
He added: "We know all the information, we prevent the need for excessive debt, there is enough system, but partly depends on the customer himself, who has to provide clear information when he wants more credit, he provides inaccurate information. "He does not have accurate financial statements, we find it difficult to keep track."
Bride and Groom Guests Arrested in Kampong Ror District, Svay Rieng Province, Authorities Detained Two Suspects
(Svay Rieng): There was a surprise at the wedding because a group of gangsters, the guests of the bride and groom argued until they started a fight, causing one person to be injured, but was arrested by the police of Svay Tayan commune administrative post Two suspects for questioning.
The shocking incident happened at 8:40 pm on March 3, 2022 in Po village, Svay Ta Yean commune, Kampong Rou district, Svay Rieng province.
According to witnesses, before the incident, many guests were invited to the wedding, each with a happy face, both the bride and groom. At the time of the incident, two groups of children got drunk and had a verbal argument, which led to a surprise fight, causing guests to run wild throughout the wedding.
