(Phnom Penh): The Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal of Phnom Penh on March 4, 2022 held a meeting to review the work of 2021 and work direction for implementation in 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Seng Sivutha, President of the Court of Appeal. And Mr. Ouk Savuth, Prosecutor General of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal in accordance with Article 54 of the Law on the Organization of the Judiciary.
The meeting to review the work results of 2021 and the direction of work for the implementation of 2022, which was held at the meeting hall of the Court of Appeal in Phnom Penh, was also attended by the Vice President of the Court of Appeal, Deputy Prosecutor General, Judge, Prosecutor, Secretary General, Deputy Secretary General of the Department. Deputy Director of the Clerk Department and also Chief of Office.
At the meeting to summarize the work results in 2021 and the work direction for implementation in 2022, Mr. Seng Sivutha and Mr. Ouk Savuth said, "Although we meet the community event on February 20 of Kovid-19 The Court of Appeal and the Attorney General accompanying the Court of Appeal a year ago achieved good results. "I appreciate and appreciate the achievements throughout the year."
Based on the results of the work achieved and the findings of the challenges and challenges that were raised in the meeting of the Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal, set the direction of the implementation of the following 9 points as follows:
1: Continue to apply the principles of speeding up the priority criminal cases, including: Crimes, money laundering, sex trafficking, drug trafficking, juvenile cases, cases involving female defendants, low-court cases and The trial court acquitted him with an appeal by the prosecution. All of these cases must be registered in the system, manually registered, sent out and put on trial as soon as possible in accordance with legal principles.
2: Continue to implement the principle of expeditious delivery of all kinds of decisions, such as decisions that are not yet final and final to the parties, especially to detainees.
3. Strengthen the cooperation between the Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal in Phnom Penh with all the institutions that are bound and competent in accordance with the policy, legal reform and the justice system through the mechanism of providing justice services quickly, equitably, transparently and fairly.
4: Continue to implement the improvement of the criminal verdict to be achieved in 2022 for the benefit of the Court of Appeal in Phnom Penh.
5: Strengthen the working mechanism between the work of judges, clerks and administrative work to be better in order to respond to the principle of speedy delivery of justice to the people.
6: Strengthen the program capacity of professional officers to register case data better.
7. Promote the implementation of the final verdict more than the previous year.
8. Strengthen the capacity and budget planning, implement the budget properly and clearly. Expenditures of the state budget must be transparent in accordance with the needs and procedures set by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
9: Continue to participate in inspecting the construction of the new Phnom Penh Court of Appeal.
At the same time, in order to achieve the nine work objectives for implementation in 2022, Mr. Seng Sivutha, President of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal, provided nine additional points to be implemented more effectively, including:
1: To increase the capacity of awareness to ensure the effective implementation of work in accordance with the state of development of the country within the ASEAN framework.
3. Must continue to strictly implement the fight against all forms of crime in order to participate in protecting social security and promoting the justice sector.
4. Continue to carry out a thorough and fair trial to increase the people's trust in the judiciary through a fast and accurate trial mechanism based on the principles of the law in force.
5. Continue to strictly implement all notifications and decisions of the parties, including lawyers representing the parties, as soon as possible, without discrimination, in order to improve the service of justice.
6. Efforts must be made to prepare all types of decisions in a reasonable, logical and decision-making manner as defined by law.
7. To continue to better cooperate with relevant institutions and civil society organizations to strengthen the justice sector and promote the rule of law in Cambodia.
8: To strengthen the internal unity better (all of our homes) without discrimination, without prejudice, family, non-violent, not to break the internal unity and not to be overly proud.
9. Adhere to the three health measures to protect ourselves, our families, our friends and our society to avoid the harassment of Kovid-19. Pakistan: At least 57 killed in attack on Shiite mosque
