Cambodia tells China why it decided to become a co-founder of the UN General Assembly emergency resolution on the situation in Ukraine
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, and Ms. Yang Yanyi, Special Representative of Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of China, on March 4, 2022, Cambodia informed the Chinese side of the reasons. It decided to join the co-founding members of the resolution of the emergency special meeting of the United Nations General Assembly (UN) on the situation in Ukraine.
A statement from the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Fresh News, stated: "Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon has informed the Chinese delegation of the reasons for the Royal Government of Cambodia's decision to join the "Resolutions of the emergency special meeting of the United Nations General Assembly on the situation in Ukraine."
The United Nations on March 2 convened an emergency assembly to vote on a resolution condemning and demanding that Russia withdraw its troops from Ukraine. Of the 181 countries, 141 voted in favor of the resolution, with five abstentions and 35 abstentions.
Cambodia is among the 141 countries that support this decision. China and Vietnam voted out of 35 countries.
On March 3, 2022, the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs issued a statement stating that "at that meeting, Cambodia expressed its deep concern over the seriousness of the escalating situation and the deteriorating humanitarian conditions that "Due to the ongoing military tensions in Ukraine."
Cambodia believes in dialogue and diplomacy to prevent the situation from falling out of control and to seek a peaceful solution in accordance with international law and the principles of the UN Charter.
"With an understanding of the security concerns involved, Cambodia maintains its firm position that all Member States must respect the sovereignty, territorial integrity and political independence of other Member States." This is according to the statement. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs presents the results of the meeting between the Cambodian diplomat and the special representative of the Chinese diplomat.
On the morning of March 4, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, met with Ms. Yang Yanyi, Special Representative of Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China. The meeting took place at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the two sides exchanged views and noted with satisfaction the growing ties between the two countries within the framework of cooperation. As a strategic partner in all aspects and building a common destiny community.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon congratulated China on its successful hosting of the 2022 Winter Olympics in Beijing and conveyed the Chinese leadership's gratitude to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. The King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, who attended the official opening ceremony of the sporting event on February 4, 2022.
Mr. Prak Sokhon expressed his gratitude to China for its continued support for Cambodia's socio-economic development and Cambodia's efforts to combat the Kovid-19 epidemic. The Deputy Prime Minister expressed hope to see the resumption of direct flights between the two for the benefit of cooperation in tourism and business.
Ms. Yang reaffirmed China's commitment to further strengthen and expand cooperation with Cambodia in all fields.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon briefed the Chinese delegation on the reasons why the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to join the co-founding member of the UN General Assembly emergency resolution on the situation in Ukraine.
She stressed that China will play a constructive role in finding a peaceful solution to the crisis in Myanmar.
Fisheries Administration cooperates with Mekong River Miracle Project to release endangered fish in Tonle Sap Lake
(Siem Reap): The Fisheries Administration of Cambodia cooperates with the Mekong River Miracle Project to release endangered fish in the Tonle Sap Lake by installing monitoring signs for further research.
Dr. Ngor Peng Bun, Dean of the Faculty of Fisheries Sciences of the Royal University of Agriculture, stated that the purpose of this event is to show endangered species and return them to their natural habitat and to monitor them. Their fate, too.
"We need to better understand the effectiveness of protected areas where shelters are threatened for endangered species, and that today's release will become a practice for future conservation," he said. "Help us to better understand whether such an approach is effective in helping to restore the amount of fish in nature."
The release of the endangered species into the Tonle Sap Lake is expected to be the first of its kind in the future, Dr. Hogan said. Researchers are optimistic that a sustainable commitment to protecting the world's endangered giant freshwater fish species will bear fruit.
A total of more than 1,000 fish have been released into a government-controlled conservation area, formerly the fourth fishing lot in the Tonle Sap Lake, not far from Siem Reap and the famous Angkor Wat temple by boat. . Most of these fish are juveniles, ranging in size from 30 cm (1 ft) to 1.6 m (over 5 ft), developed by the Cambodian Fisheries Administration in collaboration with the Mekong River Wonder Project, funded by USAID.
Please also note that this project is a collaboration between the Fisheries Administration of Cambodia, Siem Reap Provincial Fisheries Administration and the Mekong River Wonder Project, funded by USAID, with additional contributions from recreational fishermen through special partnerships with fishing resorts. Gilham in Thailand. Techo International Airport Construction Company Sells $ 15 Million in Bonds to Hattha Bank
