Ministry of Education to Celebrate 7th National Reading Day on March 11
The 7th National Reading Day is organized in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 120 dated September 14, 2015 of the Royal Government of Cambodia on National Reading Day.
The Ministry of Education states that the purpose of celebrating National Reading Day includes:
1: Cultivate reading habits, promote reading culture, enhance the ability to read dry poetry and composition to contribute to the protection and strengthening of Khmer culture and civilization to students, civil servants, all people in Cambodia, as well as promote the preservation of human heritage values.
2: Achieve the goal of sustainable development that ensures the quality of education with an equitable environment and promotes lifelong learning for all.
The Ministry of Education said that activities to celebrate National Reading Day include:
1: Poetry and Composer Reading Competition "Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award" 2: Research Lecture on "Language Development and Theory of Child Development" 3: Discussion on the topic of reading to help improve the quality of education " * How to lead reading activities in the primary library * Reading to improve the quality of education in Cambodia * Reading to improve the professional standards of teachers.
