The following is the announcement of the National Assembly: The Royal Government Disseminates the Results of the Study on "Mine Action and Sustainable Development in Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, this morning, March 3, 2022, presided over the dissemination ceremony of the study results on " "Mine action and sustainable development in Cambodia."
The event was co-sponsored by the Cambodian Mine Action Authority (IAEA) and the Geneva International Center for Humanitarian Mine Action (GICHD) with financial support from the Irish Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his deep gratitude to GICHD, the Irish Ministry of Foreign Affairs, UNDP, Mine Action Operators and the Mine Action Authority for their contribution to the study.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the development partners and donors in the past and present, such as Australia, Belgium, Canada, China, Denmark, the European Union, France, Germany, Hungary, Ireland, Japan, the Republic of Korea, the Netherlands, New Zealand, Sweden and Switzerland. British, American, UNDP, UNICEF and GICHD demining operators and demining personnel involved in demining.
It is also noteworthy that this study highlights the overall impact of the mine action sector on sustainable development in Cambodia. The results of the study in Cambodia provide clear evidence of the impact of mine action on sustainable development at various levels through the reduction of risks posed by local communities affected by the presence of munitions. Explosives.
