Minister of Culture calls on young people to avoid forgetfulness, leading to the destruction of national culture
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, called on Cambodian youth to actively contribute to the preservation and promotion of national cultural and artistic values, to avoid ignorance and self-destruction.
The Minister made this call on the 24th National Cultural Day, March 3, 2022, under the theme "Youth for National Culture" at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall, chaired by the Honorable Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection.
"For the social aspect, Cambodian youth need to be encouraged and cultivate patriotism and love of culture by actively contributing to the preservation and promotion of national cultural and artistic values, avoiding ignorance and forgetfulness," she said. To the destruction of national culture itself.
From an economic point of view, she called on Cambodian youth to be more actively involved in supporting activities and initiatives based on the protection of national identity and entrepreneurial spirit to strengthen and expand the cultural economy of To make the nation more prosperous in the spirit of caring, maintaining the balance of the development of arts and culture with the development of science and technology.
National Cultural Day was established in 1999 and is celebrated every year under different themes according to the context and priorities of Cambodia's cultural and fine arts. According to Dr. Pheung Sakona, the theme "Youth for National Culture" for the celebration of National Cultural Day so far is not a coincidence.
Dr. Men Sam An: Young people are the successors of bamboo and the successors responsible for preserving the national cultural heritage to survive forever.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, requested all citizens, especially young people, to have a patriotic conscience and a spirit of love for national arts and culture to be kept in mind and action. Its bamboo shoots and successors are responsible for preserving these national cultural treasures forever.
Dr. Men Sam An made this request on the occasion that she presided over the High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the celebration of the 24th National Cultural Day 2022 under the theme "Youth for National Culture ”this morning, March 3, 2022 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
On that occasion, Ms. Dr. Men Sam An made some recommendations, including:
First, regarding the resources for special work, the state budget, Samdech Techo Prime Minister advised all ministries and institutions to use resources with high savings, including strengthening the implementation of expenditures only on necessary work.
Second, the preservation and development of national culture can be sustainable with the participation of all people, especially local people with cultural heritage.
In this regard, she also asked the authorities as well as all local people to participate in preventing and cracking down on all the crimes of destroying ancient buildings and archeological sites that are happening almost every day across the country. The successful and sustainable preservation of historical and cultural evidence requires the support and assistance of all circles, especially local authorities and people living in heritage sites.
