(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia organized the 58th Meeting of the Monetary Policy Committee with the participation of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and Chairman of the Monetary Policy Committee.
The meeting discussed the current state of the world economy, progress and challenges of macroeconomic and financial stability in Cambodia, as well as monetary policy to be implemented in the future.
The reopening of the country has had a positive impact on domestic economic activity, including domestic transport, trade and tourism, as the global economy continues to grow. The inflation rate remains low, controllable at 3%, with a stable exchange rate of 4,108 riel per US dollar.
International reserves continue to be high enough, equivalent to eight months' worth of imports of goods and services, for the time being to serve monetary policy as well as exchange rate policy.
The National Bank of Cambodia continues to pursue a policy of innovation and support for economic activity while maintaining strong stability in the banking sector.
The meeting appreciated the results of the implementation of monetary policy and provided guidance for the implementation of monetary policy for the next time. The emergence of a new omega virus in the community may have an impact on growth momentum, but this effect is expected to diminish due to the government's control over the epidemic and supportive measures.
In order to contribute to price stability and improve the effectiveness of monetary policy for the next time, the Monetary Policy Committee has decided on the following monetary policy positions:
1. Continue to maintain a stable exchange rate of the riel against the US dollar by using various tools, including intervention and liquidity in riel.
3. Provide liquidity through the LPCO mechanism in an amount that supports the demand for riel in banking and financial institutions.
4: Continue to maintain the reserve requirement rate at 7% in both KHR and USD.
5: Continue to raise awareness and use of the riel.
