UN: Nearly 1 million people have fled Ukraine since Russia launched an attack
The United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) says more than 874,000 refugees have fled the conflict in Ukraine and sought safety in other countries. Russian attack. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, March 3, 2022.
According to the UNHCR, millions more are estimated to have been displaced in the country. Most of the refugees are currently staying in one of the five neighboring countries of Ukraine: Poland, Hungary, Romania, Moldova and Slovakia. About 70,000 people have arrived in European countries that do not have borders with Ukraine, such as Germany, Italy or Greece.
As the number of refugees from Ukraine reaches one million, more and more European countries are being asked to accept refugees. But among those countries are Hungary and Greece, which are known for their strict stance on accepting migrants. Samdech Techo Hun Sen
