(Paris): The French media watchdog announced the suspension of RT France immediately following the EU decision. This is according to the release by RT on Wednesday, March 2, 2022. The Ministry of Environment launches zero trapping campaign in the protected area of Cambodia on March 3.
(Phnom Penh): "Zero Trap Campaign in the Cambodian Protected Areas" Initiated and led by the Ministry of Environment with the participation of international organizations involved in the conservation of natural resources will officially start on March 3, 2022 and take place Six months in the eastern provinces of the Mekong River, including Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom.
Secretary of State Neth Pheaktra stated that the situation of protection and conservation of natural resources, which are the habitat of wildlife in Cambodia, is good, providing a habitat for wildlife and a source of water and food for wildlife, but what we need More consideration is given to making protected areas safer for wildlife and other biodiversity. Traps are a major threat to wildlife, he said.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the number of traps removed in 2021 was 61,611 traps, an increase of more than 20% compared to the number of traps removed in 2020, which was 43,270 traps. He said that the traps that have been removed are hidden killers who continue to kill wildlife in protected areas in Cambodia because of the type of traps, electric shocks, traps that break the legs and other dangers.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the Zero Trap Campaign will be part of helping to raise people's awareness and contribute to reducing the number of traps in protected areas.
Speaking at the press conference, Mr. Kim Nong, Director General of the General Department of Protected Areas of the Ministry of Environment, said that the campaign aims to make local people who are accustomed to trapping wildlife to obey the law and They understand the value of wildlife and come together to conserve wildlife, which is priceless.
He said that Cambodia has a law for disciplinary punishment and for trapping offenses is a third-level natural resource violation law, which includes both fines and penalties, which can face imprisonment from 1 to 5 years. And a fine from 15 million to 150 million riels.
He said that in this campaign, we will work together for six months, and during this time we will let local authorities and communities work together to prevent, as well as educate them to understand the law, the punishment and including the value of Wildlife.
Meanwhile, Mr. Seng Teak, President of WWF, said that currently only 20% of the traps have been removed in protected areas and 80% have not been released by the perpetrators in natural resource areas. In Cambodia.
According to the 2020 report, according to the 2020 report, there are about 12 million traps in Southeast Asia, such as Indonesia, Malaysia, Vietnam, Laos, Thailand and Cambodia, which are threatening wildlife. These traps are the source of the extinction of rare animals in the world, such as tigers, leopards, white tigers, wild dogs, bears and so on.
The president of the organization wants the relevant institutions to enforce the law on the perpetrators of rare wildlife killings, as well as restaurants or areas where wildlife is traded, which aims to protect Cambodian wildlife from extinction in the future.
In this regard, Mr. Chhin Sam Ath, Representative of USAID Prey Lang Baitong Project, said that if we do not have any specific measures on the traps that are being committed by the perpetrators every day, we will suffer. Wildlife will inevitably disappear. At the same time, enforcing the law and promoting it is also a must for local communities.
It should be noted that the opening ceremony of the Zero Trap Campaign on March 3, 2022 will take place online, with the participation of the inter-ministerial administration of the relevant provincial organizations in collaboration with the Ministry of Environment in the Zero Trap campaign.
Readers' point of view: In some circumstances it is not possible to use a large number of troops to overcome an enemy, and the commander must have a clear and comprehensive strategy.
