General knowledge: Russia and ancient wars
(World): Some emperors and warlords have always wanted to take control of Russian territory and have led the army to invade many times, but the king and his leaders have not been victorious over the Russian army. . In this article we want to show the events of the war between the Russians and the Gentiles.
* King Aki Dai Khan of the Mongol Empire
* Emperor Napoleon of the French Empire
In 1812, French Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte raised 600,000 troops from Vienna, Austria, to invade the Russian Empire, then ruled by Alexander the Great. In front of Napoleon's army, the Russian army retreated and refused to fight at all, which made Napoleon's army more and more advancing and advancing to the walled city of Moscow, the capital of Russia.
More than 300 years of battle with the Ottoman Empire
The war was recorded as one of the longest wars in world history, but since the 18th century the Ottoman Empire had lost its influence, causing a gradual loss of territory. Ottoman advantage continued until the end of the Ottoman era of Turkey. The Russian Empire conquered the Ottomans and conquered some of the southern territories in 1918 before the formation of the Soviet Union in late 1922.
* Adolf Hitler of Germany
Despite this victory over the German army, the Soviet Union itself lost many millions of troops and civilians. "About 14 million civilians have been killed, while Germany has lost more than 5 million troops."
Cold weather, large empires, strong population, geography, territory, good defenses and distance from other major empires were all factors that made ancient Russia able to defend itself from foreign aggression until it was able to repel the invading army. Those to withdraw from their territory.
In modern times, Russia has been able to continue to live with a prosperous world and become a communist ideological power, daring to compete with the United States, causing the world to be in turmoil for many years. . The Socialist Republic also lost its influence in 1991, but to this day, the federation remains a powerful nation on the international stage.
