In addition to the failure to fight Kovid 19, there are many other factors that contribute to the deteriorating human rights situation in the United States. According to the report, in 2021 alone, the United States had 693 large-scale shootings, an increase of 10.1 percent compared to 2020. The shootings left more than 44,000 people dead.
