National Road 3 is an important route for people to travel and transport goods between Phnom Penh to Kampot, Kep and Sihanoukville. Part of this stretch also serves for travel and freight in Kandal, Kampong Speu and Takeo provinces.
After the genocidal regime, National Road 3, as well as other sections, was in a very difficult situation to travel. Under the policy of prioritizing the construction of road and bridge infrastructure to contribute to national development, the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has continuously improved National Road No. 3.
This stretch of road passes through Phnom Penh, 12 km long, Kandal province 11 km long, Kampong Speu province 30 km long, Takeo province 30 km long and Kampot province 51 km long. This section of road has built 11 new bridges with a total length of 443 meters, a width of 12 meters and extended two old bridges with a total length of 30 meters.
This section of the road was constructed with 34 corner drains, 177 round drains, 271 canal drains on both sides of the road, and the installation of road equipment, including: traffic signs, traffic diagrams, kilometer poles and safety poles, as well as equipped with cameras. 10 fixed speeds and the construction of 2 pedestrian bridges.
For Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, National Road No. 3 is one of the many achievements that have been providing overwhelming benefits to people across the country, born of wise leadership, patriotism and patriotism. The wit and wisdom of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the founding father and a symbol of peace.
