Minister of Commerce wants to see the Czech Republic expand trade cooperation with Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, wants to see the Czech Republic expand trade cooperation to a greater extent than it is currently improving.
During the meeting, the Minister congratulated the newly appointed Ambassador to Cambodia and expressed optimism that Cambodia and the Czech Republic will continue to achieve more important achievements in the new Ambassador's diplomatic mission through Close cooperation.
Minister Pan Sosak also praised the traditional friendship and good relations between the two countries, the people of both sides, as well as the joint efforts in the past to strengthen and expand cooperation in various fields. In particular, the trade sector, focusing on rice, food processing and processing and packaging of Cambodian fruits.
The Ambassador thanked the Minister for his support for the mission of the Czech Embassy in Cambodia and expressed his appreciation for the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to diversify the Ministry of Commerce. Economy through legal, regulatory and institutional reforms that will further boost bilateral trade relations.
On that occasion, both sides highlighted the impact of the global epidemic situation, which is having a negative impact on the regional and global supply chain, leading to trade deficits between the two countries.
It should be noted that the Czech Republic is an important market in the European Union for Cambodian products. In 2019, the Cambodia-Czech trade volume reached about 126 million US dollars, with an increase of 36% compared to 2018. Affected by Kovid-19, trade between the two countries will shrink to around $ 80 million by 2020.
Authorities and residents enjoy the achievements of National Road 3, which has been expanded and improved.
(Phnom Penh): The section of National Road No. 3, more than 134 kilometers long, connecting from the Chaom Chao roundabout to Kampot provincial town will be officially put into use on March 2, 2022 tomorrow, after spending nearly 3 hours of construction. Years. The inauguration ceremony of this road will be presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
National Road 3 connects Phnom Penh to Kampot, passing through Kandal, Takeo and Kampong Speu. National Road No. 3 is seen as a road that provides many benefits for people to travel and transport goods.
Both the authorities and the people have warmly welcomed the expansion and improvement of the quality of this road. Mr. So Sina, a resident of Bati district, Takeo province, recalled that this section of National Road No. 3 after the liberation in 1979 was a dirt road for ox carts and was very small and difficult to travel. But the Royal Government has made continuous improvements to facilitate people's travel.
For Mr. So Sina, the improvement of National Road No. 3 by widening and pouring thick rubber has facilitated the travel of the people and provided more benefits by reducing the travel time, reducing the cost of gasoline and so on. The resident of Bati district saw that the improvement of National Road 3 will contribute to the betterment of people's lives.
This section of National Road No. 3 passes through Takeo province, about 30 kilometers long. Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, said that the improvement of National Road No. 3 will not only contribute to the better life of the people of Takeo Province, but will also contribute to attracting investors to set up factories in the province.
Representing the people of Takeo province, Mr. Ouch Phea expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, for his consideration and consideration for the people and for improving this section of National Road No. 3.
The section of National Road No. 3 was built under a concessional loan from the Chinese government and a contribution of the Royal Government of Cambodia of about 215 million US dollars. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the road was built in accordance with the promised techniques. If there is no overweight transport, the road can be used for more than 10 years.
On the occasion of the official opening of National Road No. 3, the Senior Minister called on people to take care of the road, especially in the market, do not throw garbage, pour water on the road, do not use the sidewalk as a shop.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on the afternoon of March 1, 2022, inspected the location of the inauguration ceremony of National Road No. 3, which will be held under the presidency of Samdech. Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on March 2 tomorrow.
This stretch of road passes through Phnom Penh, 12 km long, Kandal province 11 km long, Kampong Speu province 30 km long, Takeo province 30 km long and Kampot province 51 km long. This section of road has built 11 new bridges with a total length of 443 meters and a width of 12 meters and extended two old bridges with a total length of 30 meters.
With the inauguration of this important achievement for travel and transportation, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that this road was built properly according to the promised technique. If there is no overweight transport, the road can be used for more than 10 years.
The senior minister also called on the people not to drive more than the legal limit. The Minister of Public Works and Transport pointed out that one truck over 10 tons is equivalent to 10,000 vehicles traveling on the road. If one truck weighs more than 30 tons, it is equivalent to 810,000 vehicles traveling on the road.
The senior minister announced that strict measures will be taken for overweight vehicles with a legal limit of 20 percent or more, in addition to a fine of 300,000 riel per ton, and that the vehicle will be detained for one year. The minister claimed that the seized car would no longer be eligible for early release.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also called on all road users to obey traffic laws, not to reverse the road, drive at the speed limit, wear helmets and wear seat belts properly. He also reminded truck drivers to drive on slow lanes, not on highways.
