Cambodia is drafting a roadmap for the development of the automotive and electronics sectors, which is expected to increase exports by more than $ 2 billion and create more than 22,000 new jobs in five years.
The purpose of the current consultation with the private sector is to gather additional input and feedback in order to make the drafting process more comprehensive.
The draft roadmap outlines a long-term vision and direction for the development of the automotive and electronics sector in Cambodia, as well as an inter-ministerial action plan for implementation, an outcome-oriented initiative. Investor challenges in areas such as human resources and innovation, infrastructure, trade facilitation, and business and investment opportunities.
Addressing the meeting, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea highlighted the commitment of the Royal Government through the joint efforts of relevant ministries and institutions to ensure the comprehensiveness in defining the strategies, directions and mechanisms necessary to develop and attract Invest in the automotive and electronics sectors in Cambodia and increase price competitiveness in the operations of these sectors.
The Minister also added that the relevant ministries and institutions see the need to cooperate with the private sector to jointly develop these sectors, from the development of joint strategies to the launch and implementation of action plans and meetings today. This was organized in the spirit of consultation and partnership to gather additional input and feedback from the private sector on the draft roadmap.
The Minister also informed the meeting that after receiving comments and input from investors and stakeholders in the automotive and electronics sectors, the draft roadmap will be sent to the Economic and Finance Committee for review and recommendation. In addition, for the next step of preparing this draft before submitting to the Royal Government for review and approval.
It should be noted that in this draft roadmap, the relevant ministries and institutions will initiate the establishment of a council for the automotive and electronics sectors, representing the public and private sectors to provide guidance on the implementation of the roadmap.
The successful implementation of roadmaps in these two areas will have significant implications for Cambodia, such as increasing exports to more than $ 2 billion and creating more than 22,000 new jobs in five years. The coming years will also increase new opportunities for local SMEs in these areas.
Investors in the automotive and electronics sectors in Cambodia will also benefit from this arrangement, such as increased professional human resources, further improvements in electricity and logistics infrastructure to support the competitiveness of manufacturing and supply prices. More effective customs and trade facilitation for the import and export of products.
