General Dr. Neth Savoeun holds bilateral meeting with Australian Federal Police Commissioner
To begin with, Lt. Gen. Dr. Neth Savoeun welcomed the Australian Federal Police Commissioner, calling the visit a "special visit" to attend a bilateral meeting with the Cambodian National Police. As a partner of ASEAN Napoleon.
On that occasion, General Neth Savoeun also praised the results of the cooperation between the police of the two countries, especially the implementation of the MOU that both sides signed in the past.
In addition, the Australian side provided support and equipment as well as training, including strengthening the Transnational Crime Task Force, which has its own office at the National Police Headquarters and has become a force training center. Cambodian police are also involved in the fight against transnational crime.
On that occasion, the Australian Federal Police Commissioner thanked the Cambodian police for their cooperation in the fight against drugs and drug prevention to Australia, as well as the motorcycle gang. In this regard, he pledged to work shoulder to shoulder with the Cambodian National Police to successfully fight organized crime.
Gen. Dr. Neth Savoeun also agreed with the commitment of the Australian Federal Police Commissioner and made a number of requests for the Australian side to consider requesting support for the exchange of information related to political events as well as regional events. Related to Cambodia, in 2022-2023, Cambodia will have commune elections, National Assembly elections.
Separately, Cambodia will host the ASEAN Summit and another important forum, the SEA Games, which is the first event for Cambodia to host, especially to provide experience to the Cambodian police for defense. All of these events, through remote video conferencing, or can exchange delegations within the framework of this defense.
In addition, General Dr. Neth Savoeun also asked the Australian side to help strengthen human resources related to money laundering, economic crime, technology related crimes, which is considered a new problem for Cambodia.
During the meeting, General Neth Savoeun expressed his strong support for the Australian side's statement on the positive results of strengthening the traditional 20 years of cooperation and agreed to move forward together. Fight all kinds of crimes to ensure security in the country as well as in the region.
In addition, General Neth Savoeun also highlighted a number of legitimate challenges related to drug trends in Cambodia, including the management of chemicals for drug synthesis, which exchanged views and experiments with each other. Commit to jointly exchange information in order to strengthen cooperation and training to prevent crime, especially drug prevention remotely.
In response, the Australian side is pleased to co-operate at the request of the Cambodian side and pledges to assist the Cambodian side in both experimentation and other matters possible. Three Deputy Governors of Pursat Province will hold a handover ceremony on March 4, 2022
