Minister of Tourism: New Poipet International Gate Building is one of the first places to provide hospitality and warmth to tourists
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that the new passenger terminal at Poipet International Border Crossing is one of the first places to provide hospitality and warmth to tourists, which is another new achievement. Of the Royal Government and clearly stated the face and national pride of Cambodia.
This statement was made by the Minister of Tourism on the occasion of the inauguration ceremony of the new passenger terminal at the Poipet International Border Gate under the presidency of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior on March 1. 2022.
Minister Thong Khon said that this magnificent gate building was built on October 27, 2017 and completed on September 2, 2021.
The building embodies the Khmer style and is worthy of the image of the Kingdom of Cambodia, a country rich in rich cultural and traditional rich and functional structures in line with international standards.
The Minister added that the new building not only serves the interests of security, economy and society, but also supports the work of professional law enforcement officers with a good attitude, friendly, gentle and professional to turn the building. One of the first places to provide hospitality and warmth to tourists.
The Poipet International Border Crossing is one of Cambodia's most important international border crossings for economy and tourism, and was the main land route before Kovid-19, which welcomed about 28% of total and overland tourists. 8.7% of total international tourists come to Cambodia.
Minister Prum Sokha: In public service, to turn from an official to a servant of the people
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Royal School of Administration, on March 1, 2022, warned that in public service must be transformed from officials to servants of the people.
He said this during the recruitment program for the 11th generation of senior civil servants (Industry 4.0) and the 9th generation of Kramakar students (new normal generation) at the Royal School of Administration.
Mr. Prum Sokha does not want to see public servants working as public service providers to the people, but must act as servants of the people. In this regard, the Minister urged that future public servants must make in-depth reforms in their behavior while performing their duties.
The Minister of Public Works confirmed this: "In public administration, I ask only one! How to turn us from officials to servants of the people in public services.
The Minister of Public Works also reminded that if you want to be an official, you have to keep the value of being an official. Regarding the selection of job positions for the 11th generation of senior civil servants (Industrial version 4.0) and the 9th generation of Kramakar students (new normal generation), he also suggested that the future as a public official is to work in ministries / institutions Anything is valuable because the price is on the person.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, always recommends that "officials are the servants of the people."
For the place of function of the 11th generation of senior civil servants (Industry 4.0) and the 9th generation of Kramakas (new normal generation) of the Royal School of Administration, the ministries / institutions need a total of 298 11th generation civil servants More than 80 senior official students to be divided. This is according to Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works and Director of the Royal School of Administration.
