The following is the announcement: Minister Chea Vandeth: The Royal Government has launched a policy to transform Cambodia into a vibrant digital economy and society.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out the Digital Economy and Social Policy 2035 with the vision of transforming Cambodia into a vibrant economy and digital society.
The emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Chea Vandeth presiding over the workshop on the implementation of the project "Establishment of National Media and Digital Literacy Framework and Strategy" initiated by the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications under the technical assistance of UNESCO. Cambodia on February 28, 2022.
The purpose of this workshop is to disseminate to stakeholders the general concepts of media and digital literacy and to gather input from stakeholders in developing national media and digital literacy frameworks and strategies.
This project will produce two main draft documents:
1: A common national MIDL literacy framework that will define key competencies and skill levels using digital technologies in line with the Cambodian context and current technological developments.
2: MIDL Literacy Promotion Strategy, which will identify the various stakeholders and programs that we need to continue to implement together.
Both results will support the process of transforming Cambodia into a vibrant digital economy and society by 2035.
Speaking at the seminar, Minister Chea Vandeth stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out the 2035 Digital Economic and Social Policy, with the vision of transforming Cambodia into a vibrant economy and digital society through the establishment of a key foundation. To promote the adoption and digital transformation of all sectors of government, business and the people.
To achieve the above vision, this policy has a strategic priority as the key is to promote the transformation of Cambodians into digital citizens. The direction of this change is to make the most of the evolution of information and communication technology, promote productivity and economic efficiency, promote growth and build a civilized society.
In that, all digital citizens of Cambodia can benefit from the use of technology with high environment and trust, while maintaining the national identity and culture.
Recently, the Royal Government has launched the Cambodia Digital Government Policy 2022-2035, which aims to build a digital government to improve the quality of life through better public services.
This policy has four strategic goals and 10 strategies, one of which focuses on building digital human capital.
In addition, the Minister added that the project "Establishment of a National Media and Digital Literacy (MIDL) Literacy Framework and Strategy" is another important step towards the establishment of a comprehensive national framework. All angles can be used to accurately measure the ability and level of MIDL literacy of the people.
This framework will also become a necessary basis for ministries and institutions, including other stakeholders, to design clear and comprehensive training programs appropriate to the actual situation in Cambodia.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister requested you, officials at all levels and stakeholders to continue to support the activities of the National Framework and Strategy with the working group of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and UNESCO experts.
He said that his input was to show ownership of the work and the invaluable contribution to making the framework appropriate, quality and responsive to the real needs of our country.
