Royal Government Starts Construction and Expansion of National Road 4
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has started to build and expand National Road 4 in response to the current traffic growth.
In the announcement of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport received by Fresh News on February 28, 2022, said that the construction and expansion of National Road No. 4 from Bek Chan commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province to Bit Trang district. Prey Nob, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the Ministry, the construction and expansion of National Road No. 4 includes the expansion of the current rubber road from 7 meters to 10 meters wide, the expansion of 46 concrete bridges and drains, and the construction of eight new bridges to ensure traffic. Every season, some years are flooded.
The ministry said the construction process is scheduled for completion in December 2026. The project to build and expand National Road 4 uses a concessional loan from the World Bank.
With the implementation of the project to build and expand National Road 4, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport requests the understanding and tolerance of travelers and residents on both sides of the road who have been disturbed by the project process.
Please note that National Road 4 is about 230 kilometers long. This national road was built during the 1950s as a legacy of the relationship between Cambodia and the United States.
