The Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia hopes to have more companies after the Royal Government encourages tax for 3 years (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, encourages companies or enterprises to step up Enter the securities market to issue more equity securities and bonds to get more tax incentives from the Royal Government.
The move comes after the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued a new sub-decree to provide tax incentives to companies and investors in the sector for three years, from the date of issuance of the sub-decree to develop the securities sector in Cambodia. More progressive.
Mr. Sou Socheat stated, "If the company has the need for financing and can do in accordance with the content of this sub-decree, I think his company can use this tax incentive for him to enter the stock market and he will be able to "Strengthen his company, because we know that there are many benefits to entering the stock market."
He said that for companies that issue securities for sale in order to participate in green development or sustainable development, the company will receive more tax incentives as determined by the Minister of Economy and Finance. Those who invest or buy government securities issued this year also receive tax breaks.
The Royal Government's sub-decree states that the first publicly traded company or enterprise to be issued by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and listed on the Securities Exchange will receive a tax incentive. Withholding tax income and capital gain, etc. for 3 years.
For income incentives, companies or enterprises that issue equity securities in excess of 20% of the voting rights or issue securities in excess of 20% of total assets and loans for at least 7 years and receive Encourage by reducing income tax to 50% of income tax.
Companies or enterprises that issue equity securities in the amount of 20% or less of the voting rights, income tax incentives in proportion to not more than 20 billion riels and the issuance of bonds in the amount of 20% or less assets Receive tax incentives in proportion not to exceed 8 billion riels.
In addition, the first publicly traded company or enterprise to be listed on the stock exchange within three years from the date of entry into force of this sub-decree shall be entitled to tax liability preference. Total income, withholding tax, value added tax, special tax on certain goods and services, residence tax, public lighting tax.
Public investors will receive a 50% withholding tax deduction on interest and dividends arising from the holding or trading of state-owned securities, equity and debt securities, and will be exempt from capital gains tax on the purchase and purchase of capital. Trading of state securities, equity securities or bonds for three years.
The Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) recently predicted that by 2022, eight more companies would be listed, bringing the total number of companies listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange to 23.
