Cambodia mentions investment potential, attracts Turkish investors as Turkey is interested in investing in some sectors in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of a business visit to the Republic of Turkey, a delegation of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce led by Duke Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, and a representative of Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, met with the Turkish Chamber of Commerce and the Federation of Industrial Businessmen. Turkey too.
During the meeting, the Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce highlighted Cambodia's investment potential to Turkish investors to attract them to invest and find investment partners in Cambodia.
"Cambodia is geographically located in the center of the ASEAN region with a total population of more than 600 million," he said. "Turkish investors can set up factories in Cambodia and export to ASEAN and global markets."
Omer Zeydan, a board member of the Turkish Chamber of Commerce, said the Turkish Chamber of Commerce has 1.8 million member enterprises and 365 members of chambers of commerce and associations. The main role of the Turkish Federation of Chambers of Commerce (TOBB) is to participate in the formulation of economic policies and to deal with issues related to business and business promotion.
He stressed that the Turkish side is ready to cooperate with the Cambodian side in promoting investment business between the two countries in line with the Royal Government's goal to increase bilateral trade to more than $ 500 million a year.
Ferudun Cevahiroglu, President of the Turkish Federation of Industrial Businesses, expressed the interest of Turkish investors in Cambodia's economic potential and cooperation in key areas where the two countries can work together. He suggested that the two institutions study together on some priority projects, then the Turkish Federation of Industrial Businessmen will lead a business delegation to Cambodia to study the possibility of cooperation and implementation of the project.
Members of the Turkish Chamber of Commerce and Industry participated in discussions and studies on the business and investment environment in Cambodia on key areas, including: what sectors should be invested in Cambodia, Cambodia's strategic partners, exports, imports, traditional textiles, construction, energy, mining, agriculture. Original.
